#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:26
msgid "FILE FORMAT"
msgstr "FAILA FORMĀTS"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:34
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<replaceable>[section]</replaceable>\n"
"<replaceable>key</replaceable> = <replaceable>value</replaceable>\n"
"<replaceable>key2</replaceable> = <replaceable>value2,value3</replaceable>\n"
"            "
msgstr ""
"<replaceable>[section]</replaceable>\n"
"<replaceable>key</replaceable> = <replaceable>value</replaceable>\n"
"<replaceable>key2</replaceable> = <replaceable>value2,value3</replaceable>\n"
"            "

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:29
msgid ""
"The file has an ini-style syntax and consists of sections and parameters. A "
"section begins with the name of the section in square brackets and continues "
"until the next section begins. An example of section with single and multi-"
"valued parameters: <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Failam ir ini stila sintakse, un tas sastāv no sadaļām un parametriem. "
"Sadaļa sākas ar sadaļas nosaukumu kvadrātiekavās un turpinās līdz nākamās "
"sadaļas sākumam. Sadaļas piemērs ar vienas un vairāku vērtību parametriem: "
"<placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:41
msgid ""
"The data types used are string (no quotes needed), integer and boolean (with "
"values of <quote>TRUE/FALSE</quote>).  Boolean values are case-insensitive; "
"for example, <quote>TRUE</quote>, <quote>True</quote> and <quote>true</"
"quote> are all equivalent and valid; the same applies to <quote>FALSE</"
"quote>."
msgstr ""
"Izmantotie datu tipi ir virkne (pēdiņas nav vajadzīgas), vesels skaitlis un "
"Būla vērtība (ar vērtībām <quote>TRUE/FALSE</quote>).  Būla vērtības ir "
"reģistrnejutīgas; piemēram, <quote>TRUE</quote>, <quote>True</quote> un "
"<quote>true</quote> ir līdzvērtīgas un derīgas; tas pats attiecas uz <quote>"
"FALSE</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:49
msgid ""
"A comment line starts with a hash sign (<quote>#</quote>) or a semicolon "
"(<quote>;</quote>).  Inline comments are not supported."
msgstr ""
"Komentāra rinda sākas ar restītes zīmi (<quote>#</quote>) vai semikolu "
"(<quote>;</quote>).  Komentāri rindas vidū netiek atbalstīti."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:55
msgid ""
"All sections can have an optional <replaceable>description</replaceable> "
"parameter. Its function is only as a label for the section."
msgstr ""
"Visām sadaļām var būt neobligāts parametrs <replaceable>description</"
"replaceable>. Tas kalpo tikai kā sadaļas etiķete."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:61
msgid ""
"<filename>sssd.conf</filename> must be a regular file that is owned, "
"readable, and writeable only by 'root'."
msgstr ""
"<filename>sssd.conf</filename> jābūt parastam failam, kura īpašnieks ir „root"
"” un kuru var lasīt un rakstīt tikai „root”."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:65
msgid ""
"<filename>sssd.conf</filename> must be a regular file that is accessible "
"only by the user used to run SSSD service or root."
msgstr ""
"<filename>sssd.conf</filename> jābūt parastam failam, kas pieejams tikai "
"lietotājam, ar kuru darbojas SSSD pakalpojums, vai root."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:71
msgid "CONFIGURATION SNIPPETS FROM INCLUDE DIRECTORY"
msgstr "KONFIGURĀCIJAS FRAGMENTI NO IEKĻAUŠANAS DIREKTORIJAS"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:74
msgid ""
"The configuration file <filename>sssd.conf</filename> will include "
"configuration snippets using the include directory <filename>conf.d</"
"filename>."
msgstr ""
"Konfigurācijas fails <filename>sssd.conf</filename> iekļaus konfigurācijas "
"fragmentus no iekļaušanas direktorijas <filename>conf.d</filename>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:80
msgid ""
"Any file placed in <filename>conf.d</filename> that ends in "
"<quote><filename>.conf</filename></quote> and does not begin with a dot "
"(<quote>.</quote>) will be used together with <filename>sssd.conf</filename> "
"to configure SSSD."
msgstr ""
"Jebkurš <filename>conf.d</filename> ievietots fails, kura nosaukums beidzas "
"ar <quote><filename>.conf</filename></quote> un nesākas ar punktu (<quote>.</"
"quote>), tiks izmantots kopā ar <filename>sssd.conf</filename> SSSD "
"konfigurēšanai."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:88
msgid ""
"The configuration snippets from <filename>conf.d</filename> have higher "
"priority than <filename>sssd.conf</filename> and will override "
"<filename>sssd.conf</filename> when conflicts occur. If several snippets are "
"present in <filename>conf.d</filename>, then they are included in "
"alphabetical order (based on locale).  Files included later have higher "
"priority. Numerical prefixes (<filename>01_snippet.conf</filename>, "
"<filename>02_snippet.conf</filename> etc.) can help visualize the priority "
"(higher number means higher priority)."
msgstr ""
"Konfigurācijas fragmentiem no <filename>conf.d</filename> ir augstāka "
"prioritāte nekā <filename>sssd.conf</filename>, un konfliktu gadījumā tie "
"aizstāj <filename>sssd.conf</filename>. Ja <filename>conf.d</filename> ir "
"vairāki fragmenti, tie tiek iekļauti alfabētiskā secībā (atbilstoši lokālei)"
".  Vēlāk iekļautajiem failiem ir augstāka prioritāte. Skaitliski priedēkļi "
"(<filename>01_snippet.conf</filename>, <filename>02_snippet.conf</filename> "
"u. c.) var palīdzēt uzskatāmi parādīt prioritāti (lielāks skaitlis nozīmē "
"augstāku prioritāti)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:102
msgid ""
"The snippet files require the same owner and permissions as "
"<filename>sssd.conf</filename>."
msgstr ""
"Fragmentu failiem nepieciešams tāds pats īpašnieks un atļaujas kā <filename>"
"sssd.conf</filename>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:108
msgid "VENDOR PROVIDED CONFIGURATION"
msgstr "RAŽOTĀJA NODROŠINĀTĀ KONFIGURĀCIJA"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:111
msgid ""
"The vendor provided configuration file is installed in "
"<filename>&sssd_vendor_dir;/sssd.conf</filename>, but this file must not be "
"directly edited. It can be completely masked by creating the system specific "
"configuration file <filename>&sssd_conf_dir;/sssd.conf</filename>, or partly "
"overriden by creating config snippets in <filename>&sssd_conf_dir;/conf.d</"
"filename> directory."
msgstr ""
"Ražotāja nodrošinātais konfigurācijas fails tiek instalēts kā <filename>"
"&sssd_vendor_dir;/sssd.conf</filename>, bet šo failu nedrīkst rediģēt tieši. "
"To var pilnībā aizsegt, izveidojot sistēmai specifisku konfigurācijas failu "
"<filename>&sssd_conf_dir;/sssd.conf</filename>, vai daļēji aizstāt, "
"izveidojot konfigurācijas fragmentus direktorijā <filename>&sssd_conf_dir;/"
"conf.d</filename>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:120
msgid "CONFIGURATION FILE HIERARCHY"
msgstr "KONFIGURĀCIJAS FAILU HIERARHIJA"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:122
msgid ""
"When sssd reads the configuration it first tries to open the system specific "
"configuration file in <filename>&sssd_conf_dir;/sssd.conf</filename>. If it "
"exists, it is loaded and snippets from <filename>&sssd_conf_dir;/conf.d</"
"filename> are applied. The vendor provided configuration file "
"<filename>&sssd_vendor_dir;/sssd.conf</filename> is completely ignored in "
"this case."
msgstr ""
"Nolasot konfigurāciju, sssd vispirms mēģina atvērt sistēmai specifisko "
"konfigurācijas failu <filename>&sssd_conf_dir;/sssd.conf</filename>. Ja tas "
"eksistē, tas tiek ielādēts un tiek piemēroti fragmenti no <filename>"
"&sssd_conf_dir;/conf.d</filename>. Ražotāja nodrošinātais konfigurācijas "
"fails <filename>&sssd_vendor_dir;/sssd.conf</filename> šajā gadījumā tiek "
"pilnībā ignorēts."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:131
msgid ""
"If the system specific configuration file <filename>&sssd_conf_dir;/"
"sssd.conf</filename> does not exist, then the vendor configuration file "
"<filename>&sssd_vendor_dir;/sssd.conf</filename> is loaded and snippets from "
"<filename>&sssd_conf_dir;/conf.d</filename> are applied."
msgstr ""
"Ja sistēmai specifiskais konfigurācijas fails <filename>&sssd_conf_dir;/"
"sssd.conf</filename> neeksistē, tiek ielādēts ražotāja konfigurācijas fails "
"<filename>&sssd_vendor_dir;/sssd.conf</filename> un piemēroti fragmenti no "
"<filename>&sssd_conf_dir;/conf.d</filename>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:141
msgid "GENERAL OPTIONS"
msgstr "VISPĀRĪGĀS OPCIJAS"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:143
msgid "Following options are usable in more than one configuration sections."
msgstr ""
"Tālāk minētās opcijas var izmantot vairāk nekā vienā konfigurācijas sadaļā."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:147
msgid "Options usable in all sections"
msgstr "Opcijas, ko var izmantot visās sadaļās"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:149
msgid ""
"Note: Below options are ignored in <quote>[session_recording]</quote> "
"section, see <quote>Session recording configuration options</quote> section "
"for more details."
msgstr ""
"Piezīme: Tālāk minētās opcijas sadaļā <quote>[session_recording]</quote> "
"tiek ignorētas; sīkāk skatiet sadaļu <quote>Sesiju ierakstīšanas "
"konfigurācijas opcijas</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:156
msgid "debug_level (integer)"
msgstr "debug_level (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:160
msgid "debug (integer)"
msgstr "debug (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:163
msgid ""
"SSSD 1.14 and later also includes the <replaceable>debug</replaceable> alias "
"for <replaceable>debug_level</replaceable> as a convenience feature. If both "
"are specified, the value of <replaceable>debug_level</replaceable> will be "
"used."
msgstr ""
"SSSD 1.14 un jaunākās versijās ērtībai ir arī <replaceable>debug_level</"
"replaceable> aizstājvārds <replaceable>debug</replaceable>. Ja norādīti abi, "
"tiks izmantota <replaceable>debug_level</replaceable> vērtība."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:173
msgid "debug_timestamps (boolean)"
msgstr "debug_timestamps (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:176
msgid ""
"Add a timestamp to the debug messages.  If journald is enabled for SSSD "
"debug logging this option is ignored."
msgstr ""
"Pievienot atkļūdošanas ziņojumiem laikspiedolu.  Ja SSSD atkļūdošanas "
"žurnalēšanai ir iespējots journald, šī opcija tiek ignorēta."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:181 sssd.conf.5.xml:218 sssd.conf.5.xml:380
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:687 sssd.conf.5.xml:711 sssd.conf.5.xml:827
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:991 sssd.conf.5.xml:2236 sssd.conf.5.xml:4817
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:979 sssd-ldap.5.xml:1134 sssd-ldap.5.xml:1237
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1306 sssd-ldap.5.xml:1714 sssd-ldap.5.xml:1848
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1913 sssd-ipa.5.xml:341 sssd-ad.5.xml:252 sssd-ad.5.xml:367
#: sssd-ad.5.xml:1180 sssd-ad.5.xml:1375 sssd-krb5.5.xml:368
msgid "Default: true"
msgstr "Noklusējums: true"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:186
msgid "debug_microseconds (boolean)"
msgstr "debug_microseconds (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:189
msgid ""
"Add microseconds to the timestamp in debug messages.  If journald is enabled "
"for SSSD debug logging this option is ignored."
msgstr ""
"Pievienot atkļūdošanas ziņojumu laikspiedolam mikrosekundes.  Ja SSSD "
"atkļūdošanas žurnalēšanai ir iespējots journald, šī opcija tiek ignorēta."

#. type: Content of: <variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:194 sssd.conf.5.xml:2136 sssd.conf.5.xml:4450
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:363 sssd-ldap.5.xml:998 sssd-ldap.5.xml:1209
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1663 sssd-ldap.5.xml:1937 sssd-ipa.5.xml:141
#: sssd-ipa.5.xml:701 sssd-ad.5.xml:1140 sssd-idp.5.xml:287 sssd-krb5.5.xml:278
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:340 sssd-krb5.5.xml:442 include/krb5_options.xml:169
msgid "Default: false"
msgstr "Noklusējums: false"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:199
msgid "debug_backtrace_enabled (boolean)"
msgstr "debug_backtrace_enabled (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:202
msgid "Enable debug backtrace."
msgstr "Iespējot atkļūdošanas atpakaļceļu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:205
msgid ""
"In case SSSD is run with debug_level less than 9, everything is logged to a "
"ring buffer in memory and flushed to a log file on any error up to and "
"including `min(0x0040, debug_level)` (i.e. if debug_level is explicitly set "
"to 0 or 1 then only those error levels will trigger backtrace, otherwise up "
"to 2)."
msgstr ""
"Ja SSSD darbojas ar debug_level, kas mazāks par 9, viss tiek žurnalēts "
"atmiņas gredzenveida buferī un pie jebkuras kļūdas līdz `min(0x0040, "
"debug_level)` ieskaitot tiek izskalots žurnāla failā (t. i., ja debug_level "
"ir skaidri iestatīts uz 0 vai 1, atpakaļceļu izraisīs tikai šie kļūdu "
"līmeņi, citādi līdz 2)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:214
msgid ""
"Feature is only supported for `logger == files` (i.e.  setting doesn't have "
"effect for other logger types)."
msgstr ""
"Līdzeklis tiek atbalstīts tikai `logger == files` (t. i.  citiem žurnalētāju "
"tipiem iestatījumam nav ietekmes)."

