#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:227
msgid "Options usable in SERVICE and DOMAIN sections"
msgstr "Opcijas, ko var izmantot SERVICE un DOMAIN sadaļās"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:231
msgid "timeout (integer)"
msgstr "timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:234
msgid ""
"Timeout in seconds between heartbeats for this service. This is used to "
"ensure that the process is alive and capable of answering requests. Note "
"that after three missed heartbeats the process will terminate itself."
msgstr ""
"Noildze sekundēs starp šī pakalpojuma sirdspukstiem. To izmanto, lai "
"pārliecinātos, ka process ir dzīvs un spēj atbildēt uz pieprasījumiem. "
"Ņemiet vērā, ka pēc trim nokavētiem sirdspukstiem process pats beigs darbu."

#. type: Content of: <refsect1><refsect2><refsect3><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:241 sssd.conf.5.xml:1214 sssd.conf.5.xml:1724
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4466 sssd-ldap.5.xml:825 sssd-idp.5.xml:271
#: include/ldap_id_mapping.xml:270
msgid "Default: 10"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 10"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:251
msgid "SPECIAL SECTIONS"
msgstr "ĪPAŠĀS SADAĻAS"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:254
msgid "The [sssd] section"
msgstr "Sadaļa [sssd]"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:263
msgid "Section parameters"
msgstr "Sadaļas parametri"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:265
msgid "services (string)"
msgstr "services (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:268
msgid ""
"Comma separated list of services that are started when sssd itself starts.  "
"<phrase condition=\"have_systemd\"> The services' list is optional on "
"platforms where systemd is supported, as they will either be socket or D-Bus "
"activated when needed.  </phrase>"
msgstr ""
"Ar komatiem atdalīts pakalpojumu saraksts, kas tiek palaisti, kad palaižas "
"pats sssd.  <phrase condition=\"have_systemd\"> Platformās, kur tiek "
"atbalstīts systemd, pakalpojumu saraksts nav obligāts, jo tie vajadzības "
"gadījumā tiks aktivizēti caur ligzdu vai D-Bus.  </phrase>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:277
msgid ""
"Supported services: nss, pam, ifp <phrase condition=\"with_sudo\">, sudo</"
"phrase> <phrase condition=\"with_autofs\">, autofs</phrase> <phrase "
"condition=\"with_ssh\">, ssh</phrase> <phrase "
"condition=\"with_pac_responder\">, pac</phrase>"
msgstr ""
"Atbalstītie pakalpojumi: nss, pam, ifp <phrase condition=\"with_sudo\">, "
"sudo</phrase> <phrase condition=\"with_autofs\">, autofs</phrase> <phrase "
"condition=\"with_ssh\">, ssh</phrase> <phrase "
"condition=\"with_pac_responder\">, pac</phrase>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:284
msgid ""
"<phrase condition=\"have_systemd\"> By default, all services are disabled "
"and the administrator must enable the ones allowed to be used by executing: "
"\"systemctl enable sssd-@service@.socket\".  </phrase>"
msgstr ""
"<phrase condition=\"have_systemd\"> Pēc noklusējuma visi pakalpojumi ir "
"atspējoti, un administratoram jāiespējo tie, kurus atļauts izmantot, "
"izpildot: \"systemctl enable sssd-@service@.socket\".  </phrase>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:293 sssd.conf.5.xml:4649
msgid "domains (string)"
msgstr "domains (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:296
msgid ""
"A domain is a database containing user information. SSSD can use more "
"domains at the same time, but at least one must be configured or SSSD won't "
"start.  This parameter describes the list of domains in the order you want "
"them to be queried.  A domain name is recommended to contain only "
"alphanumeric ASCII characters, dashes, dots and underscores. '/' character "
"is forbidden."
msgstr ""
"Domēns ir datubāze, kas satur lietotāju informāciju. SSSD vienlaikus var "
"izmantot vairākus domēnus, bet vismaz vienam jābūt konfigurētam, citādi SSSD "
"nepalaidīsies.  Šis parametrs apraksta domēnu sarakstu tādā secībā, kādā "
"vēlaties tos vaicāt.  Domēna nosaukumā ieteicams izmantot tikai burtciparu "
"ASCII rakstzīmes, defises, punktus un pasvītras. Rakstzīme „/” ir aizliegta."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:309 sssd.conf.5.xml:3685
msgid "re_expression (string)"
msgstr "re_expression (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:312
msgid ""
"Default regular expression that describes how to parse the string containing "
"user name and domain into these components."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējuma regulārā izteiksme, kas apraksta, kā virkni, kas satur "
"lietotājvārdu un domēnu, sadalīt šajās komponentēs."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:317
msgid ""
"Each domain can have an individual regular expression configured. For some "
"ID providers there are also default regular expressions. See DOMAIN SECTIONS "
"for more info on these regular expressions."
msgstr ""
"Katram domēnam var konfigurēt atsevišķu regulāro izteiksmi. Dažiem ID "
"nodrošinātājiem ir arī noklusējuma regulārās izteiksmes. Plašāku informāciju "
"par šīm regulārajām izteiksmēm skatiet sadaļā DOMĒNU SADAĻAS."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:326 sssd.conf.5.xml:3742
msgid "full_name_format (string)"
msgstr "full_name_format (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:329 sssd.conf.5.xml:3745
msgid ""
"A <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>printf</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>3</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry>-compatible format that describes how to compose a "
"fully qualified name from user name and domain name components."
msgstr ""
"Ar <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>printf</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>3</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry> saderīgs formāts, kas apraksta, kā no "
"lietotājvārda un domēna nosaukuma komponentēm izveidot pilnībā kvalificētu "
"nosaukumu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:340 sssd.conf.5.xml:3756
msgid "%1$s"
msgstr "%1$s"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:341 sssd.conf.5.xml:3757
msgid "user name"
msgstr "lietotājvārds"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:344 sssd.conf.5.xml:3760
msgid "%2$s"
msgstr "%2$s"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:347 sssd.conf.5.xml:3763
msgid "domain name as specified in the SSSD config file."
msgstr "domēna nosaukums, kā norādīts SSSD konfigurācijas failā."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:353 sssd.conf.5.xml:3769
msgid "%3$s"
msgstr "%3$s"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:356 sssd.conf.5.xml:3772
msgid ""
"domain flat name. Mostly usable for Active Directory domains, both directly "
"configured or discovered via IPA trusts."
msgstr ""
"domēna plakanais nosaukums. Galvenokārt izmantojams Active Directory "
"domēniem — gan tieši konfigurētiem, gan atklātiem caur IPA uzticēšanās "
"attiecībām."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:337 sssd.conf.5.xml:3753
msgid ""
"The following expansions are supported: <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" "
"id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Tiek atbalstītas šādi izvērsumi: <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" "
"id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:366
msgid ""
"Each domain can have an individual format string configured.  See DOMAIN "
"SECTIONS for more info on this option."
msgstr ""
"Katram domēnam var konfigurēt atsevišķu formāta virkni.  Plašāku informāciju "
"par šo opciju skatiet sadaļā DOMĒNU SADAĻAS."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:372
msgid "monitor_resolv_conf (boolean)"
msgstr "monitor_resolv_conf (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:375
msgid ""
"Controls if SSSD should monitor the state of resolv.conf to identify when it "
"needs to update its internal DNS resolver."
msgstr ""
"Nosaka, vai SSSD jāuzrauga resolv.conf stāvoklis, lai noteiktu, kad "
"jāatjaunina tā iekšējais DNS atrisinātājs."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:385
msgid "try_inotify (boolean)"
msgstr "try_inotify (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:388
msgid ""
"By default, SSSD will attempt to use inotify to monitor configuration files "
"changes and will fall back to polling every five seconds if inotify cannot "
"be used."
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma SSSD mēģinās izmantot inotify, lai uzraudzītu konfigurācijas "
"failu izmaiņas, un, ja inotify nevar izmantot, pārslēgsies uz aptauju ik pēc "
"piecām sekundēm."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:394
msgid ""
"There are some limited situations where it is preferred that we should skip "
"even trying to use inotify. In these rare cases, this option should be set "
"to 'false'"
msgstr ""
"Ir dažas retas situācijas, kad vēlams pat nemēģināt izmantot inotify. Šajos "
"retajos gadījumos šī opcija jāiestata uz „false”"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:400
msgid ""
"Default: true on platforms where inotify is supported. False on other "
"platforms."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: true platformās, kur tiek atbalstīts inotify. False citās "
"platformās."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:404
msgid ""
"Note: this option will have no effect on platforms where inotify is "
"unavailable. On these platforms, polling will always be used."
msgstr ""
"Piezīme: platformās, kur inotify nav pieejams, šai opcijai nebūs ietekmes. "
"Šajās platformās vienmēr tiks izmantota aptauja."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:411
msgid "krb5_rcache_dir (string)"
msgstr "krb5_rcache_dir (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:414
msgid ""
"Directory on the filesystem where SSSD should store Kerberos replay cache "
"files."
msgstr ""
"Direktorija failu sistēmā, kurā SSSD jāglabā Kerberos atkārtošanas "
"kešatmiņas faili."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:418
msgid ""
"This option accepts a special value __LIBKRB5_DEFAULTS__ that will instruct "
"SSSD to let libkrb5 decide the appropriate location for the replay cache."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija pieņem īpašu vērtību __LIBKRB5_DEFAULTS__, kas liks SSSD ļaut "
"libkrb5 izlemt piemērotu atkārtošanas kešatmiņas atrašanās vietu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:424
msgid ""
"Default: Distribution-specific and specified at build-time. "
"(__LIBKRB5_DEFAULTS__ if not configured)"
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: atkarīgs no distribūcijas un norādīts būvēšanas laikā. "
"(__LIBKRB5_DEFAULTS__, ja nav konfigurēts)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:431
msgid "default_domain_suffix (string)"
msgstr "default_domain_suffix (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:434
msgid ""
"Please note that this option is deprecated and domain_resolution_order "
"should be used."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka šī opcija ir novecojusi un jāizmanto "
"domain_resolution_order."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:438
msgid ""
"This string will be used as a default domain name for all names without a "
"domain name component. The main use case is environments where the primary "
"domain is intended for managing host policies and all users are located in a "
"trusted domain.  The option allows those users to log in just with their "
"user name without giving a domain name as well."
msgstr ""
"Šī virkne tiks izmantota kā noklusējuma domēna nosaukums visiem nosaukumiem "
"bez domēna nosaukuma komponentes. Galvenais lietojuma gadījums ir vides, "
"kurās primārais domēns paredzēts resursdatoru politiku pārvaldībai, bet visi "
"lietotāji atrodas uzticamā domēnā.  Šī opcija ļauj šiem lietotājiem "
"pieteikties tikai ar savu lietotājvārdu, nenorādot arī domēna nosaukumu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:448
msgid ""
"Please note that if this option is set all users from the primary domain "
"have to use their fully qualified name, e.g. user@domain.name, to log in. "
"Setting this option changes default of use_fully_qualified_names to True. It "
"is not allowed to use this option together with use_fully_qualified_names "
"set to False."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā: ja šī opcija ir iestatīta, visiem primārā domēna "
"lietotājiem pieteikšanās jāizmanto savs pilnībā kvalificētais nosaukums, "
"piem., user@domain.name. Šīs opcijas iestatīšana maina "
"use_fully_qualified_names noklusējumu uz True. Šo opciju nav atļauts "
"izmantot kopā ar use_fully_qualified_names, kas iestatīts uz False."

#. type: Content of: <variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:457 sssd.conf.5.xml:2070 sssd-ldap.5.xml:937
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:949 sssd-ldap.5.xml:1042 sssd-ad.5.xml:926
#: sssd-ad.5.xml:1001 sssd-krb5.5.xml:478 sssd-ldap-attributes.5.xml:470
#: sssd-ldap-attributes.5.xml:978 include/ldap_id_mapping.xml:211
#: include/ldap_id_mapping.xml:222 include/krb5_options.xml:154
msgid "Default: not set"
msgstr "Noklusējums: nav iestatīts"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:462
msgid "override_space (string)"
msgstr "override_space (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:465
msgid ""
"This parameter will replace spaces (space bar)  with the given character for "
"user and group names.  e.g. (_). User name &quot;john doe&quot; will be "
"&quot;john_doe&quot; This feature was added to help compatibility with shell "
"scripts that have difficulty handling spaces, due to the default field "
"separator in the shell."
msgstr ""
"Šis parametrs lietotāju un grupu nosaukumos aizstās atstarpes (atstarpes "
"taustiņu) ar norādīto rakstzīmi.  Piem., (_). Lietotājvārds &quot;john "
"doe&quot; kļūs par &quot;john_doe&quot;. Šis līdzeklis pievienots, lai "
"uzlabotu saderību ar čaulas skriptiem, kuriem ir grūti apstrādāt atstarpes "
"čaulas noklusējuma lauku atdalītāja dēļ."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:474
msgid ""
"Please note it is a configuration error to use a replacement character that "
"might be used in user or group names. If a name contains the replacement "
"character SSSD tries to return the unmodified name but in general the result "
"of a lookup is undefined."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka par konfigurācijas kļūdu tiek uzskatīta tādas "
"aizstājējrakstzīmes izmantošana, kas var tikt lietota lietotāju vai grupu "
"nosaukumos. Ja nosaukums satur aizstājējrakstzīmi, SSSD mēģina atgriezt "
"nemainītu nosaukumu, bet kopumā uzmeklēšanas rezultāts nav definēts."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:482
msgid "Default: not set (spaces will not be replaced)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: nav iestatīts (atstarpes netiks aizstātas)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:487
msgid "certificate_verification (string)"
msgstr "certificate_verification (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:495
msgid "no_ocsp"
msgstr "no_ocsp"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:497
msgid ""
"Disables Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) checks. This might be "
"needed if the OCSP servers defined in the certificate are not reachable from "
"the client."
msgstr ""
"Atspējo tiešsaistes sertifikātu statusa protokola (OCSP) pārbaudes. Tas var "
"būt vajadzīgs, ja sertifikātā definētie OCSP serveri no klienta nav "
"sasniedzami."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:505
msgid "soft_ocsp"
msgstr "soft_ocsp"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:507
msgid ""
"If a connection cannot be established to an OCSP responder the OCSP check is "
"skipped.  This option should be used to allow authentication when the system "
"is offline and the OCSP responder cannot be reached."
msgstr ""
"Ja ar OCSP atbildētāju nevar izveidot savienojumu, OCSP pārbaude tiek "
"izlaista.  Šī opcija jāizmanto, lai atļautu autentifikāciju, kad sistēma ir "
"bezsaistē un OCSP atbildētājs nav sasniedzams."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:517
msgid "ocsp_dgst"
msgstr "ocsp_dgst"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:519
msgid ""
"Digest (hash) function used to create the certificate ID for the OCSP "
"request. Allowed values are:"
msgstr ""
"Īssavilkuma (jaucējvērtības) funkcija, ko izmanto, lai izveidotu sertifikāta "
"ID OCSP pieprasījumam. Atļautās vērtības:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:523
msgid "sha1"
msgstr "sha1"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:524
msgid "sha256"
msgstr "sha256"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:525
msgid "sha384"
msgstr "sha384"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:526
msgid "sha512"
msgstr "sha512"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:529
msgid "Default: sha1 (to allow compatibility with RFC5019-compliant responder)"
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: sha1 (lai nodrošinātu saderību ar RFC5019 atbilstošu "
"atbildētāju)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:535
msgid "no_verification"
msgstr "no_verification"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:537
msgid ""
"Disables verification completely.  This option should only be used for "
"testing."
msgstr "Pilnībā atspējo pārbaudi.  Šo opciju drīkst izmantot tikai testēšanai."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:543
msgid "partial_chain"
msgstr "partial_chain"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:545
msgid ""
"Allow verification to succeed even if a <replaceable>complete</replaceable> "
"chain cannot be built to a self-signed trust-anchor, provided it is possible "
"to construct a chain to a trusted certificate that might not be self-signed."
msgstr ""
"Atļaut pārbaudei izdoties, pat ja <replaceable>pilnu</replaceable> ķēdi līdz "
"pašparakstītam uzticamības enkuram nevar izveidot, ja vien iespējams "
"izveidot ķēdi līdz uzticamam sertifikātam, kas var nebūt pašparakstīts."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:554
msgid "ocsp_default_responder=URL"
msgstr "ocsp_default_responder=URL"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:556
msgid ""
"Sets the OCSP default responder which should be used instead of the one "
"mentioned in the certificate. URL must be replaced with the URL of the OCSP "
"default responder e.g.  http://example.com:80/ocsp."
msgstr ""
"Iestata OCSP noklusējuma atbildētāju, kas jāizmanto sertifikātā minētā "
"vietā. URL jāaizstāj ar OCSP noklusējuma atbildētāja URL, piem.,  http://"
"example.com:80/ocsp."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:566
msgid "ocsp_default_responder_signing_cert=NAME"
msgstr "ocsp_default_responder_signing_cert=NAME"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:568
msgid ""
"This option is currently ignored. All needed certificates must be available "
"in the PEM file given by pam_cert_db_path."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija pašlaik tiek ignorēta. Visiem vajadzīgajiem sertifikātiem jābūt "
"pieejamiem PEM failā, kas norādīts ar pam_cert_db_path."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:576
msgid "crl_file=/PATH/TO/CRL/FILE"
msgstr "crl_file=/PATH/TO/CRL/FILE"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:578
msgid ""
"Use the Certificate Revocation List (CRL) from the given file during the "
"verification of the certificate. The CRL must be given in PEM format, see "
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>crl</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>1ssl</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry> for details."
msgstr ""
"Sertifikāta pārbaudes laikā izmantot sertifikātu atsaukšanas sarakstu (CRL) "
"no norādītā faila. CRL jābūt PEM formātā; sīkāk skatiet <citerefentry> "
"<refentrytitle>crl</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>1ssl</manvolnum> </"
"citerefentry>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:591
msgid "soft_crl"
msgstr "soft_crl"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:594
msgid ""
"If a Certificate Revocation List (CRL)  is expired ignore the expiration "
"time of the CRL and check the related certificates with the expired CRL. "
"This option should be used to allow authentication when the system is "
"offline and the CRL cannot be renewed."
msgstr ""
"Ja sertifikātu atsaukšanas sarakstam (CRL)  beidzies derīgums, ignorēt CRL "
"derīguma beigu laiku un pārbaudīt saistītos sertifikātus ar novecojušo CRL. "
"Šī opcija jāizmanto, lai atļautu autentifikāciju, kad sistēma ir bezsaistē "
"un CRL nevar atjaunot."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:490
msgid ""
"With this parameter the certificate verification can be tuned with a comma "
"separated list of options. Supported options are: <placeholder "
"type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Ar šo parametru sertifikātu pārbaudi var pielāgot ar komatiem atdalītu "
"opciju sarakstu. Atbalstītās opcijas: <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" "
"id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:607
msgid "Unknown options are reported but ignored."
msgstr "Par nezināmām opcijām tiek ziņots, bet tās tiek ignorētas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:610
msgid "Default: not set, i.e. do not restrict certificate verification"
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: nav iestatīts, t. i., sertifikātu pārbaude netiek ierobežota"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:616
msgid "disable_netlink (boolean)"
msgstr "disable_netlink (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:619
msgid ""
"SSSD hooks into the netlink interface to monitor changes to routes, "
"addresses, links and trigger certain actions."
msgstr ""
"SSSD piesaistās netlink saskarnei, lai uzraudzītu maršrutu, adrešu, saišu "
"izmaiņas un izraisītu noteiktas darbības."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:624
msgid ""
"The SSSD state changes caused by netlink events may be undesirable and can "
"be disabled by setting this option to 'true'"
msgstr ""
"Netlink notikumu izraisītās SSSD stāvokļa izmaiņas var būt nevēlamas, un tās "
"var atspējot, iestatot šo opciju uz „true”"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:629
msgid "Default: false (netlink changes are detected)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: false (netlink izmaiņas tiek konstatētas)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:634
msgid "domain_resolution_order (string)"
msgstr "domain_resolution_order (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:637
msgid ""
"Comma separated list of domains and subdomains representing the lookup order "
"that will be followed.  The list doesn't have to include all possible "
"domains as the missing domains will be looked up based on the order they're "
"presented in the <quote>domains</quote> configuration option.  The "
"subdomains which are not listed as part of <quote>lookup_order</quote> will "
"be looked up in a random order for each parent domain."
msgstr ""
"Ar komatiem atdalīts domēnu un apakšdomēnu saraksts, kas nosaka uzmeklēšanas "
"secību.  Sarakstā nav jāiekļauj visi iespējamie domēni, jo trūkstošie domēni "
"tiks uzmeklēti tādā secībā, kādā tie norādīti konfigurācijas opcijā <quote>"
"domains</quote>.  Apakšdomēni, kas nav uzskaitīti <quote>lookup_order</quote>"
", katram vecākdomēnam tiks uzmeklēti nejaušā secībā."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:649
msgid ""
"Please, note that when this option is set the output format of all commands "
"is always fully-qualified even when using short names for input.  In case "
"the administrator wants the output not fully-qualified, the full_name_format "
"option can be used as shown below: <quote>full_name_format=%1$s</quote> "
"However, keep in mind that during login, login applications often "
"canonicalize the username by calling <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>getpwnam</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>3</manvolnum> </citerefentry> which, if a "
"shortname is returned for a qualified input (while trying to reach a user "
"which exists in multiple domains) might re-route the login attempt into the "
"domain which uses shortnames, making this workaround totally not recommended "
"in cases where usernames may overlap between domains."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā: ja šī opcija ir iestatīta, visu komandu izvades formāts "
"vienmēr ir pilnībā kvalificēts, pat ja ievadē izmantoti īsie nosaukumi.  Ja "
"administrators vēlas, lai izvade nebūtu pilnībā kvalificēta, var izmantot "
"opciju full_name_format, kā parādīts tālāk: <quote>full_name_format=%1$s</"
"quote> Tomēr paturiet prātā, ka pieteikšanās laikā pieteikšanās lietotnes "
"bieži kanonizē lietotājvārdu, izsaucot <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>"
"getpwnam</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>3</manvolnum> </citerefentry>, kas, ja "
"kvalificētai ievadei tiek atgriezts īsais nosaukums (mēģinot sasniegt "
"lietotāju, kas eksistē vairākos domēnos), var pāradresēt pieteikšanās "
"mēģinājumu uz domēnu, kurā izmanto īsos nosaukumus, tāpēc šis apiešanas "
"risinājums nav ieteicams gadījumos, kad lietotājvārdi domēnos var pārklāties."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:673 sssd.conf.5.xml:1085 sssd.conf.5.xml:1748
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4516 sssd-ad.5.xml:187 sssd-ad.5.xml:328 sssd-ad.5.xml:342
#: sssd-idp.5.xml:112 sssd-idp.5.xml:136 sssd-idp.5.xml:149 sssd-idp.5.xml:167
#: sssd-idp.5.xml:188
msgid "Default: Not set"
msgstr "Noklusējums: nav iestatīts"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:678
msgid "implicit_pac_responder (boolean)"
msgstr "implicit_pac_responder (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:681
msgid ""
"The PAC responder is enabled automatically for the IPA and AD provider to "
"evaluate and check the PAC. If it has to be disabled set this option to "
"'false'."
msgstr ""
"PAC atbildētājs IPA un AD nodrošinātājam tiek iespējots automātiski, lai "
"izvērtētu un pārbaudītu PAC. Ja tas jāatspējo, iestatiet šo opciju uz „false"
"”."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:692
msgid "core_dumpable (boolean)"
msgstr "core_dumpable (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:695
msgid ""
"This option can be used for general system hardening: setting it to 'false' "
"forbids core dumps for all SSSD processes to avoid leaking plain text "
"passwords. See man page prctl:PR_SET_DUMPABLE on Linux or "
"procctl:PROC_TRACE_CTL on FreeBSD for details."
msgstr ""
"Šo opciju var izmantot vispārējai sistēmas nostiprināšanai: iestatot to uz „"
"false”, visiem SSSD procesiem tiek aizliegtas kodola izmetes, lai novērstu "
"atklāta teksta paroļu noplūdi. Sīkāk skatiet rokasgrāmatas lapu "
"prctl:PR_SET_DUMPABLE Linux sistēmā vai procctl:PROC_TRACE_CTL FreeBSD."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:703
msgid ""
"Take a note that this setting has no effect for 'ldap_child', 'krb5_child' "
"and 'sssd_pam' as those privileged binaries can have a copy of a host keytab "
"data in a memory and their behavior in this regards is governed by /proc/sys/"
"fs/suid_dumpable system setting."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka šim iestatījumam nav ietekmes uz „ldap_child”, „krb5_child” "
"un „sssd_pam”, jo šiem priviliģētajiem binārajiem failiem atmiņā var būt "
"resursdatora keytab datu kopija, un to rīcību šajā ziņā nosaka sistēmas "
"iestatījums /proc/sys/fs/suid_dumpable."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:716
msgid "passkey_verification (string)"
msgstr "passkey_verification (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:724
msgid "user_verification (boolean)"
msgstr "user_verification (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:726
msgid ""
"Enable or disable the user verification (i.e. PIN, fingerprint)  during "
"authentication. If enabled, the PIN will always be requested."
msgstr ""
"Iespējot vai atspējot lietotāja pārbaudi (t. i., PIN, pirkstu nospiedums)  "
"autentifikācijas laikā. Ja iespējots, PIN tiks pieprasīts vienmēr."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:732
msgid ""
"The default is that the key settings decide what to do. In the IPA or "
"kerberos pre-authentication case, this value will be overwritten by the "
"server."
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma rīcību nosaka atslēgas iestatījumi. IPA vai kerberos "
"priekšautentifikācijas gadījumā šo vērtību pārrakstīs serveris."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:719
msgid ""
"With this parameter the passkey verification can be tuned with a comma "
"separated list of options. Supported options are: <placeholder "
"type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Ar šo parametru piekļuves atslēgu pārbaudi var pielāgot ar komatiem atdalītu "
"opciju sarakstu. Atbalstītās opcijas: <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" "
"id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:256
msgid ""
"Individual pieces of SSSD functionality are provided by special SSSD "
"services that are started and stopped together with SSSD.  The services are "
"managed by a special service frequently called <quote>monitor</quote>. The "
"<quote>[sssd]</quote> section is used to configure the monitor as well as "
"some other important options like the identity domains.  <placeholder "
"type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Atsevišķas SSSD funkcionalitātes daļas nodrošina īpaši SSSD pakalpojumi, kas "
"tiek palaisti un apturēti kopā ar SSSD.  Pakalpojumus pārvalda īpašs "
"pakalpojums, ko bieži sauc par <quote>monitoru</quote>. Sadaļu <quote>"
"[sssd]</quote> izmanto monitora, kā arī dažu citu svarīgu opciju, piemēram, "
"identitātes domēnu, konfigurēšanai.  <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" "
"id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:751
msgid "SERVICES SECTIONS"
msgstr "PAKALPOJUMU SADAĻAS"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:753
msgid ""
"Settings that can be used to configure different services are described in "
"this section. They should reside in the [<replaceable>$NAME</replaceable>] "
"section, for example, for NSS service, the section would be <quote>[nss]</"
"quote>"
msgstr ""
"Šajā sadaļā aprakstīti iestatījumi, ar kuriem var konfigurēt dažādus "
"pakalpojumus. Tiem jāatrodas sadaļā [<replaceable>$NAME</replaceable>]; "
"piemēram, NSS pakalpojumam sadaļa būtu <quote>[nss]</quote>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:760
msgid "General service configuration options"
msgstr "Vispārīgās pakalpojumu konfigurācijas opcijas"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:762
msgid "These options can be used to configure any service."
msgstr "Šīs opcijas var izmantot jebkura pakalpojuma konfigurēšanai."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:766
msgid "fd_limit (integer)"
msgstr "fd_limit (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:769
msgid ""
"This option specifies the maximum number of file descriptors that may be "
"opened at one time by this SSSD process. Note this value will be capped by "
"the init system at the startup of SSSD, see e.g.  man systemd.exec for "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija norāda maksimālo failu deskriptoru skaitu, ko šis SSSD process "
"vienlaikus var atvērt. Ņemiet vērā, ka init sistēma SSSD palaišanas brīdī šo "
"vērtību ierobežos; sīkāk skatiet, piem.,  man systemd.exec."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:776
msgid "Default: 8192 (or limits.conf \"hard\" limit)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 8192 (vai limits.conf \"hard\" ierobežojums)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:781
msgid "client_idle_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "client_idle_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:784
msgid ""
"This option specifies the number of seconds that a client of an SSSD process "
"can hold onto a file descriptor without communicating on it. This value is "
"limited in order to avoid resource exhaustion on the system. The timeout "
"can't be shorter than 10 seconds. If a lower value is configured, it will be "
"adjusted to 10 seconds."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija norāda sekunžu skaitu, cik ilgi SSSD procesa klients var turēt "
"faila deskriptoru, nesazinoties caur to. Šī vērtība ir ierobežota, lai "
"izvairītos no sistēmas resursu izsmelšanas. Noildze nevar būt īsāka par 10 "
"sekundēm. Ja konfigurēta mazāka vērtība, tā tiks pielāgota uz 10 sekundēm."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:793
msgid "Default: 60, KCM: 300"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 60, KCM: 300"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:798
msgid "responder_idle_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "responder_idle_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:801
msgid ""
"This option specifies the number of seconds that an SSSD responder process "
"can be up without being used. This value is limited in order to avoid "
"resource exhaustion on the system.  The minimum acceptable value for this "
"option is 60 seconds.  Setting this option to 0 (zero) means that no timeout "
"will be set up to the responder.  This option only has effect when SSSD is "
"built with systemd support and when services are either socket or D-Bus "
"activated."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija norāda sekunžu skaitu, cik ilgi SSSD atbildētāja process var "
"darboties, netiekot izmantots. Šī vērtība ir ierobežota, lai izvairītos no "
"sistēmas resursu izsmelšanas.  Minimālā pieņemamā šīs opcijas vērtība ir 60 "
"sekundes.  Iestatot šo opciju uz 0 (nulle), atbildētājam noildze netiks "
"iestatīta.  Šai opcijai ir ietekme tikai tad, ja SSSD ir būvēts ar systemd "
"atbalstu un pakalpojumi tiek aktivizēti caur ligzdu vai D-Bus."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:815 sssd.conf.5.xml:1138 sssd.conf.5.xml:2372
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:377
msgid "Default: 300"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 300"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:820
msgid "cache_first (boolean)"
msgstr "cache_first (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:823
msgid ""
"This option specifies whether the responder should query all caches before "
"querying the Data Providers."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija norāda, vai atbildētājam pirms datu nodrošinātāju vaicāšanas "
"jāvaicā visas kešatmiņas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:835
msgid "NSS configuration options"
msgstr "NSS konfigurācijas opcijas"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:837
msgid ""
"These options can be used to configure the Name Service Switch (NSS) service "
"and should be specified under the <quote>[nss]</quote> section."
msgstr ""
"Šīs opcijas var izmantot nosaukumu pakalpojumu komutatora (NSS) pakalpojuma "
"konfigurēšanai, un tās jānorāda sadaļā <quote>[nss]</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:843
msgid "enum_cache_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "enum_cache_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:846
msgid ""
"How many seconds should nss_sss cache enumerations (requests for info about "
"all users)"
msgstr ""
"Cik sekundes nss_sss jākešo uzskaitījumi (pieprasījumi pēc informācijas par "
"visiem lietotājiem)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:850
msgid "Default: 120"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 120"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:855
msgid "entry_cache_nowait_percentage (integer)"
msgstr "entry_cache_nowait_percentage (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:858
msgid ""
"The entry cache can be set to automatically update entries in the background "
"if they are requested beyond a percentage of the entry_cache_timeout value "
"for the domain."
msgstr ""
"Ierakstu kešatmiņu var iestatīt tā, lai ieraksti tiktu automātiski "
"atjaunināti fonā, ja tie tiek pieprasīti pēc noteiktas domēna "
"entry_cache_timeout vērtības procentuālās daļas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:864
msgid ""
"For example, if the domain's entry_cache_timeout is set to 30s and "
"entry_cache_nowait_percentage is set to 50 (percent), entries that come in "
"after 15 seconds past the last cache update will be returned immediately, "
"but the SSSD will go and update the cache on its own, so that future "
"requests will not need to block waiting for a cache update."
msgstr ""
"Piemēram, ja domēna entry_cache_timeout ir iestatīts uz 30s un "
"entry_cache_nowait_percentage ir iestatīts uz 50 (procentiem), ieraksti, kas "
"pieprasīti vēlāk nekā 15 sekundes pēc pēdējās kešatmiņas atjaunināšanas, "
"tiks atgriezti nekavējoties, bet SSSD pats atjauninās kešatmiņu, lai "
"turpmākajiem pieprasījumiem nebūtu jābloķējas, gaidot kešatmiņas "
"atjaunināšanu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:874
msgid ""
"Valid values for this option are 0-99 and represent a percentage of the "
"entry_cache_timeout for each domain. For performance reasons, this "
"percentage will never reduce the nowait timeout to less than 10 seconds.  (0 "
"disables this feature)"
msgstr ""
"Derīgās šīs opcijas vērtības ir 0–99, un tās nozīmē katra domēna "
"entry_cache_timeout procentuālo daļu. Veiktspējas apsvērumu dēļ šī "
"procentuālā daļa nekad nesamazinās nowait noildzi zem 10 sekundēm.  (0 "
"atspējo šo līdzekli)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:882 sssd.conf.5.xml:2157
msgid "Default: 50"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 50"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:887
msgid "entry_negative_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "entry_negative_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:890
msgid ""
"Specifies for how many seconds nss_sss should cache negative cache hits "
"(that is, queries for invalid database entries, like nonexistent ones)  "
"before asking the back end again."
msgstr ""
"Norāda, cik sekundes nss_sss jākešo negatīvie kešatmiņas trāpījumi (t. i., "
"vaicājumi pēc nederīgiem datubāzes ierakstiem, piemēram, neeksistējošiem), "
"pirms atkal vaicāt aizmugursistēmai."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:896 sssd.conf.5.xml:1736 sssd.conf.5.xml:2206
msgid "Default: 15"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 15"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:901
msgid "filter_users, filter_groups (string)"
msgstr "filter_users, filter_groups (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:904
msgid ""
"Exclude certain users or groups from being fetched from the sss NSS "
"database. This is particularly useful for system accounts. This option can "
"also be set per-domain or include fully-qualified names to filter only users "
"from the particular domain or by a user principal name (UPN)."
msgstr ""
"Izslēgt noteiktus lietotājus vai grupas no ienešanas no sss NSS datubāzes. "
"Tas īpaši noderīgi sistēmas kontiem. Šo opciju var iestatīt arī katram "
"domēnam atsevišķi vai iekļaut pilnībā kvalificētus nosaukumus, lai filtrētu "
"tikai konkrētā domēna lietotājus vai pēc lietotāja principāla nosaukuma (UPN)"
"."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:912
msgid ""
"NOTE: The filter_groups option doesn't affect inheritance of nested group "
"members, since filtering happens after they are propagated for returning via "
"NSS. E.g. a group having a member group filtered out will still have the "
"member users of the latter listed."
msgstr ""
"PIEZĪME: Opcija filter_groups neietekmē ligzdoto grupu dalībnieku mantošanu, "
"jo filtrēšana notiek pēc tam, kad tie ir izplatīti atgriešanai caur NSS. "
"Piem., grupai, kuras dalībnieka grupa ir izfiltrēta, joprojām būs uzskaitīti "
"pēdējās dalībnieki lietotāji."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:920
msgid ""
"NOTE: Please be aware that these options will only filter request on the "
"user or group name, but not on the UID or GID. If you also need to filter "
"the UID or GID, you have to set <quote>filter_uids</quote> or "
"<quote>filter_gids</quote> too."
msgstr ""
"PIEZĪME: Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka šīs opcijas filtrēs pieprasījumus tikai pēc "
"lietotāja vai grupas nosaukuma, bet ne pēc UID vai GID. Ja jāfiltrē arī UID "
"vai GID, jāiestata arī <quote>filter_uids</quote> vai <quote>filter_gids</"
"quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:927 sssd.conf.5.xml:975
msgid "Default: Not set."
msgstr "Noklusējums: nav iestatīts."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:930
msgid ""
"NOTE: The root user and group are always filtered out regardless of this "
"option."
msgstr ""
"PIEZĪME: Lietotājs un grupa root vienmēr tiek izfiltrēti neatkarīgi no šīs "
"opcijas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:936
msgid "filter_uids, filter_gids (string)"
msgstr "filter_uids, filter_gids (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:939
msgid ""
"Exclude certain UIDs or GIDs from being fetched from the sss NSS database. "
"Requests for a filtered ID are answered immediately with \"not found\", "
"without querying the back end at all, which avoids the latency and the "
"directory server load caused by lookups for IDs known never to exist there, "
"such as the ones of local system accounts."
msgstr ""
"Izslēgt noteiktus UID vai GID no ienešanas no sss NSS datubāzes. Uz "
"pieprasījumiem pēc filtrēta ID nekavējoties tiek atbildēts ar \"nav "
"atrasts\", vispār nevaicājot aizmugursistēmai, tādējādi izvairoties no "
"aiztures un direktoriju servera slodzes, ko rada uzmeklēšana pēc ID, kuri "
"tur noteikti neeksistē, piemēram, lokālo sistēmas kontu ID."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:948
msgid ""
"Each value is either a single ID or an inclusive range written as <quote>MIN-"
"MAX</quote> (spaces not allowed around the '-'). This option can also be set "
"per-domain, in which case it applies to that domain and its sub-domains only."
msgstr ""
"Katra vērtība ir vai nu viens ID, vai iekļaujošs diapazons, kas rakstīts kā "
"<quote>MIN-MAX</quote> (atstarpes ap „-” nav atļautas). Šo opciju var "
"iestatīt arī katram domēnam atsevišķi; tādā gadījumā tā attiecas tikai uz šo "
"domēnu un tā apakšdomēniem."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:955
msgid ""
"NOTE: As with <quote>filter_groups</quote>, filtering a GID doesn't affect "
"inheritance of nested group members, since filtering happens after they are "
"propagated for returning via NSS."
msgstr ""
"PIEZĪME: Tāpat kā ar <quote>filter_groups</quote>, GID filtrēšana neietekmē "
"ligzdoto grupu dalībnieku mantošanu, jo filtrēšana notiek pēc tam, kad tie "
"ir izplatīti atgriešanai caur NSS."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:961
msgid ""
"NOTE: These options will only filter request on the UID or GID, but not on "
"the name. If you also need to filter the name, you have to set "
"<quote>filter_users</quote> or <quote>filter_groups</quote> too."
msgstr ""
"PIEZĪME: Šīs opcijas filtrēs pieprasījumus tikai pēc UID vai GID, bet ne pēc "
"nosaukuma. Ja jāfiltrē arī nosaukums, jāiestata arī <quote>filter_users</"
"quote> vai <quote>filter_groups</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:970
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"filter_uids = 0-999, 65534\n"
"filter_gids = 0-999, 65534\n"
"                            "
msgstr ""
"filter_uids = 0-999, 65534\n"
"filter_gids = 0-999, 65534\n"
"                            "

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:968 sssd.conf.5.xml:1940 sssd.conf.5.xml:2087
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4129
msgid "Example: <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr "Piemērs: <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:978
msgid ""
"NOTE: The 0 user and group are always filtered out regardless of this option."
msgstr ""
"PIEZĪME: Lietotājs un grupa 0 vienmēr tiek izfiltrēti neatkarīgi no šīs "
"opcijas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:984
msgid "filter_users_in_groups (boolean)"
msgstr "filter_users_in_groups (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:987
msgid ""
"If you want filtered users to remain group members set this option to false"
msgstr ""
"Ja vēlaties, lai filtrētie lietotāji paliktu grupu dalībnieki, iestatiet šo "
"opciju uz false"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:998
msgid "fallback_homedir (string)"
msgstr "fallback_homedir (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1001
msgid ""
"Set a default template for a user's home directory if one is not specified "
"explicitly by the domain's data provider."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt noklusējuma veidni lietotāja mājas direktorijai, ja domēna datu "
"nodrošinātājs to nav norādījis skaidri."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1006
msgid ""
"The available values for this option are the same as for override_homedir."
msgstr "Šīs opcijas pieejamās vērtības ir tādas pašas kā override_homedir."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1012
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"fallback_homedir = /home/%u\n"
"                            "
msgstr ""
"fallback_homedir = /home/%u\n"
"                            "

#. type: Content of: <varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1010 sssd.conf.5.xml:1583 sssd.conf.5.xml:1602
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1704 sssd-krb5.5.xml:461 include/override_homedir.xml:78
msgid "example: <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr "piemērs: <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1016
msgid "Default: not set (no substitution for unset home directories)"
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: nav iestatīts (neiestatītām mājas direktorijām aizstāšana "
"netiek veikta)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1022
msgid "override_shell (string)"
msgstr "override_shell (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1025
msgid ""
"Override the login shell for all users. This option supersedes any other "
"shell options if it takes effect and can be set either in the [nss] section "
"or per-domain."
msgstr ""
"Aizstāt pieteikšanās čaulu visiem lietotājiem. Ja šī opcija stājas spēkā, tā "
"aizstāj visas citas čaulas opcijas, un to var iestatīt vai nu sadaļā [nss], "
"vai katram domēnam atsevišķi."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1031
msgid "Default: not set (SSSD will use the value retrieved from LDAP)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: nav iestatīts (SSSD izmantos no LDAP izgūto vērtību)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1037
msgid "allowed_shells (string)"
msgstr "allowed_shells (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1040
msgid ""
"Restrict user shell to one of the listed values. The order of evaluation is:"
msgstr ""
"Ierobežot lietotāja čaulu ar vienu no uzskaitītajām vērtībām. Izvērtēšanas "
"secība:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1043
msgid "1. If the shell is present in <quote>/etc/shells</quote>, it is used."
msgstr "1. Ja čaula ir <quote>/etc/shells</quote>, tā tiek izmantota."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1047
msgid ""
"2. If the shell is in the allowed_shells list but not in <quote>/etc/shells</"
"quote>, use the value of the shell_fallback parameter."
msgstr ""
"2. Ja čaula ir sarakstā allowed_shells, bet nav <quote>/etc/shells</quote>, "
"izmantot parametra shell_fallback vērtību."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1052
msgid ""
"3. If the shell is not in the allowed_shells list and not in <quote>/etc/"
"shells</quote>, a nologin shell is used."
msgstr ""
"3. Ja čaula nav ne sarakstā allowed_shells, ne <quote>/etc/shells</quote>, "
"tiek izmantota nologin čaula."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1057
msgid "The wildcard (*) can be used to allow any shell."
msgstr "Lai atļautu jebkuru čaulu, var izmantot aizstājējzīmi (*)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1060
msgid ""
"The (*) is useful if you want to use shell_fallback in case that user's "
"shell is not in <quote>/etc/shells</quote> and maintaining list of all "
"allowed shells in allowed_shells would be to much overhead."
msgstr ""
"(*) noder, ja vēlaties izmantot shell_fallback gadījumā, kad lietotāja čaula "
"nav <quote>/etc/shells</quote>, bet visu atļauto čaulu saraksta uzturēšana "
"allowed_shells būtu pārāk apgrūtinoša."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1067
msgid "An empty string for shell is passed as-is to libc."
msgstr "Tukša čaulas virkne tiek nodota libc bez izmaiņām."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1070
msgid ""
"The <quote>/etc/shells</quote> is only read on SSSD start up, which means "
"that a restart of the SSSD is required in case a new shell is installed."
msgstr ""
"<quote>/etc/shells</quote> tiek nolasīts tikai SSSD palaišanas laikā, tāpēc, "
"ja tiek instalēta jauna čaula, SSSD jārestartē."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1074
msgid "Default: Not set. The user shell is automatically used."
msgstr "Noklusējums: nav iestatīts. Lietotāja čaula tiek izmantota automātiski."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1079
msgid "vetoed_shells (string)"
msgstr "vetoed_shells (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1082
msgid "Replace any instance of these shells with the shell_fallback"
msgstr "Aizstāt jebkuru šo čaulu instanci ar shell_fallback"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1090
msgid "shell_fallback (string)"
msgstr "shell_fallback (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1093
msgid ""
"The default shell to use if an allowed shell is not installed on the machine."
msgstr "Noklusējuma čaula, ko izmantot, ja atļautā čaula datorā nav instalēta."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1097
msgid "Default: /bin/sh"
msgstr "Noklusējums: /bin/sh"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1102
msgid "default_shell (string)"
msgstr "default_shell (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1105
msgid ""
"The default shell to use if the provider does not return one during lookup. "
"This option can be specified globally in the [nss] section or per-domain."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējuma čaula, ko izmantot, ja nodrošinātājs uzmeklēšanas laikā to "
"neatgriež. Šo opciju var norādīt globāli sadaļā [nss] vai katram domēnam "
"atsevišķi."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1111
msgid ""
"Default: not set (Return NULL if no shell is specified and rely on libc to "
"substitute something sensible when necessary, usually /bin/sh)"
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: nav iestatīts (atgriezt NULL, ja čaula nav norādīta, un "
"paļauties, ka libc vajadzības gadījumā aizstās ar kaut ko saprātīgu, "
"parasti /bin/sh)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1118 sssd.conf.5.xml:1509
msgid "get_domains_timeout (int)"
msgstr "get_domains_timeout (int)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1121 sssd.conf.5.xml:1512
msgid ""
"Specifies time in seconds for which the list of subdomains will be "
"considered valid."
msgstr ""
"Norāda laiku sekundēs, cik ilgi apakšdomēnu saraksts tiks uzskatīts par "
"derīgu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1125 sssd.conf.5.xml:1516 sssd.conf.5.xml:1852
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:2949 sssd-ldap.5.xml:550
msgid "Default: 60"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 60"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1130
msgid "memcache_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "memcache_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1133
msgid ""
"Specifies time in seconds for which records in the in-memory cache will be "
"valid. Setting this option to zero will disable the in-memory cache."
msgstr ""
"Norāda laiku sekundēs, cik ilgi ieraksti atmiņas kešatmiņā būs derīgi. "
"Iestatot šo opciju uz nulli, atmiņas kešatmiņa tiks atspējota."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1141
msgid ""
"WARNING: Disabling the in-memory cache will have significant negative impact "
"on SSSD's performance and should only be used for testing."
msgstr ""
"BRĪDINĀJUMS: Atmiņas kešatmiņas atspējošana būtiski negatīvi ietekmēs SSSD "
"veiktspēju, un to drīkst izmantot tikai testēšanai."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1147 sssd.conf.5.xml:1172 sssd.conf.5.xml:1197
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1222 sssd.conf.5.xml:1249
msgid ""
"NOTE: If the environment variable SSS_NSS_USE_MEMCACHE is set to \"NO\", "
"client applications will not use the fast in-memory cache."
msgstr ""
"PIEZĪME: Ja vides mainīgais SSS_NSS_USE_MEMCACHE ir iestatīts uz \"NO\", "
"klientu lietotnes neizmantos ātro atmiņas kešatmiņu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1155
msgid "memcache_size_passwd (integer)"
msgstr "memcache_size_passwd (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1158
msgid ""
"Size (in megabytes) of the data table allocated inside fast in-memory cache "
"for passwd requests.  Setting the size to 0 will disable the passwd in-"
"memory cache."
msgstr ""
"Datu tabulas izmērs (megabaitos), kas ātrajā atmiņas kešatmiņā piešķirts "
"passwd pieprasījumiem.  Iestatot izmēru uz 0, passwd atmiņas kešatmiņa tiks "
"atspējota."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1164 sssd.conf.5.xml:3100 sssd-ldap.5.xml:604
msgid "Default: 8"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 8"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1167 sssd.conf.5.xml:1192 sssd.conf.5.xml:1217
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1244
msgid ""
"WARNING: Disabled or too small in-memory cache can have significant negative "
"impact on SSSD's performance."
msgstr ""
"BRĪDINĀJUMS: Atspējota vai pārāk maza atmiņas kešatmiņa var būtiski negatīvi "
"ietekmēt SSSD veiktspēju."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1180
msgid "memcache_size_group (integer)"
msgstr "memcache_size_group (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1183
msgid ""
"Size (in megabytes) of the data table allocated inside fast in-memory cache "
"for group requests.  Setting the size to 0 will disable the group in-memory "
"cache."
msgstr ""
"Datu tabulas izmērs (megabaitos), kas ātrajā atmiņas kešatmiņā piešķirts "
"group pieprasījumiem.  Iestatot izmēru uz 0, group atmiņas kešatmiņa tiks "
"atspējota."

#. type: Content of: <variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1189 sssd.conf.5.xml:1241 sssd.conf.5.xml:3922
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:534 sssd-ldap.5.xml:581 include/failover.xml:116
#: include/krb5_options.xml:11
msgid "Default: 6"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 6"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1205
msgid "memcache_size_initgroups (integer)"
msgstr "memcache_size_initgroups (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1208
msgid ""
"Size (in megabytes) of the data table allocated inside fast in-memory cache "
"for initgroups requests.  Setting the size to 0 will disable the initgroups "
"in-memory cache."
msgstr ""
"Datu tabulas izmērs (megabaitos), kas ātrajā atmiņas kešatmiņā piešķirts "
"initgroups pieprasījumiem.  Iestatot izmēru uz 0, initgroups atmiņas "
"kešatmiņa tiks atspējota."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1230
msgid "memcache_size_sid (integer)"
msgstr "memcache_size_sid (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1233
msgid ""
"Size (in megabytes) of the data table allocated inside fast in-memory cache "
"for SID related requests.  Only SID-by-ID and ID-by-SID requests are "
"currently cached in fast in-memory cache.  Setting the size to 0 will "
"disable the SID in-memory cache."
msgstr ""
"Datu tabulas izmērs (megabaitos), kas ātrajā atmiņas kešatmiņā piešķirts ar "
"SID saistītiem pieprasījumiem.  Ātrajā atmiņas kešatmiņā pašlaik tiek kešoti "
"tikai SID-by-ID un ID-by-SID pieprasījumi.  Iestatot izmēru uz 0, SID "
"atmiņas kešatmiņa tiks atspējota."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1257 sssd-ifp.5.xml:90
msgid "user_attributes (string)"
msgstr "user_attributes (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1260
msgid ""
"Some of the additional NSS responder requests can return more attributes "
"than just the POSIX ones defined by the NSS interface. The list of "
"attributes is controlled by this option. It is handled the same way as the "
"<quote>user_attributes</quote> option of the InfoPipe responder (see "
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd-ifp</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry> for details) but with no default values."
msgstr ""
"Daži papildu NSS atbildētāja pieprasījumi var atgriezt vairāk atribūtu nekā "
"tikai NSS saskarnes definētos POSIX atribūtus. Atribūtu sarakstu nosaka šī "
"opcija. Tā tiek apstrādāta tāpat kā InfoPipe atbildētāja opcija <quote>"
"user_attributes</quote> (sīkāk skatiet <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd-"
"ifp</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</manvolnum> </citerefentry>), bet bez "
"noklusējuma vērtībām."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1273
msgid ""
"To make configuration more easy the NSS responder will check the InfoPipe "
"option if it is not set for the NSS responder."
msgstr ""
"Lai vienkāršotu konfigurēšanu, NSS atbildētājs pārbaudīs InfoPipe opciju, ja "
"tā nav iestatīta NSS atbildētājam."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1278
msgid "Default: not set, fallback to InfoPipe option"
msgstr "Noklusējums: nav iestatīts, tiek izmantota InfoPipe opcija"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1283
msgid "pwfield (string)"
msgstr "pwfield (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1286
msgid ""
"The value that NSS operations that return users or groups will return for "
"the <quote>password</quote> field."
msgstr ""
"Vērtība, ko NSS darbības, kas atgriež lietotājus vai grupas, atgriezīs laukā "
"<quote>password</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1291
msgid ""
"This option can also be set per-domain, which overwrites the value in the "
"<quote>[nss]</quote> section for that domain. This is particularly useful "
"when using a proxy domain with <option>proxy_lib_name=files</option> and a "
"<option>proxy_pam_target</option> other than <quote>sssd-shadowutils</"
"quote>. In that case, SSSD returns <quote>*</quote> for the password field "
"by default, which causes <command>pam_unix</command> to treat all accounts "
"as locked. Setting <option>pwfield = x</option> in the domain section "
"restores the expected behavior."
msgstr ""
"Šo opciju var iestatīt arī katram domēnam atsevišķi; tad tā aizstāj šī "
"domēna vērtību sadaļā <quote>[nss]</quote>. Tas īpaši noderīgi, izmantojot "
"starpniekdomēnu ar <option>proxy_lib_name=files</option> un <option>"
"proxy_pam_target</option>, kas nav <quote>sssd-shadowutils</quote>. Tādā "
"gadījumā SSSD pēc noklusējuma paroles laukā atgriež <quote>*</quote>, kā "
"rezultātā <command>pam_unix</command> visus kontus uzskata par bloķētiem. "
"Iestatot domēna sadaļā <option>pwfield = x</option>, tiek atjaunota gaidītā "
"rīcība."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1305
msgid "Default: <quote>*</quote>"
msgstr "Noklusējums: <quote>*</quote>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1308
msgid ""
"Default (per-domain): <quote>not set</quote> (remote domains), <quote>x</"
"quote> (proxy domain with nss_files and sssd-shadowutils target)"
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums (katram domēnam): <quote>nav iestatīts</quote> (attālie domēni), "
"<quote>x</quote> (starpniekdomēns ar nss_files un sssd-shadowutils mērķi)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1317
msgid "PAM configuration options"
msgstr "PAM konfigurācijas opcijas"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1319
msgid ""
"These options can be used to configure the Pluggable Authentication Module "
"(PAM) service and should be specified under the <quote>[pam]</quote> section."
msgstr ""
"Šīs opcijas var izmantot spraudņautentifikācijas moduļa (PAM) pakalpojuma "
"konfigurēšanai, un tās jānorāda sadaļā <quote>[pam]</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1325
msgid "offline_credentials_expiration (integer)"
msgstr "offline_credentials_expiration (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1328
msgid ""
"If the authentication provider is offline, how long should we allow cached "
"logins (in days since the last successful online login)."
msgstr ""
"Ja autentifikācijas nodrošinātājs ir bezsaistē, cik ilgi atļaut kešotās "
"pieteikšanās (dienās kopš pēdējās veiksmīgās tiešsaistes pieteikšanās)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1333 sssd.conf.5.xml:1346
msgid "Default: 0 (No limit)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 0 (bez ierobežojuma)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1339
msgid "offline_failed_login_attempts (integer)"
msgstr "offline_failed_login_attempts (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1342
msgid ""
"If the authentication provider is offline, how many failed login attempts "
"are allowed."
msgstr ""
"Ja autentifikācijas nodrošinātājs ir bezsaistē, cik neveiksmīgu pieteikšanās "
"mēģinājumu ir atļauts."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1352
msgid "offline_failed_login_delay (integer)"
msgstr "offline_failed_login_delay (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1355
msgid ""
"The time in minutes which has to pass after offline_failed_login_attempts "
"has been reached before a new login attempt is possible."
msgstr ""
"Laiks minūtēs, kam jāpaiet pēc offline_failed_login_attempts sasniegšanas, "
"pirms iespējams jauns pieteikšanās mēģinājums."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1360
msgid ""
"If set to 0 the user cannot authenticate offline if "
"offline_failed_login_attempts has been reached. Only a successful online "
"authentication can enable offline authentication again."
msgstr ""
"Ja iestatīts uz 0, lietotājs pēc offline_failed_login_attempts sasniegšanas "
"nevar autentificēties bezsaistē. Bezsaistes autentifikāciju atkal var "
"iespējot tikai veiksmīga tiešsaistes autentifikācija."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1366 sssd.conf.5.xml:1476
msgid "Default: 5"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 5"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1372
msgid "pam_verbosity (integer)"
msgstr "pam_verbosity (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1375
msgid ""
"Controls what kind of messages are shown to the user during authentication. "
"The higher the number to more messages are displayed."
msgstr ""
"Nosaka, kāda veida ziņojumi autentifikācijas laikā tiek rādīti lietotājam. "
"Jo lielāks skaitlis, jo vairāk ziņojumu tiek rādīts."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1380
msgid "Currently sssd supports the following values:"
msgstr "Pašlaik sssd atbalsta šādas vērtības:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1383
msgid "<emphasis>0</emphasis>: do not show any message"
msgstr "<emphasis>0</emphasis>: nerādīt nekādus ziņojumus"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1386
msgid "<emphasis>1</emphasis>: show only important messages"
msgstr "<emphasis>1</emphasis>: rādīt tikai svarīgus ziņojumus"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1390
msgid "<emphasis>2</emphasis>: show informational messages"
msgstr "<emphasis>2</emphasis>: rādīt informatīvus ziņojumus"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1393
msgid "<emphasis>3</emphasis>: show all messages and debug information"
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>3</emphasis>: rādīt visus ziņojumus un atkļūdošanas informāciju"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1397 sssd.8.xml:63
msgid "Default: 1"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 1"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1403
msgid "pam_response_filter (string)"
msgstr "pam_response_filter (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1406
msgid ""
"A comma separated list of strings which allows to remove (filter) data sent "
"by the PAM responder to pam_sss PAM module. There are different kind of "
"responses sent to pam_sss e.g. messages displayed to the user or environment "
"variables which should be set by pam_sss."
msgstr ""
"Ar komatiem atdalīts virkņu saraksts, kas ļauj noņemt (filtrēt) datus, ko "
"PAM atbildētājs sūta PAM modulim pam_sss. Uz pam_sss tiek sūtītas dažāda "
"veida atbildes, piem., lietotājam rādāmi ziņojumi vai vides mainīgie, kas "
"pam_sss jāiestata."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1414
msgid ""
"While messages already can be controlled with the help of the pam_verbosity "
"option this option allows to filter out other kind of responses as well."
msgstr ""
"Kamēr ziņojumus jau var vadīt ar opciju pam_verbosity, šī opcija ļauj "
"izfiltrēt arī cita veida atbildes."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1421
msgid "ENV"
msgstr "ENV"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1422
msgid "Do not send any environment variables to any service."
msgstr "Nesūtīt nevienam pakalpojumam nekādus vides mainīgos."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1425
msgid "ENV:var_name"
msgstr "ENV:var_name"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1426
msgid "Do not send environment variable var_name to any service."
msgstr "Nesūtīt nevienam pakalpojumam vides mainīgo var_name."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1430
msgid "ENV:var_name:service"
msgstr "ENV:var_name:service"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1431
msgid "Do not send environment variable var_name to service."
msgstr "Nesūtīt pakalpojumam service vides mainīgo var_name."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1419
msgid ""
"Currently the following filters are supported: <placeholder "
"type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Pašlaik tiek atbalstīti šādi filtri: <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" "
"id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1438
msgid ""
"The list of strings can either be the list of filters which would set this "
"list of filters and overwrite the defaults. Or each element of the list can "
"be prefixed by a '+' or '-' character which would add the filter to the "
"existing default or remove it from the defaults, respectively. Please note "
"that either all list elements must have a '+' or '-' prefix or none. It is "
"considered as an error to mix both styles."
msgstr ""
"Virkņu saraksts var būt vai nu filtru saraksts, kas iestatītu šo filtru "
"sarakstu un pārrakstītu noklusējumus, vai arī katram saraksta elementam var "
"būt priedēklis „+” vai „-”, kas attiecīgi pievienotu filtru esošajiem "
"noklusējumiem vai noņemtu to no noklusējumiem. Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka "
"priedēklis „+” vai „-” jābūt vai nu visiem saraksta elementiem, vai "
"nevienam. Abu stilu jaukšana tiek uzskatīta par kļūdu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1449
msgid "Default: ENV:KRB5CCNAME:sudo, ENV:KRB5CCNAME:sudo-i"
msgstr "Noklusējums: ENV:KRB5CCNAME:sudo, ENV:KRB5CCNAME:sudo-i"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1452
msgid ""
"Example: -ENV:KRB5CCNAME:sudo-i will remove the filter from the default list"
msgstr "Piemērs: -ENV:KRB5CCNAME:sudo-i noņems filtru no noklusējuma saraksta"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1459
msgid "pam_id_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "pam_id_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1462
msgid ""
"For any PAM request while SSSD is online, the SSSD will attempt to "
"immediately update the cached identity information for the user in order to "
"ensure that authentication takes place with the latest information."
msgstr ""
"Katram PAM pieprasījumam, kamēr SSSD ir tiešsaistē, SSSD mēģinās "
"nekavējoties atjaunināt lietotāja kešoto identitātes informāciju, lai "
"autentifikācija notiktu ar jaunāko informāciju."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1468
msgid ""
"A complete PAM conversation may perform multiple PAM requests, such as "
"account management and session opening. This option controls (on a per-"
"client-application basis) how long (in seconds) we can cache the identity "
"information to avoid excessive round-trips to the identity provider."
msgstr ""
"Pilnā PAM sarunā var tikt veikti vairāki PAM pieprasījumi, piemēram, kontu "
"pārvaldība un sesijas atvēršana. Šī opcija (katrai klienta lietotnei "
"atsevišķi) nosaka, cik ilgi (sekundēs) identitātes informāciju var kešot, "
"lai izvairītos no pārmērīgiem vaicājumiem identitātes nodrošinātājam."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1482
msgid "pam_pwd_expiration_warning (integer)"
msgstr "pam_pwd_expiration_warning (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1485 sssd.conf.5.xml:3124
msgid "Display a warning N days before the password expires."
msgstr "Rādīt brīdinājumu N dienas pirms paroles derīguma beigām."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1488
msgid ""
"Please note that the backend server has to provide information about the "
"expiration time of the password.  If this information is missing, sssd "
"cannot display a warning."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka aizmugursistēmas serverim jānodrošina informācija par "
"paroles derīguma beigu laiku.  Ja šīs informācijas nav, sssd nevar parādīt "
"brīdinājumu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1494 sssd.conf.5.xml:3127
msgid ""
"If zero is set, then this filter is not applied, i.e. if the expiration "
"warning was received from backend server, it will automatically be displayed."
msgstr ""
"Ja iestatīta nulle, šis filtrs netiek piemērots, t. i., ja derīguma beigu "
"brīdinājums tika saņemts no aizmugursistēmas servera, tas tiks parādīts "
"automātiski."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1499
msgid ""
"This setting can be overridden by setting <emphasis>pwd_expiration_warning</"
"emphasis> for a particular domain."
msgstr ""
"Šo iestatījumu var aizstāt, konkrētam domēnam iestatot <emphasis>"
"pwd_expiration_warning</emphasis>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1504 sssd.conf.5.xml:4205 sssd-ldap.5.xml:662
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1733 sssd.8.xml:79
msgid "Default: 0"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 0"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1521
msgid "pam_trusted_users (string)"
msgstr "pam_trusted_users (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1524
msgid ""
"Specifies the comma-separated list of UID values or user names that are "
"allowed to run PAM conversations against trusted domains.  Users not "
"included in this list can only access domains marked as public with "
"<quote>pam_public_domains</quote>.  User names are resolved to UIDs at "
"startup."
msgstr ""
"Norāda ar komatiem atdalītu UID vērtību vai lietotājvārdu sarakstu, kuriem "
"atļauts veikt PAM sarunas ar uzticamiem domēniem.  Lietotāji, kas nav "
"iekļauti šajā sarakstā, var piekļūt tikai domēniem, kas atzīmēti kā publiski "
"ar <quote>pam_public_domains</quote>.  Lietotājvārdi palaišanas laikā tiek "
"atrisināti uz UID."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1534
msgid "Default: All users are considered trusted by default"
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: pēc noklusējuma visi lietotāji tiek uzskatīti par uzticamiem"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1538
msgid ""
"Please note that UID 0 is always allowed to access the PAM responder even in "
"case it is not in the pam_trusted_users list."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka UID 0 vienmēr drīkst piekļūt PAM atbildētājam, pat ja "
"tas nav sarakstā pam_trusted_users."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1545
msgid "pam_public_domains (string)"
msgstr "pam_public_domains (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1548
msgid ""
"Specifies the comma-separated list of domain names that are accessible even "
"to untrusted users."
msgstr ""
"Norāda ar komatiem atdalītu domēnu nosaukumu sarakstu, kas pieejami arī "
"neuzticamiem lietotājiem."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1552
msgid "Two special values for pam_public_domains option are defined:"
msgstr "Opcijai pam_public_domains ir definētas divas īpašas vērtības:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1556
msgid ""
"all (Untrusted users are allowed to access all domains in PAM responder.)"
msgstr ""
"all (neuzticamiem lietotājiem PAM atbildētājā atļauts piekļūt visiem "
"domēniem.)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1560
msgid ""
"none (Untrusted users are not allowed to access any domains PAM in "
"responder.)"
msgstr ""
"none (neuzticamiem lietotājiem PAM atbildētājā nav atļauts piekļūt nevienam "
"domēnam.)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1564 sssd.conf.5.xml:1589 sssd.conf.5.xml:1608
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1885 sssd.conf.5.xml:4135 sssd-ldap.5.xml:1270
msgid "Default: none"
msgstr "Noklusējums: none"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1569
msgid "pam_account_expired_message (string)"
msgstr "pam_account_expired_message (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1572
msgid ""
"Allows a custom expiration message to be set, replacing the default "
"'Permission denied' message."
msgstr ""
"Ļauj iestatīt pielāgotu derīguma beigu ziņojumu, kas aizstāj noklusējuma "
"ziņojumu „Permission denied”."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1577
msgid ""
"Note: Please be aware that message is only printed for the SSH service "
"unless pam_verbosity is set to 3 (show all messages and debug information)."
msgstr ""
"Piezīme: lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka ziņojums tiek izvadīts tikai SSH "
"pakalpojumam, ja vien pam_verbosity nav iestatīts uz 3 (rādīt visus "
"ziņojumus un atkļūdošanas informāciju)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1585
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"pam_account_expired_message = Account expired, please contact help desk.\n"
"                            "
msgstr ""
"pam_account_expired_message = Konta derīgums beidzies, lūdzu, sazinieties ar "
"palīdzības dienestu.\n"
"                            "

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1594
msgid "pam_account_locked_message (string)"
msgstr "pam_account_locked_message (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1597
msgid ""
"Allows a custom lockout message to be set, replacing the default 'Permission "
"denied' message."
msgstr ""
"Ļauj iestatīt pielāgotu bloķēšanas ziņojumu, kas aizstāj noklusējuma "
"ziņojumu „Permission denied”."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1604
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"pam_account_locked_message = Account locked, please contact help desk.\n"
"                            "
msgstr ""
"pam_account_locked_message = Konts bloķēts, lūdzu, sazinieties ar palīdzības "
"dienestu.\n"
"                            "

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1613
msgid "pam_passkey_auth (boolean)"
msgstr "pam_passkey_auth (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1616
msgid "Enable passkey device based authentication."
msgstr "Iespējot uz piekļuves atslēgas ierīcēm balstītu autentifikāciju."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1619 sssd.conf.5.xml:1971 sssd-ad.5.xml:1279
#: sss_rpcidmapd.5.xml:76
msgid "Default: True"
msgstr "Noklusējums: True"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1624
msgid "passkey_debug_libfido2 (boolean)"
msgstr "passkey_debug_libfido2 (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1627
msgid "Enable libfido2 library debug messages."
msgstr "Iespējot libfido2 bibliotēkas atkļūdošanas ziņojumus."

#. type: Content of: <refsect1><refsect2><refsect3><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1630 sssd.conf.5.xml:1644 sssd.conf.5.xml:4868
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:727 sssd-ldap.5.xml:752 sssd-ldap.5.xml:848
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1356 sssd-ad.5.xml:506 sssd-ad.5.xml:582 sssd-ad.5.xml:1160
#: include/ldap_id_mapping.xml:250
msgid "Default: False"
msgstr "Noklusējums: False"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1635
msgid "pam_cert_auth (boolean)"
msgstr "pam_cert_auth (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1638
msgid ""
"Enable certificate based Smartcard authentication.  Since this requires "
"additional communication with the Smartcard which will delay the "
"authentication process this option is disabled by default."
msgstr ""
"Iespējot uz sertifikātiem balstītu viedkaršu autentifikāciju.  Tā kā tam "
"nepieciešama papildu saziņa ar viedkarti, kas aizkavēs autentifikācijas "
"procesu, šī opcija pēc noklusējuma ir atspējota."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1647
msgid ""
"Note: In case OpenSC is used for Smartcard access SSSD supports the "
"filesystem caching in OpenSC when enabled in opensc.conf. The cached files "
"are located in a common <quote>opensc</quote> directory in SSSD's state "
"directory.  The behaviour can be changed in opensc.conf"
msgstr ""
"Piezīme: ja viedkaršu piekļuvei izmanto OpenSC, SSSD atbalsta failu sistēmas "
"kešošanu OpenSC, ja tā iespējota opensc.conf. Kešotie faili atrodas kopīgā "
"direktorijā <quote>opensc</quote> SSSD stāvokļa direktorijā.  Rīcību var "
"mainīt opensc.conf"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1656
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"app /usr/libexec/sssd/p11_child {\n"
"        framework pkcs15 {\n"
"                use_file_caching = no;\n"
"        }\n"
"}\n"
"app /usr/libexec/sssd/krb5_child {\n"
"        framework pkcs15 {\n"
"                use_file_caching = no;\n"
"        }\n"
"}\n"
"                            "
msgstr ""
"app /usr/libexec/sssd/p11_child {\n"
"        framework pkcs15 {\n"
"                use_file_caching = no;\n"
"        }\n"
"}\n"
"app /usr/libexec/sssd/krb5_child {\n"
"        framework pkcs15 {\n"
"                use_file_caching = no;\n"
"        }\n"
"}\n"
"                            "

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1654
msgid ""
"Example opensc.conf (*): <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"opensc.conf piemērs (*): <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1669
msgid ""
"(*) The actual <quote>libexec</quote> directory for p11_child and krb5_child "
"depends on the distribution."
msgstr ""
"(*) Faktiskā p11_child un krb5_child direktorija <quote>libexec</quote> ir "
"atkarīga no distribūcijas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1674
msgid "pam_cert_db_path (string)"
msgstr "pam_cert_db_path (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1677
msgid "The path to the certificate database."
msgstr "Ceļš uz sertifikātu datubāzi."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1680 sssd.conf.5.xml:2286 sssd.conf.5.xml:4630
msgid "Default:"
msgstr "Noklusējums:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1682 sssd.conf.5.xml:2288
msgid ""
"/etc/sssd/pki/sssd_auth_ca_db.pem (path to a file with trusted CA "
"certificates in PEM format)"
msgstr ""
"/etc/sssd/pki/sssd_auth_ca_db.pem (ceļš uz failu ar uzticamiem CA "
"sertifikātiem PEM formātā)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1692
msgid "pam_cert_verification (string)"
msgstr "pam_cert_verification (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1695
msgid ""
"With this parameter the PAM certificate verification can be tuned with a "
"comma separated list of options that override the "
"<quote>certificate_verification</quote> value in <quote>[sssd]</quote> "
"section.  Supported options are the same of <quote>certificate_verification</"
"quote>."
msgstr ""
"Ar šo parametru PAM sertifikātu pārbaudi var pielāgot ar komatiem atdalītu "
"opciju sarakstu, kas aizstāj vērtību <quote>certificate_verification</quote> "
"sadaļā <quote>[sssd]</quote>.  Atbalstītās opcijas ir tādas pašas kā <quote>"
"certificate_verification</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1706
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"pam_cert_verification = partial_chain\n"
"                            "
msgstr ""
"pam_cert_verification = partial_chain\n"
"                            "

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1710
msgid ""
"Default: not set, i.e. use default <quote>certificate_verification</quote> "
"option defined in <quote>[sssd]</quote> section."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: nav iestatīts, t. i., tiek izmantota sadaļā <quote>[sssd]</"
"quote> definētā noklusējuma opcija <quote>certificate_verification</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:1717
msgid "p11_child_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "p11_child_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

