#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4174
msgid ""
"Various tags stored by the realmd configuration service for this domain."
msgstr "Dažādas birkas, ko šim domēnam glabā konfigurācijas pakalpojums realmd."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4180
msgid "cached_auth_timeout (int)"
msgstr "cached_auth_timeout (int)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4183
msgid ""
"Specifies the number of seconds since the last successful online "
"authentication during which SSSD will authenticate users via cached "
"credentials, even while online.  If the cached authentication fails, SSSD "
"immediately falls back to online authentication."
msgstr ""
"Norāda sekunžu skaitu kopš pēdējās veiksmīgās tiešsaistes autentifikācijas, "
"kuru laikā SSSD autentificēs lietotājus ar kešotiem akreditācijas datiem, "
"pat esot tiešsaistē.  Ja kešotā autentifikācija neizdodas, SSSD nekavējoties "
"pārslēdzas uz tiešsaistes autentifikāciju."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4190
msgid ""
"This option's value is inherited by all trusted domains. At the moment it is "
"not possible to set a different value per trusted domain."
msgstr ""
"Šīs opcijas vērtību manto visi uzticamie domēni. Pašlaik nav iespējams "
"iestatīt atšķirīgu vērtību katram uzticamajam domēnam."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4195
msgid "Special value 0 implies that this feature is disabled."
msgstr "Īpašā vērtība 0 nozīmē, ka šis līdzeklis ir atspējots."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4199
msgid ""
"Please note that if <quote>cached_auth_timeout</quote> is longer than "
"<quote>pam_id_timeout</quote> then the back end could be called to handle "
"<quote>initgroups.</quote>"
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā: ja <quote>cached_auth_timeout</quote> ir garāks par "
"<quote>pam_id_timeout</quote>, aizmugursistēma var tikt izsaukta, lai "
"apstrādātu <quote>initgroups.</quote>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4210
msgid "local_auth_policy (string)"
msgstr "local_auth_policy (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4213
msgid ""
"Local authentication methods policy. Some backends (i.e. LDAP, proxy "
"provider) only support a password based authentication, while others can "
"handle PKINIT based Smartcard authentication (AD, IPA), two-factor "
"authentication (IPA), or other methods against a central instance. By "
"default in such cases authentication is only performed with the methods "
"supported by the backend. With this option additional methods can be enabled "
"which are evaluated and checked locally."
msgstr ""
"Lokālo autentifikācijas metožu politika. Dažas aizmugursistēmas (t. i., "
"LDAP, starpniekservera nodrošinātājs) atbalsta tikai uz parolēm balstītu "
"autentifikāciju, bet citas var apstrādāt uz PKINIT balstītu viedkaršu "
"autentifikāciju (AD, IPA), divfaktoru autentifikāciju (IPA) vai citas "
"metodes pret centrālu instanci. Pēc noklusējuma šādos gadījumos "
"autentifikācija tiek veikta tikai ar aizmugursistēmas atbalstītajām metodēm. "
"Ar šo opciju var iespējot papildu metodes, kas tiek izvērtētas un "
"pārbaudītas lokāli."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4225
msgid ""
"There are three possible values for this option: match, only, enable. "
"<quote>match</quote> is used to match offline and online states for Kerberos "
"methods. <quote>only</quote> ignores the online methods and only offer the "
"local ones. enable allows explicitly defining the methods for local "
"authentication. As an example, <quote>enable:passkey</quote>, only enables "
"passkey for local authentication. Multiple enable values should be comma-"
"separated, such as <quote>enable:passkey, enable:smartcard</quote>"
msgstr ""
"Šai opcijai ir trīs iespējamās vērtības: match, only, enable. <quote>match</"
"quote> izmanto, lai saskaņotu bezsaistes un tiešsaistes stāvokļus Kerberos "
"metodēm. <quote>only</quote> ignorē tiešsaistes metodes un piedāvā tikai "
"lokālās. enable ļauj skaidri definēt lokālās autentifikācijas metodes. "
"Piemēram, <quote>enable:passkey</quote> lokālai autentifikācijai iespējo "
"tikai piekļuves atslēgu. Vairākas enable vērtības jāatdala ar komatiem, "
"piemēram, <quote>enable:passkey, enable:smartcard</quote>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4238
msgid ""
"The following table shows which authentication methods, if configured "
"properly, are currently enabled or disabled for each backend, with the "
"default local_auth_policy: <quote>match</quote>"
msgstr ""
"Tālāk dotā tabula parāda, kuras autentifikācijas metodes, ja pareizi "
"konfigurētas, katrai aizmugursistēmai pašlaik ir iespējotas vai atspējotas "
"ar noklusējuma local_auth_policy: <quote>match</quote>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><informaltable><tgroup><thead><row><entry>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4251
msgid "local_auth_policy = match (default)"
msgstr "local_auth_policy = match (noklusējums)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><informaltable><tgroup><thead><row><entry>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4252
msgid "Passkey"
msgstr "Piekļuves atslēga"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><informaltable><tgroup><thead><row><entry>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4253
msgid "Smartcard"
msgstr "Viedkarte"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4256 sssd-ldap.5.xml:228
msgid "IPA"
msgstr "IPA"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><informaltable><tgroup><tbody><row><entry><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4256 sssd.conf.5.xml:4257 sssd.conf.5.xml:4260
msgid "enabled"
msgstr "enabled"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4259 sssd-ldap.5.xml:233
msgid "AD"
msgstr "AD"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><informaltable><tgroup><tbody><row><entry><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4259 sssd.conf.5.xml:4262 sssd.conf.5.xml:4263
msgid "disabled"
msgstr "disabled"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><informaltable><tgroup><tbody><row><entry>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4262
msgid "LDAP"
msgstr "LDAP"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4267
msgid ""
"Please note that if local Smartcard authentication is enabled and a "
"Smartcard is present, Smartcard authentication will be preferred over the "
"authentication methods supported by the backend.  I.e. there will be a PIN "
"prompt instead of e.g. a password prompt."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā: ja ir iespējota lokālā viedkaršu autentifikācija un "
"viedkarte ir klāt, viedkaršu autentifikācijai tiks dota priekšroka pār "
"aizmugursistēmas atbalstītajām autentifikācijas metodēm.  T. i., tiks "
"prasīts PIN, nevis, piem., parole."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4279
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[domain/shadowutils]\n"
"id_provider = proxy\n"
"proxy_lib_name = files\n"
"auth_provider = none\n"
"local_auth_policy = only\n"
msgstr ""
"[domain/shadowutils]\n"
"id_provider = proxy\n"
"proxy_lib_name = files\n"
"auth_provider = none\n"
"local_auth_policy = only\n"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4275
msgid ""
"The following configuration example allows local users to authenticate "
"locally using any enabled method (i.e. smartcard, passkey).  <placeholder "
"type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Tālāk dotais konfigurācijas piemērs ļauj lokālajiem lietotājiem "
"autentificēties lokāli, izmantojot jebkuru iespējotu metodi (t. i., "
"viedkarti, piekļuves atslēgu).  <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" "
"id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4287
msgid "Default: match"
msgstr "Noklusējums: match"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4292
msgid "auto_private_groups (string)"
msgstr "auto_private_groups (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4298
msgid "true"
msgstr "true"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4301
msgid ""
"Create user's private group unconditionally from user's UID number.  The GID "
"number is ignored in this case."
msgstr ""
"Bez nosacījumiem izveidot lietotāja privāto grupu no lietotāja UID numura.  "
"GID numurs šajā gadījumā tiek ignorēts."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4305
msgid ""
"NOTE: Because the GID number and the user private group are inferred from "
"the UID number, it is not supported to have multiple entries with the same "
"UID or GID number with this option. In other words, enabling this option "
"enforces uniqueness across the ID space."
msgstr ""
"PIEZĪME: Tā kā GID numurs un lietotāja privātā grupa tiek atvasināti no UID "
"numura, ar šo opciju netiek atbalstīti vairāki ieraksti ar vienu un to pašu "
"UID vai GID numuru. Citiem vārdiem, šīs opcijas iespējošana piespiež "
"unikalitāti visā ID telpā."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4314
msgid "false"
msgstr "false"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4317
msgid ""
"Always use the user's primary GID number. The GID number must refer to a "
"group object in the LDAP database."
msgstr ""
"Vienmēr izmantot lietotāja primārā GID numuru. GID numuram jāatsaucas uz "
"grupas objektu LDAP datubāzē."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4323
msgid "hybrid"
msgstr "hybrid"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4326
msgid ""
"A primary group is autogenerated for user entries whose UID and GID numbers "
"have the same value and at the same time the GID number does not correspond "
"to a real group object in LDAP.  If the values are the same, but the primary "
"GID in the user entry is also used by a group object, the primary GID of the "
"user resolves to that group object."
msgstr ""
"Primārā grupa tiek automātiski ģenerēta lietotāju ierakstiem, kuru UID un "
"GID numuriem ir vienāda vērtība un tajā pašā laikā GID numurs neatbilst "
"reālam grupas objektam LDAP.  Ja vērtības ir vienādas, bet lietotāja "
"ieraksta primāro GID izmanto arī grupas objekts, lietotāja primārais GID "
"tiek atrisināts uz šo grupas objektu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4339
msgid ""
"If the UID and GID of a user are different, then the GID must correspond to "
"a group entry, otherwise the GID is simply not resolvable."
msgstr ""
"Ja lietotāja UID un GID atšķiras, GID jāatbilst grupas ierakstam, citādi GID "
"vienkārši nav atrisināms."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4346
msgid ""
"This feature is useful for environments that wish to stop maintaining a "
"separate group objects for the user private groups, but also wish to retain "
"the existing user private groups."
msgstr ""
"Šis līdzeklis noder vidēs, kurās vēlas pārtraukt atsevišķu grupas objektu "
"uzturēšanu lietotāju privātajām grupām, bet vēlas saglabāt esošās lietotāju "
"privātās grupas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4295
msgid ""
"This option takes any of three available values: <placeholder "
"type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija pieņem jebkuru no trim pieejamajām vērtībām: <placeholder "
"type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4358
msgid ""
"For the LDAP based id providers (LDAP, IPA and AD) the default for the "
"configured domain is typically False because the sources have the concept of "
"a primary group.  <phrase condition=\"with_idp_provider\">The IdP id "
"provider is using True because IdPs typically do not have primary groups.</"
"phrase>"
msgstr ""
"Uz LDAP balstītajiem id nodrošinātājiem (LDAP, IPA un AD) konfigurētā domēna "
"noklusējums parasti ir False, jo avotos ir primārās grupas jēdziens.  "
"<phrase condition=\"with_idp_provider\">IdP id nodrošinātājs izmanto True, "
"jo IdP parasti nav primāro grupu.</phrase>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4367
msgid ""
"For subdomains, the default value is False for subdomains that use assigned "
"POSIX IDs and True for subdomains that use automatic ID-mapping."
msgstr ""
"Apakšdomēniem noklusējuma vērtība ir False apakšdomēniem, kas izmanto "
"piešķirtus POSIX ID, un True apakšdomēniem, kas izmanto automātisku ID "
"kartēšanu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4375
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[domain/forest.domain/sub.domain]\n"
"auto_private_groups = false\n"
msgstr ""
"[domain/forest.domain/sub.domain]\n"
"auto_private_groups = false\n"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4381
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[domain/forest.domain]\n"
"subdomain_inherit = auto_private_groups\n"
"auto_private_groups = false\n"
msgstr ""
"[domain/forest.domain]\n"
"subdomain_inherit = auto_private_groups\n"
"auto_private_groups = false\n"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4372
msgid ""
"The value of auto_private_groups can either be set per subdomains in a "
"subsection, for example: <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/> or "
"globally for all subdomains in the main domain section using the "
"subdomain_inherit option: <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"1\"/>"
msgstr ""
"auto_private_groups vērtību var iestatīt vai nu katram apakšdomēnam "
"apakšsadaļā, piemēram: <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/>, vai "
"globāli visiem apakšdomēniem galvenā domēna sadaļā, izmantojot opciju "
"subdomain_inherit: <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"1\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:2636
msgid ""
"These configuration options can be present in a domain configuration "
"section, that is, in a section called <quote>[domain/<replaceable>NAME</"
"replaceable>]</quote> <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Šīs konfigurācijas opcijas var būt domēna konfigurācijas sadaļā, t. i., "
"sadaļā ar nosaukumu <quote>[domain/<replaceable>NAME</replaceable>]</quote> "
"<placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4396
msgid "proxy_pam_target (string)"
msgstr "proxy_pam_target (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4399
msgid "The proxy target PAM proxies to."
msgstr "Starpniekservera mērķis, uz kuru PAM pārsūta."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4402
msgid ""
"Default: not set by default, you have to take an existing pam configuration "
"or create a new one and add the service name here. As an alternative you can "
"enable local authentication with the local_auth_policy option."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: pēc noklusējuma nav iestatīts; jāizmanto esoša pam "
"konfigurācija vai jāizveido jauna un šeit jāpievieno pakalpojuma nosaukums. "
"Alternatīvi var iespējot lokālo autentifikāciju ar opciju local_auth_policy."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4412
msgid "proxy_lib_name (string)"
msgstr "proxy_lib_name (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4415
msgid ""
"The name of the NSS library to use in proxy domains. The NSS functions "
"searched for in the library are in the form of _nss_$(libName)_$(function), "
"for example _nss_files_getpwent."
msgstr ""
"Starpniekdomēnos izmantojamās NSS bibliotēkas nosaukums. Bibliotēkā meklētās "
"NSS funkcijas ir formā _nss_$(libName)_$(function), piemēram, "
"_nss_files_getpwent."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4425
msgid "proxy_resolver_lib_name (string)"
msgstr "proxy_resolver_lib_name (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4428
msgid ""
"The name of the NSS library to use for hosts and networks lookups in proxy "
"domains. The NSS functions searched for in the library are in the form of "
"_nss_$(libName)_$(function), for example _nss_dns_gethostbyname2_r."
msgstr ""
"Starpniekdomēnos resursdatoru un tīklu uzmeklēšanai izmantojamās NSS "
"bibliotēkas nosaukums. Bibliotēkā meklētās NSS funkcijas ir formā _nss_$"
"(libName)_$(function), piemēram, _nss_dns_gethostbyname2_r."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4439
msgid "proxy_fast_alias (boolean)"
msgstr "proxy_fast_alias (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4442
msgid ""
"When a user or group is looked up by name in the proxy provider, a second "
"lookup by ID is performed to \"canonicalize\" the name in case the requested "
"name was an alias. Setting this option to true would cause the SSSD to "
"perform the ID lookup from cache for performance reasons."
msgstr ""
"Kad starpniekservera nodrošinātājā lietotājs vai grupa tiek uzmeklēta pēc "
"nosaukuma, tiek veikta otra uzmeklēšana pēc ID, lai \"kanonizētu\" nosaukumu "
"gadījumā, ja pieprasītais nosaukums bija aizstājvārds. Iestatot šo opciju uz "
"true, SSSD veiktspējas apsvērumu dēļ veiks ID uzmeklēšanu no kešatmiņas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4456
msgid "proxy_max_children (integer)"
msgstr "proxy_max_children (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4459
msgid ""
"This option specifies the number of pre-forked proxy children. It is useful "
"for high-load SSSD environments where sssd may run out of available child "
"slots, which would cause some issues due to the requests being queued."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija norāda iepriekš sazaroto starpniekservera bērnprocesu skaitu. Tā "
"noder lielas slodzes SSSD vidēs, kur sssd var pietrūkt pieejamo bērnprocesu "
"slotu, kas pieprasījumu rindošanas dēļ radītu zināmas problēmas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4392
msgid ""
"Options valid for proxy domains.  <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" "
"id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Starpniekdomēniem derīgās opcijas.  <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" "
"id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4475
msgid "Application domains"
msgstr "Lietotņu domēni"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4477
msgid ""
"SSSD, with its D-Bus interface (see <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd-ifp</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</manvolnum> </citerefentry>) is appealing to "
"applications as a gateway to an LDAP directory where users and groups are "
"stored. However, contrary to the traditional SSSD deployment where all users "
"and groups either have POSIX attributes or those attributes can be inferred "
"from the Windows SIDs, in many cases the users and groups in the application "
"support scenario have no POSIX attributes.  Instead of setting a "
"<quote>[domain/<replaceable>NAME</replaceable>]</quote> section, the "
"administrator can set up an <quote>[application/<replaceable>NAME</"
"replaceable>]</quote> section that internally represents a domain with type "
"<quote>application</quote> optionally inherits settings from a tradition "
"SSSD domain."
msgstr ""
"SSSD ar savu D-Bus saskarni (skatiet <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd-ifp</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</manvolnum> </citerefentry>) ir pievilcīgs "
"lietotnēm kā vārteja uz LDAP direktoriju, kurā glabājas lietotāji un grupas. "
"Tomēr atšķirībā no tradicionālā SSSD izvietojuma, kur visiem lietotājiem un "
"grupām ir POSIX atribūti vai tos var atvasināt no Windows SID, lietotņu "
"atbalsta scenārijā lietotājiem un grupām bieži nav POSIX atribūtu.  Tā "
"vietā, lai iestatītu sadaļu <quote>[domain/<replaceable>NAME</replaceable>]</"
"quote>, administrators var iestatīt sadaļu <quote>[application/<replaceable>"
"NAME</replaceable>]</quote>, kas iekšēji attēlo domēnu ar tipu <quote>"
"application</quote> un pēc izvēles manto iestatījumus no tradicionāla SSSD "
"domēna."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4497
msgid ""
"Please note that the application domain must still be explicitly enabled in "
"the <quote>domains</quote> parameter so that the lookup order between the "
"application domain and its POSIX sibling domain is set correctly."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka lietotnes domēns joprojām skaidri jāiespējo parametrā "
"<quote>domains</quote>, lai uzmeklēšanas secība starp lietotnes domēnu un tā "
"POSIX radniecīgo domēnu būtu iestatīta pareizi."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4503
msgid "Application domain parameters"
msgstr "Lietotnes domēna parametri"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4505
msgid "inherit_from (string)"
msgstr "inherit_from (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4508
msgid ""
"The SSSD POSIX-type domain the application domain inherits all settings "
"from. The application domain can moreover add its own settings to the "
"application settings that augment or override the <quote>sibling</quote> "
"domain settings."
msgstr ""
"SSSD POSIX tipa domēns, no kura lietotnes domēns manto visus iestatījumus. "
"Turklāt lietotnes domēns var lietotnes iestatījumiem pievienot savus "
"iestatījumus, kas papildina vai aizstāj <quote>radniecīgā</quote> domēna "
"iestatījumus."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4522
msgid ""
"The following example illustrates the use of an application domain. In this "
"setup, the POSIX domain is connected to an LDAP server and is used by the OS "
"through the NSS responder. In addition, the application domain also requests "
"the telephoneNumber attribute, stores it as the phone attribute in the cache "
"and makes the phone attribute reachable through the D-Bus interface."
msgstr ""
"Tālāk dotais piemērs ilustrē lietotnes domēna izmantošanu. Šajā iestatījumā "
"POSIX domēns ir savienots ar LDAP serveri, un to OS izmanto caur NSS "
"atbildētāju. Turklāt lietotnes domēns pieprasa arī atribūtu telephoneNumber, "
"saglabā to kešatmiņā kā atribūtu phone un padara atribūtu phone sasniedzamu "
"caur D-Bus saskarni."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4530
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[sssd]\n"
"domains = appdom, posixdom\n"
"\n"
"[ifp]\n"
"user_attributes = +phone\n"
"\n"
"[domain/posixdom]\n"
"id_provider = ldap\n"
"ldap_uri = ldap://ldap.example.com\n"
"ldap_search_base = dc=example,dc=com\n"
"\n"
"[application/appdom]\n"
"inherit_from = posixdom\n"
"ldap_user_extra_attrs = phone:telephoneNumber\n"
msgstr ""
"[sssd]\n"
"domains = appdom, posixdom\n"
"\n"
"[ifp]\n"
"user_attributes = +phone\n"
"\n"
"[domain/posixdom]\n"
"id_provider = ldap\n"
"ldap_uri = ldap://ldap.example.com\n"
"ldap_search_base = dc=example,dc=com\n"
"\n"
"[application/appdom]\n"
"inherit_from = posixdom\n"
"ldap_user_extra_attrs = phone:telephoneNumber\n"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4550
msgid "TRUSTED DOMAIN SECTION"
msgstr "UZTICAMĀ DOMĒNA SADAĻA"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4552
msgid ""
"Some options used in the domain section can also be used in the trusted "
"domain section, that is, in a section called <quote>[domain/"
"<replaceable>DOMAIN_NAME</replaceable>/<replaceable>TRUSTED_DOMAIN_NAME</"
"replaceable>]</quote>.  Where DOMAIN_NAME is the actual joined-to base "
"domain. Please refer to examples below for explanation.  Currently supported "
"options in the trusted domain section are:"
msgstr ""
"Dažas domēna sadaļā izmantotās opcijas var izmantot arī uzticamā domēna "
"sadaļā, t. i., sadaļā ar nosaukumu <quote>[domain/<replaceable>DOMAIN_NAME</"
"replaceable>/<replaceable>TRUSTED_DOMAIN_NAME</replaceable>]</quote>.  Kur "
"DOMAIN_NAME ir faktiskais bāzes domēns, kuram pievienots. Paskaidrojumu "
"skatiet tālāk dotajos piemēros.  Uzticamā domēna sadaļā pašlaik tiek "
"atbalstītas šādas opcijas:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4559
msgid "ldap_search_base,"
msgstr "ldap_search_base,"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4560
msgid "ldap_user_search_base,"
msgstr "ldap_user_search_base,"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4561
msgid "ldap_group_search_base,"
msgstr "ldap_group_search_base,"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4562
msgid "ldap_netgroup_search_base,"
msgstr "ldap_netgroup_search_base,"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4563
msgid "ldap_service_search_base,"
msgstr "ldap_service_search_base,"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4564
msgid "ldap_sasl_mech,"
msgstr "ldap_sasl_mech,"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4565
msgid "ad_server,"
msgstr "ad_server,"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4566
msgid "ad_backup_server,"
msgstr "ad_backup_server,"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4567
msgid "ad_site,"
msgstr "ad_site,"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><refsect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4568 sssd-ipa.5.xml:929
msgid "use_fully_qualified_names"
msgstr "use_fully_qualified_names"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4569
msgid "pam_gssapi_services"
msgstr "pam_gssapi_services"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4570
msgid "pam_gssapi_check_upn"
msgstr "pam_gssapi_check_upn"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4572
msgid ""
"For more details about these options see their individual description in the "
"manual page."
msgstr ""
"Sīkāku informāciju par šīm opcijām skatiet to atsevišķajos aprakstos "
"rokasgrāmatas lapā."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4578
msgid "CERTIFICATE MAPPING SECTION"
msgstr "SERTIFIKĀTU KARTĒŠANAS SADAĻA"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4580
msgid ""
"To allow authentication with Smartcards and certificates SSSD must be able "
"to map certificates to users. This can be done by adding the full "
"certificate to the LDAP object of the user or to a local override. While "
"using the full certificate is required to use the Smartcard authentication "
"feature of SSH (see <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sss_ssh_authorizedkeys</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>8</manvolnum> </citerefentry> for details) it "
"might be cumbersome or not even possible to do this for the general case "
"where local services use PAM for authentication."
msgstr ""
"Lai atļautu autentifikāciju ar viedkartēm un sertifikātiem, SSSD jāspēj "
"kartēt sertifikātus uz lietotājiem. To var izdarīt, pievienojot pilno "
"sertifikātu lietotāja LDAP objektam vai lokālam pārdefinējumam. Lai gan "
"pilnais sertifikāts ir nepieciešams SSH viedkaršu autentifikācijas līdzekļa "
"izmantošanai (sīkāk skatiet <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>"
"sss_ssh_authorizedkeys</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>8</manvolnum> </"
"citerefentry>), vispārējā gadījumā, kad lokālie pakalpojumi autentifikācijai "
"izmanto PAM, tas var būt apgrūtinoši vai pat neiespējami."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4594
msgid ""
"To make the mapping more flexible mapping and matching rules were added to "
"SSSD (see <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sss-certmap</refentrytitle> "
"<manvolnum>5</manvolnum> </citerefentry> for details)."
msgstr ""
"Lai kartēšana būtu elastīgāka, SSSD tika pievienotas kartēšanas un "
"atbilstības kārtulas (sīkāk skatiet <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sss-"
"certmap</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</manvolnum> </citerefentry>)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4603
msgid ""
"A mapping and matching rule can be added to the SSSD configuration in a "
"section on its own with a name like <quote>[certmap/"
"<replaceable>DOMAIN_NAME</replaceable>/<replaceable>RULE_NAME</"
"replaceable>]</quote>.  In this section the following options are allowed:"
msgstr ""
"Kartēšanas un atbilstības kārtulu var pievienot SSSD konfigurācijai "
"atsevišķā sadaļā ar nosaukumu, piemēram, <quote>[certmap/<replaceable>"
"DOMAIN_NAME</replaceable>/<replaceable>RULE_NAME</replaceable>]</quote>.  "
"Šajā sadaļā atļautas šādas opcijas:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4610
msgid "matchrule (string)"
msgstr "matchrule (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4613
msgid ""
"Only certificates from the Smartcard which matches this rule will be "
"processed, all others are ignored."
msgstr ""
"Tiks apstrādāti tikai tie viedkartes sertifikāti, kas atbilst šai kārtulai; "
"visi pārējie tiek ignorēti."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4617
msgid ""
"Default: KRB5:&lt;EKU&gt;clientAuth, i.e. only certificates which have the "
"Extended Key Usage <quote>clientAuth</quote>"
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: KRB5:&lt;EKU&gt;clientAuth, t. i., tikai sertifikāti ar "
"paplašināto atslēgas lietojumu <quote>clientAuth</quote>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4624
msgid "maprule (string)"
msgstr "maprule (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4627
msgid "Defines how the user is found for a given certificate."
msgstr "Definē, kā norādītajam sertifikātam tiek atrasts lietotājs."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4633
msgid ""
"LDAP:(userCertificate;binary={cert!bin})  for LDAP based providers like "
"<quote>ldap</quote>, <quote>AD</quote> or <quote>ipa</quote>."
msgstr ""
"LDAP:(userCertificate;binary={cert!bin})  uz LDAP balstītiem "
"nodrošinātājiem, piemēram, <quote>ldap</quote>, <quote>AD</quote> vai <quote>"
"ipa</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4639
msgid ""
"If maprule is not set and provider is <quote>proxy</quote>, the RULE_NAME "
"name is assumed to be the name of the matching user."
msgstr ""
"Ja maprule nav iestatīts un nodrošinātājs ir <quote>proxy</quote>, tiek "
"pieņemts, ka RULE_NAME ir atbilstošā lietotāja vārds."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4652
msgid ""
"Comma separated list of domain names the rule should be applied. By default "
"a rule is only valid in the domain configured in sssd.conf. If the provider "
"supports subdomains this option can be used to add the rule to subdomains as "
"well."
msgstr ""
"Ar komatiem atdalīts domēnu nosaukumu saraksts, kuros jāpiemēro kārtula. Pēc "
"noklusējuma kārtula ir derīga tikai sssd.conf konfigurētajā domēnā. Ja "
"nodrošinātājs atbalsta apakšdomēnus, ar šo opciju kārtulu var pievienot arī "
"apakšdomēniem."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4659
msgid "Default: the configured domain in sssd.conf"
msgstr "Noklusējums: sssd.conf konfigurētais domēns"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4664
msgid "priority (integer)"
msgstr "priority (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4667
msgid ""
"Unsigned integer value defining the priority of the rule. The higher the "
"number the lower the priority.  <quote>0</quote> stands for the highest "
"priority while <quote>4294967295</quote> is the lowest."
msgstr ""
"Bezzīmes vesela skaitļa vērtība, kas definē kārtulas prioritāti. Jo lielāks "
"skaitlis, jo zemāka prioritāte.  <quote>0</quote> apzīmē augstāko "
"prioritāti, bet <quote>4294967295</quote> — zemāko."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4673
msgid "Default: the lowest priority"
msgstr "Noklusējums: zemākā prioritāte"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4681
msgid "PROMPTING CONFIGURATION SECTION"
msgstr "UZVEDŅU KONFIGURĀCIJAS SADAĻA"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4683
msgid ""
"If a special file (<filename>/var/lib/sss/pubconf/pam_preauth_available</"
"filename>)  exists SSSD's PAM module pam_sss will ask SSSD to figure out "
"which authentication methods are available for the user trying to log in.  "
"Based on the results pam_sss will prompt the user for appropriate "
"credentials."
msgstr ""
"Ja eksistē īpašs fails (<filename>/var/lib/sss/pubconf/"
"pam_preauth_available</filename>), SSSD PAM modulis pam_sss lūgs SSSD "
"noskaidrot, kuras autentifikācijas metodes ir pieejamas lietotājam, kas "
"mēģina pieteikties.  Pamatojoties uz rezultātiem, pam_sss vaicās lietotājam "
"atbilstošos akreditācijas datus."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4691
msgid ""
"With the growing number of authentication methods and the possibility that "
"there are multiple ones for a single user the heuristic used by pam_sss to "
"select the prompting might not be suitable for all use cases. The following "
"options should provide a better flexibility here."
msgstr ""
"Pieaugot autentifikācijas metožu skaitam un pastāvot iespējai, ka vienam "
"lietotājam ir vairākas metodes, pam_sss izmantotā heiristika uzvedņu izvēlei "
"var nebūt piemērota visiem lietojuma gadījumiem. Tālāk minētajām opcijām "
"šeit jānodrošina lielāka elastība."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4703
msgid "[prompting/password]"
msgstr "[prompting/password]"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4706
msgid "password_prompt"
msgstr "password_prompt"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4707
msgid "to change the string of the password prompt"
msgstr "lai mainītu paroles uzvednes virkni"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4705
msgid ""
"to configure password prompting, allowed options are: <placeholder "
"type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"lai konfigurētu paroles uzvedni; atļautās opcijas: <placeholder "
"type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4715
msgid "[prompting/2fa]"
msgstr "[prompting/2fa]"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4719
msgid "first_prompt"
msgstr "first_prompt"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4720
msgid "to change the string of the prompt for the first factor"
msgstr "lai mainītu pirmā faktora uzvednes virkni"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4723
msgid "second_prompt"
msgstr "second_prompt"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4724
msgid "to change the string of the prompt for the second factor"
msgstr "lai mainītu otrā faktora uzvednes virkni"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4727
msgid "single_prompt"
msgstr "single_prompt"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4728
msgid ""
"boolean value, if True there will be only a single prompt using the value of "
"first_prompt where it is expected that both factors are entered as a single "
"string. Please note that both factors have to be entered here, even if the "
"second factor is optional."
msgstr ""
"Būla vērtība; ja True, būs tikai viena uzvedne, kurā izmanto first_prompt "
"vērtību un kurā paredzēts abus faktorus ievadīt kā vienu virkni. Lūdzu, "
"ņemiet vērā, ka šeit jāievada abi faktori, pat ja otrais faktors nav "
"obligāts."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4717
msgid ""
"to configure two-factor authentication prompting, allowed options are: "
"<placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/> If the second factor is "
"optional and it should be possible to log in either only with the password "
"or with both factors two-step prompting has to be used."
msgstr ""
"lai konfigurētu divfaktoru autentifikācijas uzvedni; atļautās opcijas: "
"<placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/> Ja otrais faktors nav obligāts "
"un jābūt iespējai pieteikties vai nu tikai ar paroli, vai ar abiem "
"faktoriem, jāizmanto divu soļu uzvedne."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4741
msgid ""
"Some clients, such as SSH with 'PasswordAuthentication yes', generate their "
"own prompts and do not use prompts provided by SSSD or other PAM modules. "
"Additionally, for SSH with PasswordAuthentication, if two-factor "
"authentication is available, SSSD expects that the credentials entered by "
"the user at the SSH password prompt will always be the two factors in a "
"single string, even if two-factor authentication is optional."
msgstr ""
"Daži klienti, piemēram, SSH ar „PasswordAuthentication yes”, ģenerē paši "
"savas uzvednes un neizmanto SSSD vai citu PAM moduļu nodrošinātās uzvednes. "
"Turklāt SSH ar PasswordAuthentication gadījumā, ja ir pieejama divfaktoru "
"autentifikācija, SSSD sagaida, ka lietotāja SSH paroles uzvednē ievadītie "
"akreditācijas dati vienmēr būs abi faktori vienā virknē, pat ja divfaktoru "
"autentifikācija nav obligāta."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4756
msgid "[prompting/passkey]"
msgstr "[prompting/passkey]"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4762 sssd.conf.5.xml:4806 sssd-ad.5.xml:1027
msgid "interactive"
msgstr "interactive"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4764
msgid ""
"boolean value, if True prompt a message and wait before testing the presence "
"of a passkey device.  Recommended if your device doesn’t have a tactile "
"trigger."
msgstr ""
"Būla vērtība; ja True, parādīt ziņojumu un gaidīt pirms piekļuves atslēgas "
"ierīces klātbūtnes pārbaudes.  Ieteicams, ja jūsu ierīcei nav taustes slēdža."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
