msgstr "lai mainītu pieskāriena uzvednes ziņojumu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4758
msgid ""
"to configure passkey authentication prompting, allowed options are: "
"<placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"lai konfigurētu piekļuves atslēgas autentifikācijas uzvedni; atļautās "
"opcijas: <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4800
msgid "[prompting/oauth2]"
msgstr "[prompting/oauth2]"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4808
msgid ""
"boolean value, if True prompt a message after asking the user to "
"authenticate, and wait before requesting the access token."
msgstr ""
"Būla vērtība; ja True, pēc lūguma lietotājam autentificēties parādīt "
"ziņojumu un gaidīt pirms piekļuves marķiera pieprasīšanas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4812
msgid ""
"If False, make sure to set the <quote>idp_request_timeout</quote> "
"sufficiently high, to give the user time to authenticate."
msgstr ""
"Ja False, pārliecinieties, ka <quote>idp_request_timeout</quote> ir "
"iestatīts pietiekami liels, lai lietotājam būtu laiks autentificēties."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4802
msgid ""
"to configure OAuth2 authentication prompting, allowed options are: "
"<placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"lai konfigurētu OAuth2 autentifikācijas uzvedni; atļautās opcijas: "
"<placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4835
msgid "[prompting/cert_auth]"
msgstr "[prompting/cert_auth]"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4841
msgid "pin_prompt"
msgstr "pin_prompt"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4843
msgid ""
"to change the message which asks the user to enter the PIN at the computer "
"keyboard. At the end of the message the token name is printed."
msgstr ""
"lai mainītu ziņojumu, kas lūdz lietotāju ievadīt PIN ar datora tastatūru. "
"Ziņojuma beigās tiek izvadīts marķiera nosaukums."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4851
msgid "keypad_prompt"
msgstr "keypad_prompt"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4853
msgid ""
"to change the message which asks the user to enter the PIN at keypad of the "
"Smartcard reader. At the end of the message the token name is printed."
msgstr ""
"lai mainītu ziņojumu, kas lūdz lietotāju ievadīt PIN ar viedkaršu lasītāja "
"tastatūru. Ziņojuma beigās tiek izvadīts marķiera nosaukums."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4861
msgid "user_name_hint"
msgstr "user_name_hint"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4863
msgid ""
"boolean value, if True ask for a user name if no name was given before and "
"the found certificate can be mapped to more than one user."
msgstr ""
"Būla vērtība; ja True, vaicāt lietotājvārdu, ja vārds iepriekš netika "
"norādīts un atrasto sertifikātu var kartēt uz vairāk nekā vienu lietotāju."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4837
msgid ""
"to configure Smartcard authentication prompting, allowed options are: "
"<placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"lai konfigurētu viedkaršu autentifikācijas uzvedni; atļautās opcijas: "
"<placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4698
msgid ""
"Each supported authentication method has its own configuration subsection "
"under <quote>[prompting/...]</quote>. Currently there are: <placeholder "
"type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/> <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"1\"/"
"> <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"2\"/> <placeholder "
"type=\"variablelist\" id=\"3\"/> <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"4\"/"
">"
msgstr ""
"Katrai atbalstītajai autentifikācijas metodei ir sava konfigurācijas "
"apakšsadaļa zem <quote>[prompting/...]</quote>. Pašlaik ir: <placeholder "
"type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/> <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" "
"id=\"1\"/> <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"2\"/> <placeholder "
"type=\"variablelist\" id=\"3\"/> <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" "
"id=\"4\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4879
msgid ""
"It is possible to add a subsection for specific PAM services, e.g. "
"<quote>[prompting/password/sshd]</quote> to individual change the prompting "
"for this service."
msgstr ""
"Konkrētiem PAM pakalpojumiem var pievienot apakšsadaļu, piem., <quote>"
"[prompting/password/sshd]</quote>, lai šim pakalpojumam atsevišķi mainītu "
"uzvedni."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4886 pam_sss_gss.8.xml:157 idmap_sss.8.xml:43
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr "PIEMĒRI"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4892
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[sssd]\n"
"domains = LDAP\n"
"services = nss, pam\n"
"\n"
"[nss]\n"
"filter_groups = root\n"
"filter_users = root\n"
"\n"
"[pam]\n"
"\n"
"[domain/LDAP]\n"
"id_provider = ldap\n"
"ldap_uri = ldap://ldap.example.com\n"
"ldap_search_base = dc=example,dc=com\n"
"\n"
"auth_provider = krb5\n"
"krb5_server = kerberos.example.com\n"
"krb5_realm = EXAMPLE.COM\n"
"cache_credentials = true\n"
"\n"
"min_id = 10000\n"
"max_id = 20000\n"
"enumerate = False\n"
msgstr ""
"[sssd]\n"
"domains = LDAP\n"
"services = nss, pam\n"
"\n"
"[nss]\n"
"filter_groups = root\n"
"filter_users = root\n"
"\n"
"[pam]\n"
"\n"
"[domain/LDAP]\n"
"id_provider = ldap\n"
"ldap_uri = ldap://ldap.example.com\n"
"ldap_search_base = dc=example,dc=com\n"
"\n"
"auth_provider = krb5\n"
"krb5_server = kerberos.example.com\n"
"krb5_realm = EXAMPLE.COM\n"
"cache_credentials = true\n"
"\n"
"min_id = 10000\n"
"max_id = 20000\n"
"enumerate = False\n"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4888
msgid ""
"1. The following example shows a typical SSSD config. It does not describe "
"configuration of the domains themselves - refer to documentation on "
"configuring domains for more details.  <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" "
"id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"1. Tālāk dotais piemērs parāda tipisku SSSD konfigurāciju. Tas neapraksta "
"pašu domēnu konfigurāciju — sīkāk skatiet dokumentāciju par domēnu "
"konfigurēšanu.  <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4924
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[domain/ipa.com/child.ad.com]\n"
"use_fully_qualified_names = false\n"
msgstr ""
"[domain/ipa.com/child.ad.com]\n"
"use_fully_qualified_names = false\n"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4918
msgid ""
"2. The following example shows configuration of IPA AD trust where the AD "
"forest consists of two domains in a parent-child structure.  Suppose IPA "
"domain (ipa.com) has trust with AD domain(ad.com).  ad.com has child domain "
"(child.ad.com). To enable shortnames in the child domain the following "
"configuration should be used.  <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/"
">"
msgstr ""
"2. Tālāk dotais piemērs parāda IPA AD uzticēšanās konfigurāciju, kurā AD "
"mežs sastāv no diviem domēniem vecāka-bērna struktūrā.  Pieņemsim, ka IPA "
"domēnam (ipa.com) ir uzticēšanās attiecības ar AD domēnu (ad.com).  ad.com "
"ir bērndomēns (child.ad.com). Lai bērndomēnā iespējotu īsos nosaukumus, "
"jāizmanto šāda konfigurācija.  <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" "
"id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><programlisting>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4935
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[certmap/my.domain/rule_name]\n"
"matchrule = &lt;ISSUER&gt;^CN=My-CA,DC=MY,DC=DOMAIN$\n"
"maprule = (userCertificate;binary={cert!bin})\n"
"domains = my.domain, your.domain\n"
"priority = 10\n"
msgstr ""
"[certmap/my.domain/rule_name]\n"
"matchrule = &lt;ISSUER&gt;^CN=My-CA,DC=MY,DC=DOMAIN$\n"
"maprule = (userCertificate;binary={cert!bin})\n"
"domains = my.domain, your.domain\n"
"priority = 10\n"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd.conf.5.xml:4929
msgid ""
"3. The following example shows the configuration of a certificate mapping "
"rule. It is valid for the configured domain <quote>my.domain</quote> and "
"additionally for the subdomains <quote>your.domain</quote> and uses the full "
"certificate in the search filter.  <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" "
"id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"3. Tālāk dotais piemērs parāda sertifikātu kartēšanas kārtulas "
"konfigurāciju. Tā ir derīga konfigurētajam domēnam <quote>my.domain</quote> "
"un papildus apakšdomēniem <quote>your.domain</quote>, un meklēšanas filtrā "
"izmanto pilno sertifikātu.  <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refnamediv><refname>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:10 sssd-ldap.5.xml:16
msgid "sssd-ldap"
msgstr "sssd-ldap"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refnamediv><refpurpose>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:17
msgid "SSSD LDAP provider"
msgstr "SSSD LDAP nodrošinātājs"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:21 pam_sss.8.xml:66 pam_sss_gss.8.xml:30
#: sssd_krb5_locator_plugin.8.xml:20 sssd-simple.5.xml:22 sss-certmap.5.xml:21
#: sssd-ipa.5.xml:21 sssd-ad.5.xml:21 sssd-sudo.5.xml:21 sssd-idp.5.xml:21
#: sssd.8.xml:29 sss_obfuscate.8.xml:29 sss_override.8.xml:30
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:21 sss_cache.8.xml:29 sss_debuglevel.8.xml:30
#: sss_seed.8.xml:31 sssd-ifp.5.xml:21 sss_ssh_authorizedkeys.1.xml:30
#: sss_ssh_knownhosts.1.xml:30 idmap_sss.8.xml:20 sssctl.8.xml:30
#: sssd-session-recording.5.xml:21 sssd-kcm.8.xml:21 sssd-systemtap.5.xml:21
#: sssd-ldap-attributes.5.xml:21 sssd_krb5_localauth_plugin.8.xml:20
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "APRAKSTS"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:23
msgid ""
"This manual page describes the configuration of LDAP domains for "
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>8</manvolnum> "
"</citerefentry>.  Refer to the <quote>FILE FORMAT</quote> section of the "
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd.conf</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry> manual page for detailed syntax information."
msgstr ""
"Šī rokasgrāmatas lapa apraksta LDAP domēnu konfigurāciju rīkam "
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>8</manvolnum> "
"</citerefentry>.  Detalizētu sintakses informāciju skatiet rokasgrāmatas "
"lapas <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd.conf</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry> sadaļā <quote>FAILA FORMĀTS</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:35
msgid "You can configure SSSD to use more than one LDAP domain."
msgstr "SSSD var konfigurēt izmantot vairāk nekā vienu LDAP domēnu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:38
msgid ""
"LDAP back end supports id, auth, access and chpass providers. If you want to "
"authenticate against an LDAP server either TLS/SSL or LDAPS is required. "
"<command>sssd</command> <emphasis>does not</emphasis> support authentication "
"over an unencrypted channel.  Even if the LDAP server is used only as an "
"identity provider, an encrypted channel is strongly recommended. Please "
"refer to the <quote>ldap_access_filter</quote> config option for more "
"information about using LDAP as an access provider."
msgstr ""
"LDAP aizmugursistēma atbalsta id, auth, access un chpass nodrošinātājus. Ja "
"vēlaties autentificēties pret LDAP serveri, nepieciešams TLS/SSL vai LDAPS. "
"<command>sssd</command> <emphasis>neatbalsta</emphasis> autentifikāciju pa "
"nešifrētu kanālu.  Pat ja LDAP serveri izmanto tikai kā identitātes "
"nodrošinātāju, šifrēts kanāls ir stingri ieteicams. Plašāku informāciju par "
"LDAP izmantošanu kā piekļuves nodrošinātāju skatiet konfigurācijas opcijā "
"<quote>ldap_access_filter</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:50 sssd-simple.5.xml:82 sssd-ipa.5.xml:82 sssd-ad.5.xml:130
#: sssd-idp.5.xml:54 sssd-krb5.5.xml:63 sssd-ifp.5.xml:60
#: sssd-session-recording.5.xml:58 sssd-kcm.8.xml:202
msgid "CONFIGURATION OPTIONS"
msgstr "KONFIGURĒŠANAS OPCIJAS"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:67
msgid "ldap_uri, ldap_backup_uri (string)"
msgstr "ldap_uri, ldap_backup_uri (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:70
msgid ""
"Specifies the comma-separated list of URIs of the LDAP servers to which SSSD "
"should connect in the order of preference. Refer to the <quote>FAILOVER</"
"quote> section for more information on failover and server redundancy.  If "
"neither option is specified, service discovery is enabled. For more "
"information, refer to the <quote>SERVICE DISCOVERY</quote> section."
msgstr ""
"Norāda ar komatiem atdalītu to LDAP serveru URI sarakstu, ar kuriem SSSD "
"jāsavienojas, vēlamības secībā. Plašāku informāciju par pārņemšanu un "
"serveru dublēšanu skatiet sadaļā <quote>FAILOVER</quote>.  Ja neviena opcija "
"nav norādīta, ir iespējota pakalpojumu atklāšana. Plašāku informāciju "
"skatiet sadaļā <quote>SERVICE DISCOVERY</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:77
msgid "The format of the URI must match the format defined in RFC 2732:"
msgstr "URI formātam jāatbilst RFC 2732 definētajam formātam:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:80
msgid "ldap[s]://&lt;host&gt;[:port]"
msgstr "ldap[s]://&lt;host&gt;[:port]"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:83
msgid ""
"For explicit IPv6 addresses, &lt;host&gt; must be enclosed in brackets []"
msgstr "Skaidri norādītām IPv6 adresēm &lt;host&gt; jābūt iekavās []"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:86
msgid "example: ldap://[fc00::126:25]:389"
msgstr "piemērs: ldap://[fc00::126:25]:389"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:92
msgid "ldap_chpass_uri, ldap_chpass_backup_uri (string)"
msgstr "ldap_chpass_uri, ldap_chpass_backup_uri (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:95
msgid ""
"Specifies the comma-separated list of URIs of the LDAP servers to which SSSD "
"should connect in the order of preference to change the password of a user. "
"Refer to the <quote>FAILOVER</quote> section for more information on "
"failover and server redundancy."
msgstr ""
"Norāda ar komatiem atdalītu to LDAP serveru URI sarakstu, ar kuriem SSSD "
"vēlamības secībā jāsavienojas, lai mainītu lietotāja paroli. Plašāku "
"informāciju par pārņemšanu un serveru dublēšanu skatiet sadaļā <quote>"
"FAILOVER</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:102
msgid "To enable service discovery ldap_chpass_dns_service_name must be set."
msgstr ""
"Lai iespējotu pakalpojumu atklāšanu, jāiestata ldap_chpass_dns_service_name."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:106
msgid "Default: empty, i.e. ldap_uri is used."
msgstr "Noklusējums: empty, i.e. ldap_uri is used."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:112
msgid "ldap_search_base (string)"
msgstr "ldap_search_base (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:115
msgid "The default base DN to use for performing LDAP user operations."
msgstr "Noklusējuma bāzes DN, ko izmantot LDAP lietotāju darbībām."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:119
msgid ""
"Starting with SSSD 1.7.0, SSSD supports multiple search bases using the "
"syntax:"
msgstr ""
"Sākot ar SSSD 1.7.0, SSSD atbalsta vairākas meklēšanas bāzes, izmantojot "
"sintaksi:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:123
msgid "search_base[?scope?[filter][?search_base?scope?[filter]]*]"
msgstr "search_base[?scope?[filter][?search_base?scope?[filter]]*]"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:126
msgid "The scope can be one of \"base\", \"onelevel\" or \"subtree\"."
msgstr "Tvērums var būt viens no \"base\", \"onelevel\" vai \"subtree\"."

#. type: Content of: <listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:129 include/ldap_search_bases.xml:18
msgid ""
"The filter must be a valid LDAP search filter as specified by http://"
"www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc2254.txt"
msgstr ""
"Filtram jābūt derīgam LDAP meklēšanas filtram, kā norādīts http://"
"www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc2254.txt"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:133 sssd-ad.5.xml:312 sss_override.8.xml:143
#: sss_override.8.xml:240 sssd-ldap-attributes.5.xml:453
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr "Examples:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:136
msgid ""
"ldap_search_base = dc=example,dc=com (which is equivalent to)  "
"ldap_search_base = dc=example,dc=com?subtree?"
msgstr ""
"ldap_search_base = dc=example,dc=com (kas ir līdzvērtīgi)  ldap_search_base "
"= dc=example,dc=com?subtree?"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:141
msgid ""
"ldap_search_base = cn=host_specific,dc=example,dc=com?subtree?"
"(host=thishost)?dc=example.com?subtree?"
msgstr ""
"ldap_search_base = cn=host_specific,dc=example,dc=com?subtree?(host=thishost)"
"?dc=example.com?subtree?"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:144
msgid ""
"Note: It is unsupported to have multiple search bases which reference "
"identically-named objects (for example, groups with the same name in two "
"different search bases). This will lead to unpredictable behavior on client "
"machines."
msgstr ""
"Piezīme: vairākas meklēšanas bāzes, kas atsaucas uz vienādi nosauktiem "
"objektiem (piemēram, grupām ar vienādu nosaukumu divās dažādās meklēšanas "
"bāzēs), netiek atbalstītas. Tas klientu datoros izraisīs neparedzamu rīcību."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:151
msgid ""
"Default: If not set, the value of the defaultNamingContext or namingContexts "
"attribute from the RootDSE of the LDAP server is used. If "
"defaultNamingContext does not exist or has an empty value namingContexts is "
"used.  The namingContexts attribute must have a single value with the DN of "
"the search base of the LDAP server to make this work. Multiple values are "
"not supported."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: ja nav iestatīts, tiek izmantota LDAP servera RootDSE atribūta "
"defaultNamingContext vai namingContexts vērtība. Ja defaultNamingContext "
"neeksistē vai tam ir tukša vērtība, tiek izmantots namingContexts.  Lai tas "
"darbotos, atribūtam namingContexts jābūt vienai vērtībai ar LDAP servera "
"meklēšanas bāzes DN. Vairākas vērtības netiek atbalstītas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:165
msgid "ldap_read_rootdse (string)"
msgstr "ldap_read_rootdse (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:168
msgid ""
"SSSD reads RootDSE to get information about LDAP and its capabilities. By "
"default, this is done anonymously. However, this may not be permitted by the "
"LDAP server. In such cases we can use this option to influence SSSD behavior."
msgstr ""
"SSSD nolasa RootDSE, lai iegūtu informāciju par LDAP un tā spējām. Pēc "
"noklusējuma tas tiek darīts anonīmi. Tomēr LDAP serveris to var neatļaut. "
"Šādos gadījumos ar šo opciju var ietekmēt SSSD rīcību."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:175
msgid "Allowed values are:"
msgstr "Atļautās vērtības:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:179
msgid "anonymous"
msgstr "anonymous"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:184
msgid "authenticated"
msgstr "authenticated"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:193
msgid ""
"By default, using the \"anonymous\" option, SSSD tries to read RootDSE "
"anonymously. If this fails SSSD retries the attempt with authentication."
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma, izmantojot opciju \"anonymous\", SSSD mēģina nolasīt "
"RootDSE anonīmi. Ja tas neizdodas, SSSD mēģina vēlreiz ar autentifikāciju."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:198
msgid "Default: anonymous"
msgstr "Noklusējums: anonymous"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:204
msgid "ldap_schema (string)"
msgstr "ldap_schema (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:207
msgid ""
"Specifies the Schema Type in use on the target LDAP server.  Depending on "
"the selected schema, the default attribute names retrieved from the servers "
"may vary.  The way that some attributes are handled may also differ."
msgstr ""
"Norāda mērķa LDAP serverī izmantoto shēmas tipu.  Atkarībā no izvēlētās "
"shēmas no serveriem izgūtie noklusējuma atribūtu nosaukumi var atšķirties.  "
"Var atšķirties arī dažu atribūtu apstrāde."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:214
msgid "Four schema types are currently supported:"
msgstr "Pašlaik tiek atbalstīti četri shēmu tipi:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:218
msgid "rfc2307"
msgstr "rfc2307"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:223
msgid "rfc2307bis"
msgstr "rfc2307bis"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:239
msgid ""
"The main difference between these schema types is how group memberships are "
"recorded in the server.  With rfc2307, group members are listed by name in "
"the <emphasis>memberUid</emphasis> attribute.  With rfc2307bis and IPA, "
"group members are listed by DN and stored in the <emphasis>member</emphasis> "
"attribute.  The AD schema type sets the attributes to correspond with Active "
"Directory 2008r2 values."
msgstr ""
"Galvenā atšķirība starp šiem shēmu tipiem ir tā, kā serverī tiek reģistrēta "
"grupu dalība.  Ar rfc2307 grupu dalībnieki tiek uzskaitīti pēc nosaukuma "
"atribūtā <emphasis>memberUid</emphasis>.  Ar rfc2307bis un IPA grupu "
"dalībnieki tiek uzskaitīti pēc DN un glabāti atribūtā <emphasis>member</"
"emphasis>.  AD shēmas tips iestata atribūtus atbilstoši Active Directory "
"2008r2 vērtībām."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:249
msgid "Default: rfc2307"
msgstr "Noklusējums: rfc2307"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:255
msgid "ldap_pwmodify_mode (string)"
msgstr "ldap_pwmodify_mode (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:258
msgid "Specify the operation that is used to modify user password."
msgstr "Norādīt darbību, ko izmanto lietotāja paroles mainīšanai."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:262
msgid "Two modes are currently supported:"
msgstr "Pašlaik tiek atbalstīti divi režīmi:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:266
msgid "exop - Password Modify Extended Operation (RFC 3062)"
msgstr "exop — paroles maiņas paplašinātā darbība (RFC 3062)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:272
msgid "ldap_modify - Direct modification of userPassword (not recommended)."
msgstr "ldap_modify — tieša userPassword mainīšana (nav ieteicams)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:278
msgid ""
"exop_force - Try Password Modify Extended Operation (RFC 3062) even if there "
"are no grace logins left.  Depending on the type and configuration of the "
"LDAP server the password change might fail because an authenticated bind is "
"not possible."
msgstr ""
"exop_force — mēģināt paroles maiņas paplašināto darbību (RFC 3062), pat ja "
"nav palikušas atvieglojuma pieteikšanās reizes.  Atkarībā no LDAP servera "
"tipa un konfigurācijas paroles maiņa var neizdoties, jo autentificēta "
"piesaiste nav iespējama."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:290
msgid ""
"Note: First, a new connection is established to verify current password by "
"binding as the user that requested password change. If successful, this "
"connection is used to change the password therefore the user must have write "
"access to userPassword attribute."
msgstr ""
"Piezīme: vispirms tiek izveidots jauns savienojums, lai pārbaudītu "
"pašreizējo paroli, piesaistoties kā lietotājs, kas pieprasīja paroles maiņu. "
"Ja tas izdodas, šo savienojumu izmanto paroles maiņai, tāpēc lietotājam "
"jābūt rakstīšanas piekļuvei atribūtam userPassword."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:298
msgid "Default: exop"
msgstr "Noklusējums: exop"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:304
msgid "ldap_default_bind_dn (string)"
msgstr "ldap_default_bind_dn (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:307
msgid "The default bind DN to use for performing LDAP operations."
msgstr "Noklusējuma piesaistes DN, ko izmantot LDAP darbībām."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:314
msgid "ldap_default_authtok_type (string)"
msgstr "ldap_default_authtok_type (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:317
msgid "The type of the authentication token of the default bind DN."
msgstr "Noklusējuma piesaistes DN autentifikācijas marķiera tips."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:321
msgid "The two mechanisms currently supported are:"
msgstr "Pašlaik tiek atbalstīti divi mehānismi:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:324
msgid "password"
msgstr "password"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:327
msgid "obfuscated_password"
msgstr "obfuscated_password"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:330
msgid "Default: password"
msgstr "Noklusējums: password"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:333
msgid ""
"See the <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sss_obfuscate</refentrytitle> "
"<manvolnum>8</manvolnum> </citerefentry> manual page for more information."
msgstr ""
"Plašāku informāciju skatiet rokasgrāmatas lapā <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>"
"sss_obfuscate</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>8</manvolnum> </citerefentry>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:344
msgid "ldap_default_authtok (string)"
msgstr "ldap_default_authtok (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:347
msgid "The authentication token of the default bind DN."
msgstr "Noklusējuma piesaistes DN autentifikācijas marķieris."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:353
msgid "ldap_force_upper_case_realm (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_force_upper_case_realm (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:356
msgid ""
"Some directory servers, for example Active Directory, might deliver the "
"realm part of the UPN in lower case, which might cause the authentication to "
"fail. Set this option to a non-zero value if you want to use an upper-case "
"realm."
msgstr ""
"Daži direktoriju serveri, piemēram, Active Directory, var piegādāt UPN "
"apgabala daļu mazajiem burtiem, kas var izraisīt autentifikācijas kļūmi. "
"Iestatiet šo opciju uz nenulles vērtību, ja vēlaties izmantot apgabalu "
"lielajiem burtiem."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:369
msgid "ldap_enumeration_refresh_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_enumeration_refresh_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:372
msgid ""
"Specifies how many seconds SSSD has to wait before refreshing its cache of "
"enumerated records."
msgstr ""
"Norāda, cik sekundes SSSD jāgaida, pirms atsvaidzināt savu uzskaitīto "
"ierakstu kešatmiņu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:383
msgid "ldap_purge_cache_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_purge_cache_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:386
msgid ""
"Determine how often to check the cache for inactive entries (such as groups "
"with no members and users who have never logged in) and remove them to save "
"space."
msgstr ""
"Nosaka, cik bieži pārbaudīt kešatmiņā neaktīvus ierakstus (piemēram, grupas "
"bez dalībniekiem un lietotājus, kuri nekad nav pieteikušies) un noņemt tos, "
"lai ietaupītu vietu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:392
msgid ""
"Setting this option to zero will disable the cache cleanup operation. Please "
"note that if enumeration is enabled, the cleanup task is required in order "
"to detect entries removed from the server and can't be disabled. By default, "
"the cleanup task will run every 3 hours with enumeration enabled."
msgstr ""
"Iestatot šo opciju uz nulli, kešatmiņas tīrīšanas darbība tiks atspējota. "
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā: ja ir iespējota uzskaitīšana, tīrīšanas uzdevums ir "
"nepieciešams, lai konstatētu no servera noņemtus ierakstus, un to nevar "
"atspējot. Pēc noklusējuma ar iespējotu uzskaitīšanu tīrīšanas uzdevums "
"darbosies ik pēc 3 stundām."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:412
msgid "ldap_group_nesting_level (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_group_nesting_level (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:415
msgid ""
"If ldap_schema is set to a schema format that supports nested groups (e.g. "
"RFC2307bis), then this option controls how many levels of nesting SSSD will "
"follow. This option has no effect on the RFC2307 schema."
msgstr ""
"Ja ldap_schema ir iestatīts uz shēmas formātu, kas atbalsta ligzdotas grupas "
"(piem., RFC2307bis), šī opcija nosaka, cik ligzdošanas līmeņiem SSSD sekos. "
"Šai opcijai nav ietekmes uz RFC2307 shēmu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:422
msgid ""
"Note: This option specifies the guaranteed level of nested groups to be "
"processed for any lookup. However, nested groups beyond this limit "
"<emphasis>may be</emphasis> returned if previous lookups already resolved "
"the deeper nesting levels.  Also, subsequent lookups for other groups may "
"enlarge the result set for original lookup if re-queried."
msgstr ""
"Piezīme: šī opcija norāda garantēto ligzdoto grupu līmeni, kas tiks "
"apstrādāts jebkurā uzmeklēšanā. Tomēr ligzdotas grupas aiz šī ierobežojuma "
"<emphasis>var tikt</emphasis> atgrieztas, ja iepriekšējās uzmeklēšanas jau "
"atrisināja dziļākos ligzdošanas līmeņus.  Turklāt citu grupu turpmākās "
"uzmeklēšanas var palielināt sākotnējās uzmeklēšanas rezultātu kopu, ja to "
"vaicā atkārtoti."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:431
msgid ""
"If ldap_group_nesting_level is set to 0 then no nested groups are processed "
"at all. However, when connected to Active-Directory Server 2008 and later "
"using <quote>id_provider=ad</quote> it is furthermore required to disable "
"usage of Token-Groups by setting ldap_use_tokengroups to false in order to "
"restrict group nesting."
msgstr ""
"Ja ldap_group_nesting_level ir iestatīts uz 0, ligzdotas grupas netiek "
"apstrādātas vispār. Tomēr, ja savienojums ir ar Active-Directory Server 2008 "
"vai jaunāku, izmantojot <quote>id_provider=ad</quote>, grupu ligzdošanas "
"ierobežošanai papildus jāatspējo Token-Groups izmantošana, iestatot "
"ldap_use_tokengroups uz false."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:440
msgid "Default: 2"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 2"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:449
msgid ""
"This options enables or disables use of Token-Groups attribute when "
"performing initgroup for users from Active Directory Server 2008 and later."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija iespējo vai atspējo atribūta Token-Groups izmantošanu, veicot "
"initgroup lietotājiem no Active Directory Server 2008 un jaunākiem."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:459
msgid "Default: True for AD and IPA otherwise False."
msgstr "Noklusējums: True AD un IPA, citādi False."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:465
msgid "ldap_host_search_base (string)"
msgstr "ldap_host_search_base (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:468
msgid "Optional. Use the given string as search base for host objects."
msgstr ""
"Neobligāts. Izmantot norādīto virkni kā resursdatoru objektu meklēšanas bāzi."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:472 sssd-ipa.5.xml:501 sssd-ipa.5.xml:520 sssd-ipa.5.xml:539
#: sssd-ipa.5.xml:558
msgid ""
"See <quote>ldap_search_base</quote> for information about configuring "
"multiple search bases."
msgstr ""
"Informāciju par vairāku meklēšanas bāzu konfigurēšanu skatiet <quote>"
"ldap_search_base</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:477 sssd-ipa.5.xml:506 include/ldap_search_bases.xml:27
msgid "Default: the value of <emphasis>ldap_search_base</emphasis>"
msgstr "Noklusējums: <emphasis>ldap_search_base</emphasis> vērtība"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:484
msgid "ldap_subid_ranges_search_base (string)"
msgstr "ldap_subid_ranges_search_base (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:487
msgid ""
"Optional. Use the given string as search base for subordinate ranges related "
"objects."
msgstr ""
"Neobligāts. Izmantot norādīto virkni kā ar pakārtotajiem diapazoniem "
"saistīto objektu meklēšanas bāzi."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:491
msgid ""
"Default: the value of <emphasis>cn=subids,%basedn</emphasis> for IPA "
"otherwise <emphasis>ldap_search_base</emphasis>."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: IPA — <emphasis>cn=subids,%basedn</emphasis> vērtība, citādi "
"<emphasis>ldap_search_base</emphasis>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:499
msgid "ldap_service_search_base (string)"
msgstr "ldap_service_search_base (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:504
msgid "ldap_iphost_search_base (string)"
msgstr "ldap_iphost_search_base (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:509
msgid "ldap_ipnetwork_search_base (string)"
msgstr "ldap_ipnetwork_search_base (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:514
msgid "ldap_search_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_search_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:517
msgid ""
"Specifies the timeout (in seconds) that ldap searches are allowed to run "
"before they are cancelled and cached results are returned (and offline mode "
"is entered)"
msgstr ""
"Norāda noildzi (sekundēs), cik ilgi drīkst darboties ldap meklēšana, pirms "
"tā tiek atcelta un tiek atgriezti kešotie rezultāti (un tiek pārslēgts "
"bezsaistes režīmā)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:523
msgid ""
"Note: this option is subject to change in future versions of the SSSD. It "
"will likely be replaced at some point by a series of timeouts for specific "
"lookup types."
msgstr ""
"Piezīme: šī opcija nākamajās SSSD versijās var mainīties. Visticamāk, kādā "
"brīdī to aizstās konkrētu uzmeklēšanas tipu noildžu kopa."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:540
msgid "ldap_enumeration_search_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_enumeration_search_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:543
msgid ""
"Specifies the timeout (in seconds) that ldap searches for user and group "
"enumerations are allowed to run before they are cancelled and cached results "
"are returned (and offline mode is entered)"
msgstr ""
"Norāda noildzi (sekundēs), cik ilgi drīkst darboties ldap meklēšana "
"lietotāju un grupu uzskaitīšanai, pirms tā tiek atcelta un tiek atgriezti "
"kešotie rezultāti (un tiek pārslēgts bezsaistes režīmā)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:556
msgid "ldap_network_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_network_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:559
msgid ""
"Specifies the timeout (in seconds) after which the <citerefentry> "
"<refentrytitle>poll</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>2</manvolnum> </citerefentry>/"
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>select</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>2</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry> following a <citerefentry> "
"<refentrytitle>connect</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>2</manvolnum> </"
"citerefentry> returns in case of no activity."
msgstr ""
"Norāda noildzi (sekundēs), pēc kuras <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>poll</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>2</manvolnum> </citerefentry>/<citerefentry> "
"<refentrytitle>select</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>2</manvolnum> </"
"citerefentry> pēc <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>connect</refentrytitle> "
"<manvolnum>2</manvolnum> </citerefentry> atgriežas, ja nav aktivitātes."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:587
msgid "ldap_opt_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_opt_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:590
msgid ""
"Specifies a timeout (in seconds) after which calls to synchronous LDAP APIs "
"will abort if no response is received. Also controls the timeout when "
"communicating with the KDC in case of SASL bind, the timeout of an LDAP bind "
"operation, password change extended operation and the StartTLS operation."
msgstr ""
"Norāda noildzi (sekundēs), pēc kuras sinhrono LDAP API izsaukumi tiks "
"pārtraukti, ja atbilde netiek saņemta. Nosaka arī noildzi saziņai ar KDC "
"SASL piesaistes gadījumā, LDAP piesaistes darbības, paroles maiņas "
"paplašinātās darbības un StartTLS darbības noildzi."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:610
msgid "ldap_connection_expire_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_connection_expire_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:613
msgid ""
"Specifies a timeout (in seconds) that a connection to an LDAP server will be "
"maintained. After this time, the connection will be re-established. If used "
"in parallel with SASL/GSSAPI, the sooner of the two values (this value vs. "
"the TGT lifetime)  will be used."
msgstr ""
"Norāda noildzi (sekundēs), cik ilgi tiks uzturēts savienojums ar LDAP "
"serveri. Pēc šī laika savienojums tiks izveidots no jauna. Ja izmanto "
"paralēli ar SASL/GSSAPI, tiks izmantota agrākā no abām vērtībām (šī vērtība "
"vai TGT dzīves ilgums)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:621
msgid ""
"If the connection is idle (not actively running an operation) within "
"<emphasis>ldap_opt_timeout</emphasis> seconds of expiration, then it will be "
"closed early to ensure that a new query cannot require the connection to "
"remain open past its expiration.  This implies that connections will always "
"be closed immediately and will never be reused if "
"<emphasis>ldap_connection_expire_timeout &lt;= ldap_opt_timeout</emphasis>"
msgstr ""
"Ja savienojums ir dīkstāvē (aktīvi neveic darbību) <emphasis>"
"ldap_opt_timeout</emphasis> sekunžu laikā pirms derīguma beigām, tas tiks "
"aizvērts agrāk, lai nodrošinātu, ka jauns vaicājums nevar pieprasīt "
"savienojuma uzturēšanu pēc tā derīguma beigām.  Tas nozīmē, ka savienojumi "
"vienmēr tiks aizvērti nekavējoties un nekad netiks izmantoti atkārtoti, ja "
"<emphasis>ldap_connection_expire_timeout &lt;= ldap_opt_timeout</emphasis>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:633
msgid ""
"This timeout can be extended of a random value specified by "
"<emphasis>ldap_connection_expire_offset</emphasis>"
msgstr ""
"Šo noildzi var pagarināt par nejaušu vērtību, kas norādīta ar <emphasis>"
"ldap_connection_expire_offset</emphasis>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:643 sssd-ldap.5.xml:686 sssd-ldap.5.xml:1809
msgid "Default: 900 (15 minutes)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 900 (15 minūtes)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:649
msgid "ldap_connection_expire_offset (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_connection_expire_offset (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:652
msgid ""
"Random offset between 0 and configured value is added to "
"<emphasis>ldap_connection_expire_timeout</emphasis>."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>ldap_connection_expire_timeout</emphasis> tiek pieskaitīta nejauša "
"nobīde starp 0 un konfigurēto vērtību."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:668
msgid "ldap_connection_idle_timeout (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_connection_idle_timeout (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:671
msgid ""
"Specifies a timeout (in seconds) that an idle connection to an LDAP server "
"will be maintained.  If the connection is idle for more than this time then "
"the connection will be closed."
msgstr ""
"Norāda noildzi (sekundēs), cik ilgi tiks uzturēts dīkstāvē esošs savienojums "
"ar LDAP serveri.  Ja savienojums ir dīkstāvē ilgāk par šo laiku, tas tiks "
"aizvērts."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:677
msgid "You can disable this timeout by setting the value to 0."
msgstr "Šo noildzi var atspējot, iestatot vērtību uz 0."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:692
msgid "ldap_page_size (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_page_size (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:695
msgid ""
"Specify the number of records to retrieve from LDAP in a single request. "
"Some LDAP servers enforce a maximum limit per-request."
msgstr ""
"Norādīt vienā pieprasījumā no LDAP izgūstamo ierakstu skaitu. Daži LDAP "
"serveri piespiež maksimālo ierobežojumu katram pieprasījumam."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:706
msgid "ldap_disable_paging (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_disable_paging (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:709
msgid ""
"Disable the LDAP paging control. This option should be used if the LDAP "
"server reports that it supports the LDAP paging control in its RootDSE but "
"it is not enabled or does not behave properly."
msgstr ""
"Atspējot LDAP lapošanas vadīklu. Šī opcija jāizmanto, ja LDAP serveris savā "
"RootDSE ziņo, ka atbalsta LDAP lapošanas vadīklu, bet tā nav iespējota vai "
"nedarbojas pareizi."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:715
msgid ""
"Example: OpenLDAP servers with the paging control module installed on the "
"server but not enabled will report it in the RootDSE but be unable to use it."
msgstr ""
"Piemērs: OpenLDAP serveri, kuros lapošanas vadīklas modulis ir instalēts, "
"bet nav iespējots, ziņos par to RootDSE, bet nespēs to izmantot."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:721
msgid ""
"Example: 389 DS has a bug where it can only support a one paging control at "
"a time on a single connection. On busy clients, this can result in some "
"requests being denied."
msgstr ""
"Piemērs: 389 DS ir kļūda, kuras dēļ tas vienā savienojumā vienlaikus var "
"atbalstīt tikai vienu lapošanas vadīklu. Noslogotos klientos tā rezultātā "
"daži pieprasījumi var tikt noraidīti."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:733
msgid "ldap_disable_range_retrieval (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_disable_range_retrieval (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:736
msgid "Disable Active Directory range retrieval."
msgstr "Atspējot Active Directory diapazona izgūšanu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:739
msgid ""
"Active Directory limits the number of members that can be retrieved in a "
"single lookup using the MaxValRange policy, which defaults to 1500 members. "
"If a group contains more than 1500 members, the reply includes an AD-"
"specific range extension. When enabled, this option prevents SSSD from "
"parsing the range extension. As a result large groups will appear as they "
"have no members.  This option does not enable SSSD to read subsequent "
"ranges. To retrieve all members of a group, you must increase the "
"MaxValRange setting in Active Directory."
msgstr ""
"Active Directory ierobežo vienā uzmeklēšanā izgūstamo dalībnieku skaitu ar "
"politiku MaxValRange, kuras noklusējums ir 1500 dalībnieku. Ja grupā ir "
"vairāk nekā 1500 dalībnieku, atbilde ietver AD specifisku diapazona "
"paplašinājumu. Ja šī opcija ir iespējota, SSSD neparsē diapazona "
"paplašinājumu. Tā rezultātā lielas grupas izskatīsies tā, it kā tām nebūtu "
"dalībnieku.  Šī opcija neļauj SSSD nolasīt nākamos diapazonus. Lai izgūtu "
"visus grupas dalībniekus, Active Directory jāpalielina iestatījums "
"MaxValRange."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:758
msgid "ldap_sasl_minssf (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_sasl_minssf (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:761
msgid ""
"When communicating with an LDAP server using SASL, specify the minimum "
"security level necessary to establish the connection. The values of this "
"option are defined by OpenLDAP."
msgstr ""
"Sazinoties ar LDAP serveri caur SASL, norādīt minimālo drošības līmeni, kas "
"nepieciešams savienojuma izveidei. Šīs opcijas vērtības definē OpenLDAP."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:767 sssd-ldap.5.xml:783
msgid "Default: Use the system default (usually specified by ldap.conf)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: izmantot sistēmas noklusējumu (parasti norādīts ldap.conf)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:774
msgid "ldap_sasl_maxssf (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_sasl_maxssf (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:777
msgid ""
"When communicating with an LDAP server using SASL, specify the maximal "
"security level necessary to establish the connection. The values of this "
"option are defined by OpenLDAP."
msgstr ""
"Sazinoties ar LDAP serveri caur SASL, norādīt maksimālo drošības līmeni, kas "
"nepieciešams savienojuma izveidei. Šīs opcijas vērtības definē OpenLDAP."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:790
msgid "ldap_deref_threshold (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_deref_threshold (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:793
msgid ""
"Specify the number of group members that must be missing from the internal "
"cache in order to trigger a dereference lookup. If less members are missing, "
"they are looked up individually."
msgstr ""
"Norādīt grupas dalībnieku skaitu, kam jātrūkst iekšējā kešatmiņā, lai "
"izraisītu atsauces atrisināšanas uzmeklēšanu. Ja trūkst mazāk dalībnieku, "
"tie tiek uzmeklēti atsevišķi."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:799
msgid ""
"You can turn off dereference lookups completely by setting the value to 0. "
"Please note that there are some codepaths in SSSD, like the IPA HBAC "
"provider, that are only implemented using the dereference call, so even with "
"dereference explicitly disabled, those parts will still use dereference if "
"the server supports it and advertises the dereference control in the rootDSE "
"object."
msgstr ""
"Atsauces atrisināšanas uzmeklēšanu var pilnībā izslēgt, iestatot vērtību uz "
"0. Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka SSSD ir daži koda ceļi, piemēram, IPA HBAC "
"nodrošinātājs, kas realizēti tikai ar atsauces atrisināšanas izsaukumu, "
"tāpēc pat ar skaidri atspējotu atsauces atrisināšanu šīs daļas joprojām to "
"izmantos, ja serveris to atbalsta un rootDSE objektā izsludina atsauces "
"atrisināšanas vadīklu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:810
msgid ""
"A dereference lookup is a means of fetching all group members in a single "
"LDAP call.  Different LDAP servers may implement different dereference "
"methods. The currently supported servers are 389/RHDS, OpenLDAP and Active "
"Directory."
msgstr ""
"Atsauces atrisināšanas uzmeklēšana ir veids, kā ienest visus grupas "
"dalībniekus vienā LDAP izsaukumā.  Dažādi LDAP serveri var realizēt dažādas "
"atsauces atrisināšanas metodes. Pašlaik atbalstītie serveri ir 389/RHDS, "
"OpenLDAP un Active Directory."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:818
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Note:</emphasis> If any of the search bases specifies a search "
"filter, then the dereference lookup performance enhancement will be disabled "
"regardless of this setting."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>Piezīme:</emphasis> ja kāda no meklēšanas bāzēm norāda meklēšanas "
"filtru, atsauces atrisināšanas uzmeklēšanas veiktspējas uzlabojums "
"neatkarīgi no šī iestatījuma tiks atspējots."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:831
msgid "ldap_ignore_unreadable_references (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_ignore_unreadable_references (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:834
msgid ""
"Ignore unreadable LDAP entries referenced in group's member attribute. If "
"this parameter is set to false an error will be returned and the operation "
"will fail instead of just ignoring the unreadable entry."
msgstr ""
"Ignorēt nelasāmus LDAP ierakstus, uz kuriem atsaucas grupas atribūts member. "
"Ja šis parametrs ir iestatīts uz false, tiks atgriezta kļūda un darbība "
"neizdosies, nevis vienkārši ignorēs nelasāmo ierakstu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:841
msgid ""
"This parameter may be useful when using the AD provider and the computer "
"account that sssd uses to connect to AD does not have access to a particular "
"entry or LDAP sub-tree for security reasons."
msgstr ""
"Šis parametrs var noderēt, izmantojot AD nodrošinātāju, ja datora kontam, ar "
"kuru sssd savienojas ar AD, drošības apsvērumu dēļ nav piekļuves konkrētam "
"ierakstam vai LDAP apakškokam."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:854
msgid "ldap_tls_reqcert (string)"
msgstr "ldap_tls_reqcert (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:857
msgid ""
"Specifies what checks to perform on server certificates in a TLS session, if "
"any. It can be specified as one of the following values:"
msgstr ""
"Norāda, kādas pārbaudes (ja vispār) veikt servera sertifikātiem TLS sesijā. "
"To var norādīt kā vienu no šīm vērtībām:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:863
msgid ""
"<emphasis>never</emphasis> = The client will not request or check any server "
"certificate."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>never</emphasis> = klients nepieprasīs un nepārbaudīs nekādu "
"servera sertifikātu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:867
msgid ""
"<emphasis>allow</emphasis> = The server certificate is requested. If no "
"certificate is provided, the session proceeds normally. If a bad certificate "
"is provided, it will be ignored and the session proceeds normally."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>allow</emphasis> = servera sertifikāts tiek pieprasīts. Ja "
"sertifikāts netiek nodrošināts, sesija turpinās normāli. Ja tiek nodrošināts "
"slikts sertifikāts, tas tiks ignorēts un sesija turpināsies normāli."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:874
msgid ""
"<emphasis>try</emphasis> = The server certificate is requested. If no "
"certificate is provided, the session proceeds normally. If a bad certificate "
"is provided, the session is immediately terminated."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>try</emphasis> = servera sertifikāts tiek pieprasīts. Ja "
"sertifikāts netiek nodrošināts, sesija turpinās normāli. Ja tiek nodrošināts "
"slikts sertifikāts, sesija nekavējoties tiek pārtraukta."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:880
msgid ""
"<emphasis>demand</emphasis> = The server certificate is requested. If no "
"certificate is provided, or a bad certificate is provided, the session is "
"immediately terminated."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>demand</emphasis> = servera sertifikāts tiek pieprasīts. Ja "
"sertifikāts netiek nodrošināts vai tiek nodrošināts slikts sertifikāts, "
"sesija nekavējoties tiek pārtraukta."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:886
msgid "<emphasis>hard</emphasis> = Same as <quote>demand</quote>"
msgstr "<emphasis>hard</emphasis> = tas pats, kas <quote>demand</quote>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:890
msgid "Default: hard"
msgstr "Noklusējums: hard"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:896
msgid "ldap_tls_cacert (string)"
msgstr "ldap_tls_cacert (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:899
msgid ""
"Specifies the file that contains certificates for all of the Certificate "
"Authorities that <command>sssd</command> will recognize."
msgstr ""
"Norāda failu, kas satur visu sertificēšanas iestāžu sertifikātus, kurus "
"<command>sssd</command> atzīs."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:904 sssd-ldap.5.xml:923 sssd-ldap.5.xml:964
msgid ""
"Default: use OpenLDAP defaults, typically in <filename>/etc/openldap/"
"ldap.conf</filename>"
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: izmantot OpenLDAP noklusējumus, parasti <filename>/etc/openldap/"
"ldap.conf</filename>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:911
msgid "ldap_tls_cacertdir (string)"
msgstr "ldap_tls_cacertdir (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:914
msgid ""
"Specifies the path of a directory that contains Certificate Authority "
"certificates in separate individual files. Typically the file names need to "
"be the hash of the certificate followed by '.0'.  If available, "
"<command>openssl rehash</command> or <command>c_rehash</command> can be used "
"to create the correct names."
msgstr ""
"Norāda ceļu uz direktoriju, kas satur sertificēšanas iestāžu sertifikātus "
"atsevišķos failos. Parasti failu nosaukumiem jābūt sertifikāta "
"jaucējvērtībai, kam seko „.0”.  Ja pieejams, pareizo nosaukumu izveidei var "
"izmantot <command>openssl rehash</command> vai <command>c_rehash</command>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:930
msgid "ldap_tls_cert (string)"
msgstr "ldap_tls_cert (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:933
msgid "Specifies the file that contains the certificate for the client's key."
msgstr "Norāda failu, kas satur klienta atslēgas sertifikātu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:943
msgid "ldap_tls_key (string)"
msgstr "ldap_tls_key (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:946
msgid "Specifies the file that contains the client's key."
msgstr "Norāda failu, kas satur klienta atslēgu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:955
msgid "ldap_tls_cipher_suite (string)"
msgstr "ldap_tls_cipher_suite (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:958
msgid ""
"Specifies acceptable cipher suites.  Typically this is a colon separated "
"list.  See <citerefentry><refentrytitle>ldap.conf</refentrytitle> "
"<manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry> for format."
msgstr ""
"Norāda pieņemamos šifru komplektus.  Parasti tas ir ar koliem atdalīts "
"saraksts.  Formātu skatiet <citerefentry><refentrytitle>ldap.conf</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:971
msgid "ldap_id_use_start_tls (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_id_use_start_tls (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:974
msgid ""
"Specifies that the id_provider connection must also use <systemitem "
"class=\"protocol\">tls</systemitem> to protect the channel.  <emphasis>true</"
"emphasis> is strongly recommended for security reasons."
msgstr ""
"Norāda, ka id_provider savienojumam kanāla aizsardzībai arī jāizmanto "
"<systemitem class=\"protocol\">tls</systemitem>.  Drošības apsvērumu dēļ "
"<emphasis>true</emphasis> ir stingri ieteicams."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:985
msgid "ldap_id_mapping (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_id_mapping (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:988
msgid ""
"Specifies that SSSD should attempt to map user and group IDs from the "
"ldap_user_objectsid and ldap_group_objectsid attributes instead of relying "
"on ldap_user_uid_number and ldap_group_gid_number."
msgstr ""
"Norāda, ka SSSD jāmēģina kartēt lietotāju un grupu ID no atribūtiem "
"ldap_user_objectsid un ldap_group_objectsid, nevis jāpaļaujas uz "
"ldap_user_uid_number un ldap_group_gid_number."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:994
msgid "Currently this feature supports only ActiveDirectory objectSID mapping."
msgstr ""
"Pašlaik šis līdzeklis atbalsta tikai ActiveDirectory objectSID kartēšanu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1004
msgid "ldap_min_id, ldap_max_id (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_min_id, ldap_max_id (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1007
msgid ""
"In contrast to the SID based ID mapping which is used if ldap_id_mapping is "
"set to true the allowed ID range for ldap_user_uid_number and "
"ldap_group_gid_number is unbound. In a setup with sub/trusted-domains this "
"might lead to ID collisions. To avoid collisions ldap_min_id and ldap_max_id "
"can be set to restrict the allowed range for the IDs which are read directly "
"from the server. Sub-domains can then pick other ranges to map IDs."
msgstr ""
"Atšķirībā no uz SID balstītās ID kartēšanas, ko izmanto, ja ldap_id_mapping "
"ir iestatīts uz true, atļautais ID diapazons ldap_user_uid_number un "
"ldap_group_gid_number nav ierobežots. Iestatījumā ar apakšdomēniem/"
"uzticamiem domēniem tas var izraisīt ID sadursmes. Lai no tām izvairītos, "
"var iestatīt ldap_min_id un ldap_max_id, ierobežojot atļauto diapazonu ID, "
"kas tiek nolasīti tieši no servera. Apakšdomēni tad ID kartēšanai var "
"izvēlēties citus diapazonus."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1019
msgid "Default: not set (both options are set to 0)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: nav iestatīts (abas opcijas iestatītas uz 0)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1025
msgid "ldap_sasl_mech (string)"
msgstr "ldap_sasl_mech (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1028
msgid ""
"Specify the SASL mechanism to use.  Currently only GSSAPI and GSS-SPNEGO are "
"tested and supported."
msgstr ""
"Norādīt izmantojamo SASL mehānismu.  Pašlaik pārbaudīti un atbalstīti ir "
"tikai GSSAPI un GSS-SPNEGO."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1032
msgid ""
"If the backend supports sub-domains the value of ldap_sasl_mech is "
"automatically inherited to the sub-domains. If a different value is needed "
"for a sub-domain it can be overwritten by setting ldap_sasl_mech for this "
"sub-domain explicitly.  Please see TRUSTED DOMAIN SECTION in "
"<citerefentry><refentrytitle>sssd.conf</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</"
"manvolnum></citerefentry> for details."
msgstr ""
"Ja aizmugursistēma atbalsta apakšdomēnus, ldap_sasl_mech vērtība automātiski "
"tiek mantota apakšdomēniem. Ja apakšdomēnam vajadzīga cita vērtība, to var "
"pārrakstīt, šim apakšdomēnam skaidri iestatot ldap_sasl_mech.  Sīkāk skatiet "
"sadaļu TRUSTED DOMAIN SECTION lapā <citerefentry><refentrytitle>sssd.conf</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1048
msgid "ldap_sasl_authid (string)"
msgstr "ldap_sasl_authid (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><programlisting>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1060
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"hostname@REALM\n"
"netbiosname$@REALM\n"
"host/hostname@REALM\n"
"*$@REALM\n"
"host/*@REALM\n"
"netbiosname$@*\n"
"host/*\n"
"                            "
msgstr ""
"hostname@REALM\n"
"netbiosname$@REALM\n"
"host/hostname@REALM\n"
"*$@REALM\n"
"host/*@REALM\n"
"netbiosname$@*\n"
"host/*\n"
"                            "

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1051
msgid ""
"Specify the SASL authorization id to use.  When GSSAPI/GSS-SPNEGO are used, "
"this represents the Kerberos principal used for authentication to the "
"directory.  This option can either contain the full principal (for example "
"host/myhost@EXAMPLE.COM) or just the principal name (for example host/"
"myhost).  By default, the value is not set and the following principals are "
"used: <placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/> If none of them are "
"found, the first principal in keytab is returned."
msgstr ""
"Norādīt izmantojamo SASL autorizācijas id.  Ja tiek izmantots GSSAPI/GSS-"
"SPNEGO, tas ir Kerberos principāls, ko izmanto autentifikācijai "
"direktorijā.  Šī opcija var saturēt vai nu pilno principālu (piemēram, host/"
"myhost@EXAMPLE.COM), vai tikai principāla nosaukumu (piemēram, host/myhost)"
".  Pēc noklusējuma vērtība nav iestatīta un tiek izmantoti šādi principāli: "
"<placeholder type=\"programlisting\" id=\"0\"/> Ja neviens no tiem netiek "
"atrasts, tiek atgriezts pirmais principāls keytab."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1072
msgid "Default: host/hostname@REALM"
msgstr "Noklusējums: host/hostname@REALM"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1078
msgid "ldap_sasl_realm (string)"
msgstr "ldap_sasl_realm (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1081
msgid ""
"Specify the SASL realm to use. When not specified, this option defaults to "
"the value of krb5_realm.  If the ldap_sasl_authid contains the realm as "
"well, this option is ignored."
msgstr ""
"Norādīt izmantojamo SASL apgabalu. Ja nav norādīts, šīs opcijas noklusējums "
"ir krb5_realm vērtība.  Ja ldap_sasl_authid satur arī apgabalu, šī opcija "
"tiek ignorēta."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1087
msgid "Default: the value of krb5_realm."
msgstr "Noklusējums: krb5_realm vērtība."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1093
msgid "ldap_sasl_canonicalize (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_sasl_canonicalize (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1096
msgid ""
"If set to true, the LDAP library would perform a reverse lookup to "
"canonicalize the host name during a SASL bind."
msgstr ""
"Ja iestatīts uz true, LDAP bibliotēka SASL piesaistes laikā veiks reverso "
"uzmeklēšanu, lai kanonizētu resursdatora nosaukumu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1101
msgid "Default: false;"
msgstr "Noklusējums: false;"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1107
msgid "ldap_krb5_keytab (string)"
msgstr "ldap_krb5_keytab (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1110
msgid "Specify the keytab to use when using SASL/GSSAPI/GSS-SPNEGO."
msgstr "Norādīt keytab, ko izmantot, izmantojot SASL/GSSAPI/GSS-SPNEGO."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1119 sssd-krb5.5.xml:257
msgid "Default: System keytab, normally <filename>/etc/krb5.keytab</filename>"
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: sistēmas keytab, parasti <filename>/etc/krb5.keytab</filename>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1125
msgid "ldap_krb5_init_creds (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_krb5_init_creds (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1128
msgid ""
"Specifies that the id_provider should init Kerberos credentials (TGT).  This "
"action is performed only if SASL is used and the mechanism selected is "
"GSSAPI or GSS-SPNEGO."
msgstr ""
"Norāda, ka id_provider jāinicializē Kerberos akreditācijas dati (TGT).  Šī "
"darbība tiek veikta tikai tad, ja tiek izmantots SASL un izvēlētais "
"mehānisms ir GSSAPI vai GSS-SPNEGO."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1140
msgid "ldap_krb5_ticket_lifetime (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_krb5_ticket_lifetime (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1143
msgid ""
"Specifies the lifetime in seconds of the TGT if GSSAPI or GSS-SPNEGO is used."
msgstr ""
"Norāda TGT dzīves ilgumu sekundēs, ja tiek izmantots GSSAPI vai GSS-SPNEGO."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1152 sssd-ad.5.xml:1260
msgid "Default: 86400 (24 hours)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 86400 (24 stundas)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1158 sssd-krb5.5.xml:74
msgid "krb5_server, krb5_backup_server (string)"
msgstr "krb5_server, krb5_backup_server (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1161
msgid ""
"Specifies the comma-separated list of IP addresses or hostnames of the "
"Kerberos servers to which SSSD should connect in the order of preference. "
"For more information on failover and server redundancy, see the "
"<quote>FAILOVER</quote> section. An optional port number (preceded by a "
"colon) may be appended to the addresses or hostnames.  If empty, service "
"discovery is enabled - for more information, refer to the <quote>SERVICE "
"DISCOVERY</quote> section."
msgstr ""
"Norāda ar komatiem atdalītu to Kerberos serveru IP adrešu vai resursdatoru "
"nosaukumu sarakstu, ar kuriem SSSD jāsavienojas, vēlamības secībā. Plašāku "
"informāciju par pārņemšanu un serveru dublēšanu skatiet sadaļā <quote>"
"FAILOVER</quote>. Adresēm vai resursdatoru nosaukumiem var pievienot "
"neobligātu porta numuru (pirms tā kols).  Ja tukšs, ir iespējota pakalpojumu "
"atklāšana — plašāku informāciju skatiet sadaļā <quote>SERVICE DISCOVERY</"
"quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1173 sssd-krb5.5.xml:89
msgid ""
"When using service discovery for KDC or kpasswd servers, SSSD first searches "
"for DNS entries that specify _udp as the protocol and falls back to _tcp if "
"none are found."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojot KDC vai kpasswd serveru pakalpojumu atklāšanu, SSSD vispirms "
"meklē DNS ierakstus, kas kā protokolu norāda _udp, un, ja tādi netiek "
"atrasti, pārslēdzas uz _tcp."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1178 sssd-krb5.5.xml:94
msgid ""
"This option was named <quote>krb5_kdcip</quote> in earlier releases of SSSD. "
"While the legacy name is recognized for the time being, users are advised to "
"migrate their config files to use <quote>krb5_server</quote> instead."
msgstr ""
"Agrākos SSSD laidienos šī opcija saucās <quote>krb5_kdcip</quote>. Lai gan "
"pagaidām mantotais nosaukums tiek atpazīts, lietotājiem ieteicams pārveidot "
"savus konfigurācijas failus, lai tie tā vietā izmantotu <quote>krb5_server</"
"quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1187 sssd-ipa.5.xml:570 sssd-krb5.5.xml:103
msgid "krb5_realm (string)"
msgstr "krb5_realm (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1190
msgid "Specify the Kerberos REALM (for SASL/GSSAPI/GSS-SPNEGO auth)."
msgstr "Norādīt Kerberos APGABALU (SASL/GSSAPI/GSS-SPNEGO autentifikācijai)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1194
msgid "Default: System defaults, see <filename>/etc/krb5.conf</filename>"
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: sistēmas noklusējumi, skatiet <filename>/etc/krb5.conf</"
"filename>"

#. type: Content of: <variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1200 include/krb5_options.xml:160
msgid "krb5_canonicalize (boolean)"
msgstr "krb5_canonicalize (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1203
msgid ""
"Specifies if the host principal should be canonicalized when connecting to "
"LDAP server. This feature is available with MIT Kerberos >= 1.7"
msgstr ""
"Norāda, vai, savienojoties ar LDAP serveri, resursdatora principāls "
"jākanonizē. Šis līdzeklis pieejams ar MIT Kerberos >= 1.7"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1215 sssd-krb5.5.xml:346
msgid "krb5_use_kdcinfo (boolean)"
msgstr "krb5_use_kdcinfo (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1218 sssd-krb5.5.xml:349
msgid ""
"Specifies if the SSSD should instruct the Kerberos libraries what realm and "
"which KDCs to use. This option is on by default, if you disable it, you need "
"to configure the Kerberos library using the <citerefentry> "
"<refentrytitle>krb5.conf</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</manvolnum> </"
"citerefentry> configuration file."
msgstr ""
"Norāda, vai SSSD jānorāda Kerberos bibliotēkām, kuru apgabalu un kurus KDC "
"izmantot. Šī opcija pēc noklusējuma ir ieslēgta; ja to atspējojat, Kerberos "
"bibliotēka jākonfigurē ar konfigurācijas failu <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>"
"krb5.conf</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</manvolnum> </citerefentry>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1229 sssd-krb5.5.xml:360
msgid ""
"See the <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd_krb5_locator_plugin</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>8</manvolnum> </citerefentry> manual page for more "
"information on the locator plugin."
msgstr ""
"Plašāku informāciju par lokatora spraudni skatiet rokasgrāmatas lapā "
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd_krb5_locator_plugin</refentrytitle> "
"<manvolnum>8</manvolnum> </citerefentry>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1243
msgid "ldap_pwd_policy (string)"
msgstr "ldap_pwd_policy (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1246
msgid ""
"Select the policy to evaluate the password expiration on the client side. "
"The following values are allowed:"
msgstr ""
"Izvēlēties politiku paroles derīguma beigu izvērtēšanai klienta pusē. "
"Atļautas šādas vērtības:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1251
msgid ""
"<emphasis>none</emphasis> - No evaluation on the client side. This option "
"cannot disable server-side password policies."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>none</emphasis> — klienta pusē izvērtēšana nenotiek. Šī opcija "
"nevar atspējot servera puses paroļu politikas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1256
msgid ""
"<emphasis>shadow</emphasis> - Use <citerefentry><refentrytitle>shadow</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry> style attributes to "
"evaluate if the password has expired.  Please see option "
"\"ldap_chpass_update_last_change\" as well."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>shadow</emphasis> — izmantot <citerefentry><refentrytitle>shadow</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry> stila atribūtus, lai "
"izvērtētu, vai parolei beidzies derīgums.  Lūdzu, skatiet arī opciju "
"\"ldap_chpass_update_last_change\"."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1264
msgid ""
"<emphasis>mit_kerberos</emphasis> - Use the attributes used by MIT Kerberos "
"to determine if the password has expired. Use chpass_provider=krb5 to update "
"these attributes when the password is changed."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>mit_kerberos</emphasis> — izmantot MIT Kerberos izmantotos "
"atribūtus, lai noteiktu, vai parolei beidzies derīgums. Lai mainot paroli "
"atjauninātu šos atribūtus, izmantojiet chpass_provider=krb5."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1273
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Note</emphasis>: if a password policy is configured on server "
"side, it always takes precedence over policy set with this option."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>Piezīme</emphasis>: ja servera pusē ir konfigurēta paroļu "
"politika, tai vienmēr ir prioritāte pār ar šo opciju iestatīto politiku."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1281
msgid "ldap_referrals (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_referrals (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1284
msgid "Specifies whether automatic referral chasing should be enabled."
msgstr "Norāda, vai jāiespējo automātiska sekošana pāradresācijām."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1288
msgid ""
"Please note that sssd only supports referral chasing when it is compiled "
"with OpenLDAP version 2.4.13 or higher."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka sssd atbalsta sekošanu pāradresācijām tikai tad, ja "
"tas kompilēts ar OpenLDAP versiju 2.4.13 vai jaunāku."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1293
msgid ""
"Chasing referrals may incur a performance penalty in environments that use "
"them heavily, a notable example is Microsoft Active Directory. If your setup "
"does not in fact require the use of referrals, setting this option to false "
"might bring a noticeable performance improvement.  Setting this option to "
"false is therefore recommended in case the SSSD LDAP provider is used "
"together with Microsoft Active Directory as a backend. Even if SSSD would be "
"able to follow the referral to a different AD DC no additional data would be "
"available."
msgstr ""
"Sekošana pāradresācijām var samazināt veiktspēju vidēs, kur tās tiek "
"intensīvi izmantotas; ievērojams piemērs ir Microsoft Active Directory. Ja "
"jūsu iestatījumam pāradresāciju izmantošana patiesībā nav vajadzīga, šīs "
"opcijas iestatīšana uz false var dot ievērojamu veiktspējas uzlabojumu.  "
"Tāpēc šo opciju ieteicams iestatīt uz false, ja SSSD LDAP nodrošinātājs tiek "
"izmantots kopā ar Microsoft Active Directory kā aizmugursistēmu. Pat ja SSSD "
"spētu sekot pāradresācijai uz citu AD DC, papildu dati nebūtu pieejami."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1312
msgid "ldap_dns_service_name (string)"
msgstr "ldap_dns_service_name (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1315
msgid "Specifies the service name to use when service discovery is enabled."
msgstr ""
"Norāda pakalpojuma nosaukumu, ko izmantot, ja ir iespējota pakalpojumu "
"atklāšana."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1319
msgid "Default: ldap"
msgstr "Noklusējums: ldap"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1325
msgid "ldap_chpass_dns_service_name (string)"
msgstr "ldap_chpass_dns_service_name (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1328
msgid ""
"Specifies the service name to use to find an LDAP server which allows "
"password changes when service discovery is enabled."
msgstr ""
"Norāda pakalpojuma nosaukumu, ko izmantot, lai atrastu LDAP serveri, kas "
"atļauj paroles maiņu, ja ir iespējota pakalpojumu atklāšana."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1333
msgid "Default: not set, i.e. service discovery is disabled"
msgstr "Noklusējums: nav iestatīts, t. i., pakalpojumu atklāšana ir atspējota"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1339
msgid "ldap_chpass_update_last_change (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_chpass_update_last_change (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1342
msgid ""
"Specifies whether to update the ldap_user_shadow_last_change attribute with "
"days since the Epoch after a password change operation."
msgstr ""
"Norāda, vai pēc paroles maiņas darbības atjaunināt atribūtu "
"ldap_user_shadow_last_change ar dienu skaitu kopš epohas sākuma."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1348
msgid ""
"It is recommended to set this option explicitly if \"ldap_pwd_policy = "
"shadow\" is used to let SSSD know if the LDAP server will update "
"shadowLastChange LDAP attribute automatically after a password change or if "
"SSSD has to update it."
msgstr ""
"Ja tiek izmantots \"ldap_pwd_policy = shadow\", šo opciju ieteicams iestatīt "
"skaidri, lai SSSD zinātu, vai LDAP serveris pēc paroles maiņas automātiski "
"atjauninās LDAP atribūtu shadowLastChange vai tas jāatjaunina SSSD."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1362
msgid "ldap_access_filter (string)"
msgstr "ldap_access_filter (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1365
msgid ""
"If using access_provider = ldap and ldap_access_order = filter (default), "
"this option is mandatory. It specifies an LDAP search filter criteria that "
"must be met for the user to be granted access on this host. If "
"access_provider = ldap, ldap_access_order = filter and this option is not "
"set, it will result in all users being denied access.  Use access_provider = "
"permit to change this default behavior. Please note that this filter is "
"applied on the LDAP user entry only and thus filtering based on nested "
"groups may not work (e.g. memberOf attribute on AD entries points only to "
"direct parents). If filtering based on nested groups is required, please see "
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd-simple</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry>."
msgstr ""
"Ja izmanto access_provider = ldap un ldap_access_order = filter (noklusējums)"
", šī opcija ir obligāta. Tā norāda LDAP meklēšanas filtra kritērijus, kas "
"jāizpilda, lai lietotājam piešķirtu piekļuvi šim resursdatoram. Ja "
"access_provider = ldap, ldap_access_order = filter un šī opcija nav "
"iestatīta, piekļuve tiks liegta visiem lietotājiem.  Lai mainītu šo "
"noklusējuma rīcību, izmantojiet access_provider = permit. Lūdzu, ņemiet "
"vērā, ka šis filtrs tiek piemērots tikai LDAP lietotāja ierakstam, tāpēc "
"filtrēšana pēc ligzdotām grupām var nedarboties (piem., atribūts memberOf AD "
"ierakstos norāda tikai uz tiešajiem vecākiem). Ja nepieciešama filtrēšana "
"pēc ligzdotām grupām, lūdzu, skatiet <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd-"
"simple</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</manvolnum> </citerefentry>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1385
msgid "Example:"
msgstr "Piemērs:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><programlisting>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1388
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"access_provider = ldap\n"
"ldap_access_filter = (employeeType=admin)\n"
"                        "
msgstr ""
"access_provider = ldap\n"
"ldap_access_filter = (employeeType=admin)\n"
"                        "

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1392
msgid ""
"This example means that access to this host is restricted to users whose "
"employeeType attribute is set to \"admin\"."
msgstr ""
"Šis piemērs nozīmē, ka piekļuve šim resursdatoram ir ierobežota ar "
"lietotājiem, kuru atribūts employeeType ir iestatīts uz \"admin\"."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1397
msgid ""
"Offline caching for this feature is limited to determining whether the "
"user's last online login was granted access permission. If they were granted "
"access during their last login, they will continue to be granted access "
"while offline and vice versa."
msgstr ""
"Bezsaistes kešošana šim līdzeklim aprobežojas ar noteikšanu, vai lietotāja "
"pēdējā tiešsaistes pieteikšanās reizē tika piešķirta piekļuves atļauja. Ja "
"pēdējās pieteikšanās laikā piekļuve tika piešķirta, tā tiks piešķirta arī "
"bezsaistē, un otrādi."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1405 sssd-ldap.5.xml:1461
msgid "Default: Empty"
msgstr "Noklusējums: Empty"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1411
msgid "ldap_account_expire_policy (string)"
msgstr "ldap_account_expire_policy (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1414
msgid ""
"With this option a client side evaluation of access control attributes can "
"be enabled."
msgstr ""
"Ar šo opciju var iespējot piekļuves vadības atribūtu izvērtēšanu klienta "
"pusē."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1418
msgid ""
"Please note that it is always recommended to use server side access control, "
"i.e. the LDAP server should deny the bind request with a suitable error code "
"even if the password is correct."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka vienmēr ieteicams izmantot servera puses piekļuves "
"vadību, t. i., LDAP serverim jānoraida piesaistes pieprasījums ar piemērotu "
"kļūdas kodu pat tad, ja parole ir pareiza."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1425
msgid "The following values are allowed:"
msgstr "Atļautas šādas vērtības:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1428
msgid ""
"<emphasis>shadow</emphasis>: use the value of ldap_user_shadow_expire to "
"determine if the account is expired."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>shadow</emphasis>: izmantot ldap_user_shadow_expire vērtību, lai "
"noteiktu, vai kontam beidzies derīgums."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1433
msgid ""
"<emphasis>ad</emphasis>: use the value of the 32bit field "
"ldap_user_ad_user_account_control and allow access if the second bit is not "
"set. If the attribute is missing access is granted. Also the expiration time "
"of the account is checked."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>ad</emphasis>: izmantot 32 bitu lauka "
"ldap_user_ad_user_account_control vērtību un atļaut piekļuvi, ja otrais bits "
"nav iestatīts. Ja atribūta nav, piekļuve tiek piešķirta. Tiek pārbaudīts arī "
"konta derīguma beigu laiks."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1440
msgid ""
"<emphasis>rhds</emphasis>, <emphasis>ipa</emphasis>, <emphasis>389ds</"
"emphasis>: use the value of ldap_ns_account_lock to check if access is "
"allowed or not."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>rhds</emphasis>, <emphasis>ipa</emphasis>, <emphasis>389ds</"
"emphasis>: izmantot ldap_ns_account_lock vērtību, lai pārbaudītu, vai "
"piekļuve ir atļauta."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1446
msgid ""
"<emphasis>nds</emphasis>: the values of "
"ldap_user_nds_login_allowed_time_map, ldap_user_nds_login_disabled and "
"ldap_user_nds_login_expiration_time are used to check if access is allowed. "
"If both attributes are missing access is granted."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>nds</emphasis>: lai pārbaudītu, vai piekļuve ir atļauta, tiek "
"izmantotas ldap_user_nds_login_allowed_time_map, "
"ldap_user_nds_login_disabled un ldap_user_nds_login_expiration_time "
"vērtības. Ja abu atribūtu nav, piekļuve tiek piešķirta."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1454
msgid ""
"Please note that the ldap_access_order configuration option <emphasis>must</"
"emphasis> include <quote>expire</quote> in order for the "
"ldap_account_expire_policy option to work."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka konfigurācijas opcijai ldap_access_order <emphasis>"
"jāietver</emphasis> <quote>expire</quote>, lai opcija "
"ldap_account_expire_policy darbotos."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1467
msgid "ldap_access_order (string)"
msgstr "ldap_access_order (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1470 sssd-ipa.5.xml:400
msgid "Comma separated list of access control options.  Allowed values are:"
msgstr ""
"Ar komatiem atdalīts piekļuves vadības opciju saraksts.  Atļautās vērtības:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1474
msgid "<emphasis>filter</emphasis>: use ldap_access_filter"
msgstr "<emphasis>filter</emphasis>: izmantot ldap_access_filter"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1477
msgid ""
"<emphasis>lockout</emphasis>: use account locking.  If set, this option "
"denies access in case that ldap attribute 'pwdAccountLockedTime' is present "
"and has value of '000001010000Z'. Please see the option ldap_pwdlockout_dn.  "
"Please note that 'access_provider = ldap' must be set for this feature to "
"work."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>lockout</emphasis>: izmantot kontu bloķēšanu.  Ja iestatīts, šī "
"opcija liedz piekļuvi gadījumā, ja ldap atribūts „pwdAccountLockedTime” ir "
"klāt un tā vērtība ir „000001010000Z”. Lūdzu, skatiet opciju "
"ldap_pwdlockout_dn.  Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka, lai šis līdzeklis darbotos, "
"jābūt iestatītam „access_provider = ldap”."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1487
msgid ""
"<emphasis> Please note that this option is superseded by the <quote>ppolicy</"
"quote> option and might be removed in a future release.  </emphasis>"
msgstr ""
"<emphasis> Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka šo opciju aizstāj opcija <quote>ppolicy</"
"quote>, un nākamajā laidienā tā var tikt noņemta.  </emphasis>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1494
msgid ""
"<emphasis>ppolicy</emphasis>: use account locking.  If set, this option "
"denies access in case that ldap attribute 'pwdAccountLockedTime' is present "
"and has value of '000001010000Z' or represents any time in the past.  The "
"value of the 'pwdAccountLockedTime' attribute must end with 'Z', which "
"denotes the UTC time zone.  Other time zones are not currently supported and "
"will result in \"access-denied\" when users attempt to log in.  Please see "
"the option ldap_pwdlockout_dn.  Please note that 'access_provider = ldap' "
"must be set for this feature to work."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>ppolicy</emphasis>: izmantot kontu bloķēšanu.  Ja iestatīts, šī "
"opcija liedz piekļuvi gadījumā, ja ldap atribūts „pwdAccountLockedTime” ir "
"klāt un tā vērtība ir „000001010000Z” vai attēlo jebkuru laiku pagātnē.  "
"Atribūta „pwdAccountLockedTime” vērtībai jābeidzas ar „Z”, kas apzīmē UTC "
"laika joslu.  Citas laika joslas pašlaik netiek atbalstītas, un, lietotājiem "
"mēģinot pieteikties, tās izraisīs \"access-denied\".  Lūdzu, skatiet opciju "
"ldap_pwdlockout_dn.  Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka, lai šis līdzeklis darbotos, "
"jābūt iestatītam „access_provider = ldap”."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1511
msgid "<emphasis>expire</emphasis>: use ldap_account_expire_policy"
msgstr "<emphasis>expire</emphasis>: izmantot ldap_account_expire_policy"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1515 sssd-ipa.5.xml:408
msgid ""
"<emphasis>pwd_expire_policy_reject, pwd_expire_policy_warn, "
"pwd_expire_policy_renew: </emphasis> These options are useful if users are "
"interested in being warned that password is about to expire and "
"authentication is based on using a different method than passwords - for "
"example SSH keys."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>pwd_expire_policy_reject, pwd_expire_policy_warn, "
"pwd_expire_policy_renew: </emphasis> Šīs opcijas noder, ja lietotāji vēlas "
"saņemt brīdinājumu par tuvojošos paroles derīguma beigām un autentifikācija "
"balstās uz citu metodi, nevis parolēm, piemēram, SSH atslēgām."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1525 sssd-ipa.5.xml:418
msgid ""
"The difference between these options is the action taken if user password is "
"expired:"
msgstr ""
"Atšķirība starp šīm opcijām ir darbība, kas tiek veikta, ja lietotāja "
"parolei beidzies derīgums:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1530 sssd-ipa.5.xml:423
msgid "pwd_expire_policy_reject - user is denied to log in,"
msgstr "pwd_expire_policy_reject — lietotājam tiek liegta pieteikšanās,"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1536 sssd-ipa.5.xml:429
msgid "pwd_expire_policy_warn - user is still able to log in,"
msgstr "pwd_expire_policy_warn — lietotājs joprojām var pieteikties,"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1542 sssd-ipa.5.xml:435
msgid ""
"pwd_expire_policy_renew - user is prompted to change their password "
"immediately."
msgstr ""
"pwd_expire_policy_renew — lietotājam nekavējoties tiek lūgts mainīt paroli."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1550
msgid ""
"Please note that 'access_provider = ldap' must be set for this feature to "
"work. Also 'ldap_pwd_policy' must be set to shadow or mit_kerberos, these "
"options do not work with server-side password policies."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka, lai šis līdzeklis darbotos, jābūt iestatītam „"
"access_provider = ldap”. Arī „ldap_pwd_policy” jābūt iestatītam uz shadow "
"vai mit_kerberos; šīs opcijas nedarbojas ar servera puses paroļu politikām."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1556
msgid ""
"<emphasis>authorized_service</emphasis>: use the authorizedService attribute "
"to determine access"
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>authorized_service</emphasis>: izmantot atribūtu "
"authorizedService, lai noteiktu piekļuvi"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1561
msgid "<emphasis>host</emphasis>: use the host attribute to determine access"
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>host</emphasis>: izmantot atribūtu host, lai noteiktu piekļuvi"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1565
msgid ""
"<emphasis>rhost</emphasis>: use the rhost attribute to determine whether "
"remote host can access"
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>rhost</emphasis>: izmantot atribūtu rhost, lai noteiktu, vai "
"attālais resursdators var piekļūt"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1569
msgid ""
"Please note, rhost field in pam is set by application, it is better to check "
"what the application sends to pam, before enabling this access control option"
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka pam lauku rhost iestata lietotne; pirms šīs piekļuves "
"vadības opcijas iespējošanas labāk pārbaudīt, ko lietotne sūta uz pam"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1574
msgid "Default: filter"
msgstr "Noklusējums: filter"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1577
msgid ""
"Please note that it is a configuration error if a value is used more than "
"once."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka vērtības izmantošana vairāk nekā vienu reizi ir "
"konfigurācijas kļūda."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1584
msgid "ldap_pwdlockout_dn (string)"
msgstr "ldap_pwdlockout_dn (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1587
msgid ""
"This option specifies the DN of password policy entry on LDAP server. Please "
"note that absence of this option in sssd.conf in case of enabled account "
"lockout checking will yield access denied as ppolicy attributes on LDAP "
"server cannot be checked properly."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija norāda paroļu politikas ieraksta DN LDAP serverī. Lūdzu, ņemiet "
"vērā, ka šīs opcijas trūkums sssd.conf ar iespējotu kontu bloķēšanas "
"pārbaudi izraisīs piekļuves liegumu, jo ppolicy atribūtus LDAP serverī nevar "
"pareizi pārbaudīt."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1595
msgid "Example: cn=ppolicy,ou=policies,dc=example,dc=com"
msgstr "Piemērs: cn=ppolicy,ou=policies,dc=example,dc=com"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1598
msgid "Default: cn=ppolicy,ou=policies,$ldap_search_base"
msgstr "Noklusējums: cn=ppolicy,ou=policies,$ldap_search_base"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1604
msgid "ldap_deref (string)"
msgstr "ldap_deref (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1607
msgid ""
"Specifies how alias dereferencing is done when performing a search. The "
"following options are allowed:"
msgstr ""
"Norāda, kā meklēšanas laikā tiek veikta aizstājvārdu atsauces atrisināšana. "
"Atļautas šādas opcijas:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1612
msgid "<emphasis>never</emphasis>: Aliases are never dereferenced."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>never</emphasis>: aizstājvārdu atsauces nekad netiek atrisinātas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1616
msgid ""
"<emphasis>searching</emphasis>: Aliases are dereferenced in subordinates of "
"the base object, but not in locating the base object of the search."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>searching</emphasis>: aizstājvārdu atsauces tiek atrisinātas bāzes "
"objekta pakārtotajos objektos, bet ne, atrodot meklēšanas bāzes objektu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1621
msgid ""
"<emphasis>finding</emphasis>: Aliases are only dereferenced when locating "
"the base object of the search."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>finding</emphasis>: aizstājvārdu atsauces tiek atrisinātas tikai, "
"atrodot meklēšanas bāzes objektu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1626
msgid ""
"<emphasis>always</emphasis>: Aliases are dereferenced both in searching and "
"in locating the base object of the search."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>always</emphasis>: aizstājvārdu atsauces tiek atrisinātas gan "
"meklēšanā, gan atrodot meklēšanas bāzes objektu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1631
msgid ""
"Default: Empty (this is handled as <emphasis>never</emphasis> by the LDAP "
"client libraries)"
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums: tukšs (LDAP klienta bibliotēkas to apstrādā kā <emphasis>never</"
"emphasis>)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1639
msgid "ldap_rfc2307_fallback_to_local_users (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_rfc2307_fallback_to_local_users (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1642
msgid ""
"Allows to retain local users as members of an LDAP group for servers that "
"use the RFC2307 schema."
msgstr ""
"Ļauj serveriem, kas izmanto RFC2307 shēmu, paturēt lokālos lietotājus kā "
"LDAP grupas dalībniekus."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1646
msgid ""
"In some environments where the RFC2307 schema is used, local users are made "
"members of LDAP groups by adding their names to the memberUid attribute.  "
"The self-consistency of the domain is compromised when this is done, so SSSD "
"would normally remove the \"missing\" users from the cached group "
"memberships as soon as nsswitch tries to fetch information about the user "
"via getpw*() or initgroups() calls."
msgstr ""
"Dažās vidēs, kur tiek izmantota RFC2307 shēma, lokālie lietotāji tiek "
"padarīti par LDAP grupu dalībniekiem, pievienojot to vārdus atribūtam "
"memberUid.  Tas apdraud domēna iekšējo konsekvenci, tāpēc SSSD parasti "
"noņemtu \"trūkstošos\" lietotājus no kešotajām grupu dalībām, tiklīdz "
"nsswitch mēģina ienest informāciju par lietotāju ar izsaukumiem getpw*() vai "
"initgroups()."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1657
msgid ""
"This option falls back to checking if local users are referenced, and caches "
"them so that later initgroups() calls will augment the local users with the "
"additional LDAP groups."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija atkāpjas uz pārbaudi, vai uz lokālajiem lietotājiem ir atsauces, "
"un kešo tos, lai vēlākie initgroups() izsaukumi papildinātu lokālos "
"lietotājus ar papildu LDAP grupām."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1669 sssd-ifp.5.xml:158
msgid "wildcard_limit (integer)"
msgstr "wildcard_limit (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1672
msgid ""
"Specifies an upper limit on the number of entries that are downloaded during "
"a wildcard lookup."
msgstr ""
"Norāda augšējo robežu ierakstu skaitam, kas tiek lejupielādēti uzmeklēšanā "
"ar aizstājējzīmēm."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1676
msgid "At the moment, only the InfoPipe responder supports wildcard lookups."
msgstr ""
"Pašlaik uzmeklēšanu ar aizstājējzīmēm atbalsta tikai InfoPipe atbildētājs."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1680
msgid "Default: 1000 (often the size of one page)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 1000 (bieži vienas lappuses izmērs)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1686
msgid "ldap_library_debug_level (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_library_debug_level (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1689
msgid ""
"Switches on libldap debugging with the given level.  The libldap debug "
"messages will be written independent of the general debug_level."
msgstr ""
"Ieslēdz libldap atkļūdošanu ar norādīto līmeni.  libldap atkļūdošanas "
"ziņojumi tiks rakstīti neatkarīgi no vispārējā debug_level."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1694
msgid ""
"OpenLDAP uses a bitmap to enable debugging for specific components, -1 will "
"enable full debug output."
msgstr ""
"OpenLDAP izmanto bitkarti, lai iespējotu atkļūdošanu konkrētām komponentēm; -"
"1 iespējos pilnu atkļūdošanas izvadi."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1699
msgid "Default: 0 (libldap debugging disabled)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 0 (libldap atkļūdošana atspējota)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1705
msgid "ldap_use_ppolicy (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_use_ppolicy (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1708
msgid ""
"Turns on requesting and relying on the server-side password policy controls. "
"Disabling this allows interacting with services which send back invalid "
"ppolicy extension."
msgstr ""
"Ieslēdz servera puses paroļu politikas vadīklu pieprasīšanu un paļaušanos uz "
"tām. To atspējojot, iespējama mijiedarbība ar pakalpojumiem, kas atpakaļ "
"sūta nederīgu ppolicy paplašinājumu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1720
msgid "ldap_ppolicy_pwd_change_threshold (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_ppolicy_pwd_change_threshold (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1723
msgid ""
"Forces a password change when server side password policy controls are "
"enabled and remaining grace logins returned by the server after the "
"authentication reach or go below the threshold.  Note that the minimum "
"useful value is 2, as changing the password consumes 2 additional grace "
"logins, one to verify the current password and a second one to perform the "
"password change."
msgstr ""
"Piespiež paroles maiņu, ja ir iespējotas servera puses paroļu politikas "
"vadīklas un pēc autentifikācijas servera atgrieztais atlikušo atvieglojuma "
"pieteikšanās reižu skaits sasniedz slieksni vai ir zem tā.  Ņemiet vērā, ka "
"minimālā lietderīgā vērtība ir 2, jo paroles maiņa patērē 2 papildu "
"atvieglojuma pieteikšanās reizes — vienu pašreizējās paroles pārbaudei un "
"otru paroles maiņas veikšanai."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:52
msgid ""
"All of the common configuration options that apply to SSSD domains also "
"apply to LDAP domains. Refer to the <quote>DOMAIN SECTIONS</quote> section "
"of the <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd.conf</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry> manual page for full details.  Note that SSSD "
"LDAP mapping attributes are described in the <citerefentry> "
"<refentrytitle>sssd-ldap-attributes</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</manvolnum> "
"</citerefentry> manual page.  <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Visas vispārīgās konfigurācijas opcijas, kas attiecas uz SSSD domēniem, "
"attiecas arī uz LDAP domēniem. Pilnu informāciju skatiet rokasgrāmatas lapas "
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd.conf</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry> sadaļā <quote>DOMĒNU SADAĻAS</quote>.  Ņemiet "
"vērā, ka SSSD LDAP kartēšanas atribūti aprakstīti rokasgrāmatas lapā "
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd-ldap-attributes</refentrytitle> "
"<manvolnum>5</manvolnum> </citerefentry>.  <placeholder "
"type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1743
msgid "SUDO OPTIONS"
msgstr "SUDO OPCIJAS"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1745
msgid ""
"The detailed instructions for configuration of sudo_provider are in the "
"manual page <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd-sudo</refentrytitle> "
"<manvolnum>5</manvolnum> </citerefentry>."
msgstr ""
"Detalizēti norādījumi par sudo_provider konfigurēšanu ir rokasgrāmatas lapā "
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd-sudo</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1756
msgid "ldap_sudo_full_refresh_interval (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_sudo_full_refresh_interval (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1759
msgid ""
"How many seconds SSSD will wait between executing a full refresh of sudo "
"rules (which downloads all rules that are stored on the server)."
msgstr ""
"Cik sekundes SSSD gaidīs starp sudo kārtulu pilnās atsvaidzināšanas izpildēm "
"(kas lejupielādē visas serverī glabātās kārtulas)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1764
msgid ""
"The value must be greater than <emphasis>ldap_sudo_smart_refresh_interval </"
"emphasis>"
msgstr ""
"Vērtībai jābūt lielākai par <emphasis>ldap_sudo_smart_refresh_interval </"
"emphasis>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1769
msgid ""
"You can disable full refresh by setting this option to 0. However, either "
"smart or full refresh must be enabled."
msgstr ""
"Pilno atsvaidzināšanu var atspējot, iestatot šo opciju uz 0. Tomēr jābūt "
"iespējotai vai nu viedajai, vai pilnajai atsvaidzināšanai."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1774
msgid "Default: 21600 (6 hours)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 21600 (6 stundas)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1780
msgid "ldap_sudo_smart_refresh_interval (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_sudo_smart_refresh_interval (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1783
msgid ""
"How many seconds SSSD has to wait before executing a smart refresh of sudo "
"rules (which downloads all rules that have USN higher than the highest "
"server USN value that is currently known by SSSD)."
msgstr ""
"Cik sekundes SSSD jāgaida pirms sudo kārtulu viedās atsvaidzināšanas "
"izpildes (kas lejupielādē visas kārtulas, kuru USN ir lielāks par augstāko "
"SSSD pašlaik zināmo servera USN vērtību)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1789
msgid ""
"If USN attributes are not supported by the server, the modifyTimestamp "
"attribute is used instead."
msgstr ""
"Ja serveris neatbalsta USN atribūtus, tā vietā tiek izmantots atribūts "
"modifyTimestamp."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1793
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Note:</emphasis> the highest USN value can be updated by three "
"tasks: 1) By sudo full and smart refresh (if updated rules are found), 2) by "
"enumeration of users and groups (if enabled and updated users or groups are "
"found) and 3) by reconnecting to the server (by default every 15 minutes, "
"see <emphasis>ldap_connection_expire_timeout</emphasis>)."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>Piezīme:</emphasis> augstāko USN vērtību var atjaunināt trīs "
"uzdevumi: 1) sudo pilnā un viedā atsvaidzināšana (ja tiek atrastas "
"atjauninātas kārtulas), 2) lietotāju un grupu uzskaitīšana (ja iespējota un "
"tiek atrasti atjaunināti lietotāji vai grupas) un 3) atkārtota savienošanās "
"ar serveri (pēc noklusējuma ik pēc 15 minūtēm, skatiet <emphasis>"
"ldap_connection_expire_timeout</emphasis>)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1804
msgid ""
"You can disable smart refresh by setting this option to 0. However, either "
"smart or full refresh must be enabled."
msgstr ""
"Viedo atsvaidzināšanu var atspējot, iestatot šo opciju uz 0. Tomēr jābūt "
"iespējotai vai nu viedajai, vai pilnajai atsvaidzināšanai."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1815
msgid "ldap_sudo_random_offset (integer)"
msgstr "ldap_sudo_random_offset (vesels skaitlis)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1818
msgid ""
"Random offset between 0 and configured value is added to smart and full "
"refresh periods each time the periodic task is scheduled. The value is in "
"seconds."
msgstr ""
"Katru reizi, kad tiek ieplānots periodiskais uzdevums, viedās un pilnās "
"atsvaidzināšanas periodiem tiek pieskaitīta nejauša nobīde starp 0 un "
"konfigurēto vērtību. Vērtība ir sekundēs."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1824
msgid ""
"Note that this random offset is also applied on the first SSSD start which "
"delays the first sudo rules refresh. This prolongs the time when the sudo "
"rules are not available for use."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka šī nejaušā nobīde tiek piemērota arī pirmajā SSSD palaišanā, "
"kas aizkavē pirmo sudo kārtulu atsvaidzināšanu. Tādējādi pagarinās laiks, "
"kad sudo kārtulas nav pieejamas lietošanai."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1830
msgid "You can disable this offset by setting the value to 0."
msgstr "Šo nobīdi var atspējot, iestatot vērtību uz 0."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1840
msgid "ldap_sudo_use_host_filter (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_sudo_use_host_filter (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1843
msgid ""
"If true, SSSD will download only rules that are applicable to this machine "
"(using the IPv4 or IPv6 host/network addresses and hostnames)."
msgstr ""
"Ja true, SSSD lejupielādēs tikai šim datoram piemērojamās kārtulas "
"(izmantojot IPv4 vai IPv6 resursdatora/tīkla adreses un resursdatoru "
"nosaukumus)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1854
msgid "ldap_sudo_hostnames (string)"
msgstr "ldap_sudo_hostnames (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1857
msgid ""
"Space separated list of hostnames or fully qualified domain names that "
"should be used to filter the rules."
msgstr ""
"Ar atstarpēm atdalīts resursdatoru nosaukumu vai pilnībā kvalificētu domēnu "
"nosaukumu saraksts, ko izmantot kārtulu filtrēšanai."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1862
msgid ""
"If this option is empty, SSSD will try to discover the hostname and the "
"fully qualified domain name automatically."
msgstr ""
"Ja šī opcija ir tukša, SSSD mēģinās resursdatora nosaukumu un pilnībā "
"kvalificēto domēna nosaukumu atklāt automātiski."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1867 sssd-ldap.5.xml:1890 sssd-ldap.5.xml:1908
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1926
msgid ""
"If <emphasis>ldap_sudo_use_host_filter</emphasis> is <emphasis>false</"
"emphasis> then this option has no effect."
msgstr ""
"Ja <emphasis>ldap_sudo_use_host_filter</emphasis> ir <emphasis>false</"
"emphasis>, šai opcijai nav ietekmes."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1872 sssd-ldap.5.xml:1895
msgid "Default: not specified"
msgstr "Noklusējums: nav norādīts"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1878
msgid "ldap_sudo_ip (string)"
msgstr "ldap_sudo_ip (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1881
msgid ""
"Space separated list of IPv4 or IPv6 host/network addresses that should be "
"used to filter the rules."
msgstr ""
"Ar atstarpēm atdalīts IPv4 vai IPv6 resursdatoru/tīklu adrešu saraksts, ko "
"izmantot kārtulu filtrēšanai."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1886
msgid ""
"If this option is empty, SSSD will try to discover the addresses "
"automatically."
msgstr "Ja šī opcija ir tukša, SSSD mēģinās adreses atklāt automātiski."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1901
msgid "ldap_sudo_include_netgroups (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_sudo_include_netgroups (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1904
msgid ""
"If true then SSSD will download every rule that contains a netgroup in "
"sudoHost attribute."
msgstr ""
"Ja true, SSSD lejupielādēs katru kārtulu, kuras atribūtā sudoHost ir tīkla "
"grupa."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1919
msgid "ldap_sudo_include_regexp (boolean)"
msgstr "ldap_sudo_include_regexp (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1922
msgid ""
"If true then SSSD will download every rule that contains a wildcard in "
"sudoHost attribute."
msgstr ""
"Ja true, SSSD lejupielādēs katru kārtulu, kuras atribūtā sudoHost ir "
"aizstājējzīme."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><note><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1932
msgid ""
"Using wildcard is an operation that is very costly to evaluate on the LDAP "
"server side!"
msgstr ""
"Aizstājējzīmes izmantošana ir darbība, kuras izvērtēšana LDAP servera pusē "
"ir ļoti dārga!"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1944
msgid ""
"This manual page only describes attribute name mapping.  For detailed "
"explanation of sudo related attribute semantics, see <citerefentry> "
"<refentrytitle>sudoers.ldap</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</manvolnum> </"
"citerefentry>"
msgstr ""
"Šī rokasgrāmatas lapa apraksta tikai atribūtu nosaukumu kartēšanu.  "
"Detalizētu ar sudo saistīto atribūtu semantikas skaidrojumu skatiet "
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sudoers.ldap</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><title>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1954
msgid "AUTOFS OPTIONS"
msgstr "AUTOFS OPCIJAS"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd-ldap.5.xml:1956
