msgid "principal name"
msgstr "principāla nosaukums"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:188
msgid "%r"
msgstr "%r"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:189
msgid "realm name"
msgstr "apgabala nosaukums"

#. type: Content of: <varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:192 include/override_homedir.xml:53
msgid "%h"
msgstr "%h"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:193 sssd-ifp.5.xml:128
msgid "home directory"
msgstr "mājas direktorija"

#. type: Content of: <varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:197 include/override_homedir.xml:19
msgid "%d"
msgstr "%d"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:198
msgid "value of krb5_ccachedir"
msgstr "krb5_ccachedir vērtība"

#. type: Content of: <varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:203 include/override_homedir.xml:31
msgid "%P"
msgstr "%P"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:204
msgid "the process ID of the SSSD client"
msgstr "SSSD klienta procesa ID"

#. type: Content of: <varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:209 include/override_homedir.xml:68
msgid "%%"
msgstr "%%"

#. type: Content of: <varlistentry><listitem><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:210 include/override_homedir.xml:69
msgid "a literal '%'"
msgstr "burtiska „%”"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:164
msgid ""
"Location of the user's credential cache. Three credential cache types are "
"currently supported: <quote>FILE</quote>, <quote>DIR</quote> and "
"<quote>KEYRING:persistent</quote>. The cache can be specified either as "
"<replaceable>TYPE:RESIDUAL</replaceable>, or as an absolute path, which "
"implies the <quote>FILE</quote> type. In the template, the following "
"sequences are substituted: <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/> If "
"the template ends with 'XXXXXX' mkstemp(3) is used to create a unique "
"filename in a safe way."
msgstr ""
"Lietotāja akreditācijas datu kešatmiņas atrašanās vieta. Pašlaik tiek "
"atbalstīti trīs akreditācijas datu kešatmiņas tipi: <quote>FILE</quote>, "
"<quote>DIR</quote> un <quote>KEYRING:persistent</quote>. Kešatmiņu var "
"norādīt vai nu kā <replaceable>TYPE:RESIDUAL</replaceable>, vai kā absolūto "
"ceļu, kas nozīmē tipu <quote>FILE</quote>. Veidnē tiek aizstātas šādas "
"secības: <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/> Ja veidne beidzas ar „"
"XXXXXX”, unikāla faila nosaukuma drošai izveidei tiek izmantots mkstemp(3)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:218
msgid ""
"When using KEYRING types, the only supported mechanism is "
"<quote>KEYRING:persistent:%U</quote>, which uses the Linux kernel keyring to "
"store credentials on a per-UID basis. This is also the recommended choice, "
"as it is the most secure and predictable method."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojot KEYRING tipus, vienīgais atbalstītais mehānisms ir <quote>"
"KEYRING:persistent:%U</quote>, kas akreditācijas datu glabāšanai katram UID "
"atsevišķi izmanto Linux kodola atslēgu saišķi. Tā ir arī ieteicamā izvēle, "
"jo tā ir drošākā un paredzamākā metode."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:226
msgid ""
"The default value for the credential cache name is sourced from the profile "
"stored in the system wide krb5.conf configuration file in the [libdefaults] "
"section. The option name is default_ccache_name.  See krb5.conf(5)'s "
"PARAMETER EXPANSION paragraph for additional information on the expansion "
"format defined by krb5.conf."
msgstr ""
"Akreditācijas datu kešatmiņas nosaukuma noklusējuma vērtība tiek ņemta no "
"profila, kas glabājas sistēmas mēroga konfigurācijas faila krb5.conf sadaļā "
"[libdefaults]. Opcijas nosaukums ir default_ccache_name.  Papildu "
"informāciju par krb5.conf definēto izvēršanas formātu skatiet krb5.conf(5) "
"rindkopā PARAMETER EXPANSION."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:235
msgid ""
"NOTE: Please be aware that libkrb5 ccache expansion template from "
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>krb5.conf</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry> uses different expansion sequences than SSSD."
msgstr ""
"PIEZĪME: Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka libkrb5 ccache izvēršanas veidne no "
"<citerefentry> <refentrytitle>krb5.conf</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</"
"manvolnum> </citerefentry> izmanto citas izvēršanas secības nekā SSSD."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:244
msgid "Default: (from libkrb5)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: (no libkrb5)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:250
msgid "krb5_keytab (string)"
msgstr "krb5_keytab (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:253
msgid ""
"The location of the keytab to use when validating credentials obtained from "
"KDCs."
msgstr ""
"Keytab atrašanās vieta, ko izmantot, validējot no KDC iegūtos akreditācijas "
"datus."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:263
msgid "krb5_store_password_if_offline (boolean)"
msgstr "krb5_store_password_if_offline (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:266
msgid ""
"Store the password of the user if the provider is offline and use it to "
"request a TGT when the provider comes online again."
msgstr ""
"Saglabāt lietotāja paroli, ja nodrošinātājs ir bezsaistē, un izmantot to TGT "
"pieprasīšanai, kad nodrošinātājs atkal ir tiešsaistē."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:271
msgid ""
"NOTE: this feature is only available on Linux.  Passwords stored in this way "
"are kept in plaintext in the kernel keyring and are potentially accessible "
"by the root user (with difficulty)."
msgstr ""
"PIEZĪME: šis līdzeklis ir pieejams tikai Linux.  Šādā veidā saglabātās "
"paroles glabājas kodola atslēgu saišķī atklātā tekstā, un lietotājs root tām "
"potenciāli var piekļūt (ar grūtībām)."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:284
msgid "krb5_use_fast (string)"
msgstr "krb5_use_fast (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:287
msgid ""
"Enables flexible authentication secure tunneling (FAST) for Kerberos pre-"
"authentication. The following options are supported:"
msgstr ""
"Iespējo elastīgo drošo autentifikācijas tunelēšanu (FAST) Kerberos "
"priekšautentifikācijai. Tiek atbalstītas šādas opcijas:"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:292
msgid ""
"<emphasis>never</emphasis> use FAST. This is equivalent to not setting this "
"option at all."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>never</emphasis> — neizmantot FAST. Tas ir līdzvērtīgi šīs opcijas "
"neiestatīšanai."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:296
msgid ""
"<emphasis>try</emphasis> to use FAST. If the server does not support FAST, "
"continue the authentication without it."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>try</emphasis> — mēģināt izmantot FAST. Ja serveris neatbalsta "
"FAST, turpināt autentifikāciju bez tā."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:301
msgid ""
"<emphasis>demand</emphasis> to use FAST. The authentication fails if the "
"server does not support FAST."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>demand</emphasis> — pieprasīt FAST. Ja serveris neatbalsta FAST, "
"autentifikācija neizdodas."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:306
msgid "Default: not set, i.e. FAST is not used."
msgstr "Noklusējums: nav iestatīts, t. i., FAST netiek izmantots."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:309
msgid "NOTE: a keytab or support for anonymous PKINIT is required to use FAST."
msgstr ""
"PIEZĪME: FAST izmantošanai nepieciešams keytab vai anonīmā PKINIT atbalsts."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:313
msgid ""
"NOTE: SSSD supports FAST only with MIT Kerberos version 1.8 and later. If "
"SSSD is used with an older version of MIT Kerberos, using this option is a "
"configuration error."
msgstr ""
"PIEZĪME: SSSD atbalsta FAST tikai ar MIT Kerberos versiju 1.8 un jaunāku. Ja "
"SSSD tiek izmantots ar vecāku MIT Kerberos versiju, šīs opcijas izmantošana "
"ir konfigurācijas kļūda."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:322
msgid "krb5_fast_principal (string)"
msgstr "krb5_fast_principal (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:325
msgid "Specifies the server principal to use for FAST."
msgstr "Norāda servera principālu, ko izmantot FAST."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:331
msgid "krb5_fast_use_anonymous_pkinit (boolean)"
msgstr "krb5_fast_use_anonymous_pkinit (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:334
msgid ""
"If set to true try to use anonymous PKINIT instead of a keytab to get the "
"required credential for FAST. The krb5_fast_principal options is ignored in "
"this case."
msgstr ""
"Ja iestatīts uz true, mēģināt FAST vajadzīgo akreditācijas datu iegūšanai "
"keytab vietā izmantot anonīmo PKINIT. Šajā gadījumā opcija "
"krb5_fast_principal tiek ignorēta."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:374
msgid "krb5_kdcinfo_lookahead (string)"
msgstr "krb5_kdcinfo_lookahead (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:377
msgid ""
"When krb5_use_kdcinfo is set to true, you can limit the amount of servers "
"handed to <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd_krb5_locator_plugin</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>8</manvolnum> </citerefentry>.  This might be "
"helpful when there are too many servers discovered using SRV record."
msgstr ""
"Ja krb5_use_kdcinfo ir iestatīts uz true, var ierobežot serveru skaitu, kas "
"tiek nodoti <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd_krb5_locator_plugin</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>8</manvolnum> </citerefentry>.  Tas var noderēt, "
"ja ar SRV ierakstu tiek atklāts pārāk daudz serveru."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:387
msgid ""
"The krb5_kdcinfo_lookahead option contains two numbers separated by a colon. "
"The first number represents number of primary servers used and the second "
"number specifies the number of backup servers."
msgstr ""
"Opcija krb5_kdcinfo_lookahead satur divus skaitļus, atdalītus ar kolu. "
"Pirmais skaitlis norāda izmantoto primāro serveru skaitu, bet otrais — "
"rezerves serveru skaitu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:393
msgid ""
"For example <emphasis>10:0</emphasis> means that up to 10 primary servers "
"will be handed to <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd_krb5_locator_plugin</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>8</manvolnum> </citerefentry> but no backup "
"servers."
msgstr ""
"Piemēram, <emphasis>10:0</emphasis> nozīmē, ka <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>"
"sssd_krb5_locator_plugin</refentrytitle> <manvolnum>8</manvolnum> </"
"citerefentry> tiks nodoti līdz 10 primārajiem serveriem, bet neviens "
"rezerves serveris."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:402
msgid "Default: 3:1"
msgstr "Noklusējums: 3:1"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:408
msgid "krb5_use_enterprise_principal (boolean)"
msgstr "krb5_use_enterprise_principal (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:411
msgid ""
"Specifies if the user principal should be treated as enterprise principal. "
"See section 5 of RFC 6806 for more details about enterprise principals."
msgstr ""
"Norāda, vai lietotāja principāls jāuzskata par uzņēmuma principālu. Sīkāk "
"par uzņēmuma principāliem skatiet RFC 6806 5. sadaļu."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:417
msgid "Default: false (AD provider: true)"
msgstr "Noklusējums: false (AD nodrošinātājam: true)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:420
msgid ""
"The IPA provider will set to option to 'true' if it detects that the server "
"is capable of handling enterprise principals and the option is not set "
"explicitly in the config file."
msgstr ""
"IPA nodrošinātājs iestatīs šo opciju uz „true”, ja konstatēs, ka serveris "
"spēj apstrādāt uzņēmuma principālus un opcija konfigurācijas failā nav "
"iestatīta skaidri."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:429
msgid "krb5_use_subdomain_realm (boolean)"
msgstr "krb5_use_subdomain_realm (Būla vērtība)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:432
msgid ""
"Specifies to use subdomains realms for the authentication of users from "
"trusted domains. This option can be set to 'true' if enterprise principals "
"are used with upnSuffixes which are not known on the parent domain KDCs. If "
"the option is set to 'true' SSSD will try to send the request directly to a "
"KDC of the trusted domain the user is coming from."
msgstr ""
"Norāda, ka uzticamo domēnu lietotāju autentifikācijai jāizmanto apakšdomēnu "
"apgabali. Šo opciju var iestatīt uz „true”, ja tiek izmantoti uzņēmuma "
"principāli ar upnSuffixes, kas vecākdomēna KDC nav zināmi. Ja opcija ir "
"iestatīta uz „true”, SSSD mēģinās nosūtīt pieprasījumu tieši uz tā uzticamā "
"domēna KDC, no kura nāk lietotājs."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:448
msgid "krb5_map_user (string)"
msgstr "krb5_map_user (virkne)"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:451
msgid ""
"The list of mappings is given as a comma-separated list of pairs "
"<quote>username:primary</quote> where <quote>username</quote> is a UNIX user "
"name and <quote>primary</quote> is a user part of a kerberos principal. This "
"mapping is used when user is authenticating using <quote>auth_provider = "
"krb5</quote>."
msgstr ""
"Kartējumu saraksts tiek dots kā ar komatiem atdalīts pāru saraksts <quote>"
"username:primary</quote>, kur <quote>username</quote> ir UNIX lietotājvārds "
"un <quote>primary</quote> ir kerberos principāla lietotāja daļa. Šo "
"kartēšanu izmanto, kad lietotājs autentificējas, izmantojot <quote>"
"auth_provider = krb5</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para><programlisting>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:463
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"krb5_realm = REALM\n"
"krb5_map_user = joe:juser,dick:richard\n"
msgstr ""
"krb5_realm = REALM\n"
"krb5_map_user = joe:juser,dick:richard\n"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:468
msgid ""
"<quote>joe</quote> and <quote>dick</quote> are UNIX user names and "
"<quote>juser</quote> and <quote>richard</quote> are primaries of kerberos "
"principals. For user <quote>joe</quote> resp.  <quote>dick</quote> SSSD will "
"try to kinit as <quote>juser@REALM</quote> resp.  <quote>richard@REALM</"
"quote>."
msgstr ""
"<quote>joe</quote> un <quote>dick</quote> ir UNIX lietotājvārdi, un <quote>"
"juser</quote> un <quote>richard</quote> ir kerberos principālu primārās "
"daļas. Lietotājam <quote>joe</quote> attiecīgi  <quote>dick</quote> SSSD "
"mēģinās izpildīt kinit kā <quote>juser@REALM</quote> attiecīgi  <quote>"
"richard@REALM</quote>."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:65
msgid ""
"If the auth-module krb5 is used in an SSSD domain, the following options "
"must be used. See the <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd.conf</"
"refentrytitle> <manvolnum>5</manvolnum> </citerefentry> manual page, section "
"<quote>DOMAIN SECTIONS</quote>, for details on the configuration of an SSSD "
"domain.  <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Ja SSSD domēnā tiek izmantots autentifikācijas modulis krb5, jāizmanto šādas "
"opcijas. Sīkāku informāciju par SSSD domēna konfigurēšanu skatiet "
"rokasgrāmatas lapas <citerefentry> <refentrytitle>sssd.conf</refentrytitle> "
"<manvolnum>5</manvolnum> </citerefentry> sadaļā <quote>DOMĒNU SADAĻAS</quote>"
".  <placeholder type=\"variablelist\" id=\"0\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:495
msgid ""
"The following example assumes that SSSD is correctly configured and FOO is "
"one of the domains in the <replaceable>[sssd]</replaceable> section. This "
"example shows only configuration of Kerberos authentication; it does not "
"include any identity provider."
msgstr ""
"Tālāk dotajā piemērā pieņemts, ka SSSD ir pareizi konfigurēts un FOO ir "
"viens no domēniem sadaļā <replaceable>[sssd]</replaceable>. Šis piemērs "
"parāda tikai Kerberos autentifikācijas konfigurāciju; tas neietver nevienu "
"identitātes nodrošinātāju."

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para><programlisting>
#: sssd-krb5.5.xml:503
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[domain/FOO]\n"
"auth_provider = krb5\n"
"krb5_server = 192.168.1.1\n"
"krb5_realm = EXAMPLE.COM\n"
msgstr ""
"[domain/FOO]\n"
"auth_provider = krb5\n"
"krb5_server = 192.168.1.1\n"
"krb5_realm = EXAMPLE.COM\n"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refnamediv><refname>
#: sss_cache.8.xml:10 sss_cache.8.xml:15
msgid "sss_cache"
msgstr "sss_cache"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refnamediv><refpurpose>
#: sss_cache.8.xml:16
msgid "perform cache cleanup"
msgstr "veikt kešatmiņas tīrīšanu"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsynopsisdiv><cmdsynopsis>
#: sss_cache.8.xml:21
msgid ""
"<command>sss_cache</command> <arg choice='opt'> <replaceable>options</"
"replaceable> </arg>"
msgstr ""
"<command>sss_cache</command> <arg choice='opt'> <replaceable>options</"
"replaceable> </arg>"

#. type: Content of: <reference><refentry><refsect1><para>
#: sss_cache.8.xml:31
msgid ""
"<command>sss_cache</command> invalidates records in SSSD cache.  Invalidated "
"records are forced to be reloaded from server as soon as related SSSD "
"backend is online. Options that invalidate a single object only accept a "
"single provided argument."
msgstr ""
"<command>sss_cache</command> padara SSSD kešatmiņas ierakstus nederīgus.  "
"Nederīgie ieraksti tiek piespiedu kārtā atkārtoti ielādēti no servera, "
"tiklīdz attiecīgā SSSD aizmugursistēma ir tiešsaistē. Opcijas, kas padara "
"nederīgu vienu objektu, pieņem tikai vienu norādītu argumentu."

